COLLDATA("sh9771","en",[[4,"ﷺ with this, something similar to it."],[9,"ﷺ , something similar to it. Shaykh Abu al-Hasan said: I saw it in a book from Abu Ja'far al-Tirmidhi, from al-Husayn b. Ali b. al-Aswad, from Abu Usama, from al-Walid b. Kathir, from Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far, with this chain."],[10,"From Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far, with this, the like of it."],[11,"Ya'qub b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and those we mentioned with him at the beginning of the book said: from Abu Usama, from al-Walid b. Kathir, from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr. When there was disagreement about Abu Usama regarding its chain, we wanted to know who gave the correct version. We looked into that and found that Shu'ayb b. Ayyub narrated it from Abu Usama, from al-Walid b. Kathir, in both ways together, from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr, then he followed it with Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far. Thus both statements from Abu Usama are correct, and it is correct that al-Walid b. Kathir narrated it from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr and from Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far, both from Abdullah b. Abdullah b. Umar, from his father. Sometimes Abu Usama narrated it from al-Walid b. Kathir, from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr, and sometimes from al-Walid b. Kathir, from Muhammad b. Abbad b. Ja'far, and Allah knows best. As for the hadith of Shu'ayb b. Ayyub, from Abu Usama, from al-Walid b. Kathir, from both men together."],[13,"ﷺ , the like of it. As for the hadith of Muhammad b. al-Fudayl al-Balkhi."],[14,"ﷺ , the like of it."],[18,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, with this chain, something similar to it."],[19,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, something similar to it."],[21,"ﷺ . In this narration there is strength for the narration of Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr, from Ubayd Allah b. Abdullah b. Umar, from his father. Hammad b. Salama narrated it from Asim b. al-Mundhir, but Hammad b. Zayd differed from him, narrating it from Asim b. al-Mundhir, from Abu Bakr b. Ubayd Allah b. Abdullah b. Umar, from his father, as a mawquf report, not marfu'. Likewise Ismail b. Ulayya narrated it from Asim b. al-Mundhir, from an unnamed man, from Ibn Umar, also as a mawquf report."],[23,"From Hammad b. Salama, with this chain. They said in it: \"When water reaches two qullahs or three.\""],[24,"From Hammad b. Salama, with this chain. They said in it: \"When water is two qullahs, it does not become impure,\" and they did not say \"or three.\""],[26,"From Asim b. al-Mundhir, with this chain, like the statement of Affan: \"When water is two qullahs, it does not become impure.\""],[27,"If the water amounts to two qullahs, it does not become impure."],[30,"The same as that, from Ibn Umar, in mawquf form."],[31,"He said: “The qilal are the large storage jars.”"],[35,"Upon him be peace, something similar."],[36,"The people of knowledge write down what is for them and what is against them, while the people of whims do not write down except what is for them."],[37,"He says: Writing down hadith is better than its place."],[39,"He said: “If the water reaches forty qullahs, it does not become impure.”"],[40,"He said: “If the water is forty qullahs, nothing makes it impure.”"],[41,"The same as that, exactly, from Abdullah b. Amr."],[42,"If the water is forty qullahs, nothing makes it impure."],[43,"If the water reaches forty qullahs, it does not become impure, or a word similar to that."],[50,"Water: nothing makes it impure except what changes its smell or its taste."],[51,"Indeed, all water is pure; nothing makes it impure."],[52,"We asked him about ponds and cisterns in which dogs lap. He said: Water was sent down pure; nothing makes it impure."],[53,"Allah, Exalted is He, sent down water pure, so nothing makes it impure."],[54,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, we perform ablution from the well of Buda'ah, while menstrual cloths, filth—and Yusuf said: carcasses—and they said: and the flesh of dogs are thrown into it. He said: Indeed, water is pure; nothing makes it impure. The hadith is according to the wording of Ibn Abi 'Awn, and Yusuf said from 'Abdullah b. 'Abdullah."],[58,"upon him ﷺ the like of it."],[67,"He used to say: Every living creature has flowing blood, so one does not perform ablution because of it. But concession was granted regarding the beetle, scorpion, locust, and cricket when they fall into a well, there is no harm in it. Shu'bah said: I think he also mentioned the gecko. Chapter on sea water."],[76,"upon him ﷺ the like of it."],[85,"'Umar b. al-Khattab used to have water heated for him in a qumqumah and would bathe with it. This is a sound chain."],[88,"He said: Do not bathe with sun-heated water, for it causes leprosy. Chapter on water in which bread is moistened."],[89,"that one performs ablution with water in which bread is moistened. Chapter on the interpretation of 'when you rise for prayer'."],[90,"He said: meaning when you rise from sleep."],[91,"From Zayd b. Aslam regarding His saying, Exalted is He: 'O you who believe, when you rise for prayer' (al-Ma'idah 6). He said: when you rise from sleep. Chapter on ablution with the leftover water of the siwak."],[92,"that he used to command his family to perform ablution with the water left over from the siwak."],[93,"He said: Jarir used to say to his family, 'Perform ablution with this [water] into which he put his siwak.' This is a sound chain of transmission."],[94,"upon him be peace, used to use the siwak with the water left over from his ablution."],[98,"upon him be peace, passed by a dead sheep and said, 'Why did you not make use of its hide?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.' He said, 'Only its eating is forbidden.' Aqil added: 'Is there not in water and tanning what purifies it?' Ibn Hani' said: 'Is there not in water and qaraz (acacia pods) what purifies it?'"],[101,"upon him be peace, passed by a domestic sheep belonging to some of his family that had died and said, 'Why did you not make use of its skin?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.' He said, 'Its tanning is its purification.' Ibn Sa'id said: 'Its tanning is its purification.'"],[102,"upon him be peace, with this, and he said, 'Only its meat is forbidden, and the tanning of its hide is its purification.'"],[103,"and he said, 'Only its meat is forbidden to you, and you are permitted its skin.' These are sound chains of transmission."],[105,"upon him be peace, 'Why did you not make use of its hide? Why did you not tan it? For that is a purification for it.'"],[107,"upon him be peace, 'Its tanning is its purification.' Ibn Kamil narrated it to us, Ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us from him."],[110,"He said: 'The tanning of the hide is its purification.'"],[111,"upon him be peace, with this. He said: 'Its tanning is its purification.'"],[112,"and he said: 'Its tanning is its purification.'"],[115,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: “Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who would eat it” (Q 6:145). He said: “The eater is the one who consumes. As for the tooth, horn, bone, wool, hair, fur, and sinew, there is no harm in them, because they are washed.” Shababah said: “Only what is eaten from the carcass is forbidden, which is the meat. As for the skin, tooth, bone, hair, and wool, they are lawful.” Abu Bakr al-Hudhali is weak."],[117,"Abd al-Baqi b. Qani narrated to us, Ismail b. al-Fadl narrated to us, Sulayman b. Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Yusuf b. al-Safar narrated to us with this chain the like of it, exactly."],[121,"Upon him ﷺ: “Any hide that is tanned has become pure.” A good chain."],[126,"Upon him ﷺ: “Make use of the skins of dead animals once they are tanned, whether with earth, ashes, salt, or whatever else, as long as you intend to treat them properly.”"],[139,"Upon him ﷺ: He performed ghusl with the leftover water of Maymunah. A sound chain."],[140,"Upon him ﷺ: He used to perform ghusl with the leftover water of Maymunah. A sound chain."],[141,"Upon him ﷺ: He performed wudu with the leftover water from her ghusl following janabah. Al-Ramadi said: He performed wudu from the leftover water of her wudu following janabah."],[142,"Upon him ﷺ: He forbade performing wudu with the leftover water of a woman’s wudu, or he said: her drink."],[146,"Ya’qub b. Ibrahim al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Humayd b. al-Rabi narrated to us, Waki and Abu Mu’awiyah and Abd Allah b. Numayr narrated to us, they said: Al-A’mash narrated to us with a chain like it."],[147,"And he said: “Let none of you clean himself with fewer than three stones.” A sound chain."],[152,"Upon him ﷺ: He forbade us to clean ourselves with bone, dung, or charcoal. Ali b. Rabah’s hearing from Ibn Mas’ud is not established and is not sound."],[155,"Upon him ﷺ: He was asked about istitabah, and he said: “Does not one of you find three stones? Two stones for the sides and one stone for the passage.” A good chain."],[159,"ﷺ with this, as a mursal report."],[160,"ﷺ with this."],[161,"Ali said: I said to Sufyan, \"Would Zam'ah raise it (to the Prophet)?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So I asked Salamah about it, and he did not recognize it—meaning he did not raise it. [End of chapter on the siwak.]"],[162,"In the siwak there are ten qualities: it pleases the Lord, Most High, and angers Satan; it gladdens the angels; it is good for the gums; it removes cavities; it sharpens the eyesight; it sweetens the breath; it reduces phlegm; it is from the Sunnah; and it increases good deeds."],[163,"I saw Ibn Umar make his camel kneel facing the qiblah, then he sat and urinated toward it. I said, \"Abu Abd al-Rahman, has this not been forbidden?\" He said, \"Yes, but that was forbidden only in open land. If there is something between you and the qiblah that screens you, there is no harm.\""],[178,"He said: It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we perform wudu with the leftover water of donkeys?\" He said, \"And with the leftover water of beasts of prey.\" Ibn Abi Habibah is also weak—he is Ibrahim b. Ismail b. Abi Habibah."],[179,"And al-Shafi'i narrated from Sa'id b. Salim, from Ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud b. al-Husayn, something similar."],[185,"From Abu Hurayrah, regarding a dog lapping from a vessel, he said: It is poured out and washed seven times. This is sahih, mawquf."],[190,"From Qatadah, with his chain, the like of it."],[191,"That he said: The first is with earth. This is sahih."],[192,"ﷺ : When a dog laps from a vessel, wash it seven times, the first of them with earth. This is sahih."],[195,"Regarding a dog lapping from a vessel: he washes it three, or five, or seven times."],[198,"He said: When a dog laps in a vessel, pour it out and then wash it three times. This is mawqūf, and no one reported it this way other than ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ, and Allah knows best."],[199,"That he, when a dog lapped in a vessel, would pour it out and wash it three times."],[201,"From Abū Hurayrah regarding the leftover water of a cat: it is poured out and the vessel is washed once or twice. Mawqūf."],[202,"He said: When a cat laps in a vessel, pour it out and wash it once."],[203,"Regarding a cat that laps in a vessel, he said: Wash it once and pour it out."],[204,"He said regarding a cat when it laps in a vessel: He washes it seven times. Layth b. Abī Sulaym is not a ḥāfiẓ, and this is mawqūf. It is not authentic from Abū Hurayrah; this is more likely from the statement of ʿAṭāʾ."],[205,"He says regarding a cat that laps in a vessel, he said: He washes it seven times."],[206,"He said: He washes it twice or three times."],[208,"Regarding a cat that laps in a vessel, he said: Wash it once or twice."],[209,"The vessel is washed from a cat just as it is washed from a dog."],[211,"Al-Maḥāmilī narrated to us, al-Ṣāʿānī narrated to us, Ibn ʿUfayr narrated to us with an isnād like it, mawqūfan."],[212,"When a cat laps in a vessel, it is washed seven times."],[213,"On the authority of Layth, with this, the like of it."],[214,"He used to regard the cat as like the dog: it is washed seven times. He said: And Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; he said: I said to 'Ata', 'The cat?' He said, 'It is in the status of the dog, or worse than it.'"],[215,"Regarding the vessel in which the cat laps, he said, 'Wash it seven times.'"],[222,"He said, 'It is among the beasts of prey, and there is no harm in it.' Chapter: Mentioning the Name of Allah over Wudu'."],[228,"They both said: Harun b. Ishaq narrated to us; Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[232,"On the authority of Ibn Harmala, with his chain, the like of it."],[238,"He said: 'Ikrima said, 'Nabidh is a means of purification for one who finds nothing else.'"],[239,"Nabidh is a means of purification when one finds nothing else."],[240,"Wudu' with nabidh when one does not find water."],[241,"He said, 'Nabidh is a means of purification for one who does not find water.'"],[242,"He was asked about a man who is unable to obtain water. He said, 'He performs wudu' with nabidh.'"],[243,"Abu Sahl narrated to us; Ibrahim al-Harbi narrated to us; Muhammad b. Sinan narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us; 'Abdullah b. Muharrir narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of 'Ikrima, on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas, who said, 'Nabidh is a means of purification for one who does not find water.' Ibn Muharrir is abandoned in hadith."],[248,"He said no."],[250,"Al-Qadi Abu Tahir Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Nasr narrated to us; Muhammad b. 'Abdus b. Kamil narrated to us; Muhammad b. 'Abbad narrated to us; Abu Sa'id, the client of Banu Hashim, narrated to us; Hammad b. Salama narrated to us with this chain something similar. 'Ali b. Zayd is weak, and Abu Rafi's hearing from Ibn Mas'ud is not established. This hadith is not in the compilations of Hammad b. Salama. 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Abi Rizma also narrated it, and he is not strong."],[255,"He said: I said to Abu al-'Aliyah, 'A man who has no water but has nabidh — may he perform ghusl with it for janabah?' He said, 'No.' Then I mentioned to him the Night of the Jinn, and he said, 'Would I give you this foul thing to drink? That was only raisins and water.'"],[256,"He said: He saw no harm in performing wudu' with nabidh. Hajjaj b. Artat reported it alone; his hadith is not used as proof."],[257,"From Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, from Mazidah b. Jabir, from 'Ali. (H) And Abu Sahl narrated to us; Ibrahim al-Harbi narrated to us; 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us; from Abu Layla al-Khurasani, from Mazidah b. Jabir, from 'Ali ﷺ , who said: There is no harm in performing wudu' with nabidh. Chapter on the encouragement to mention the name of Allah at the beginning of purification."],[261,"Muhammad b. al-Qasim narrated to us; Isma'il b. Musa al-Suddi narrated to us; Zafir b. Sulayman narrated to us; from Sallam Abu 'Abd Allah, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Mu'awiyah b. Qurrah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[262,"upon him be peace, with that."],[270,"And he wiped his head and his feet twice."],[271,"upon him be peace, washed his face three times and his hands twice twice."],[275,"When he performed wudu', he would move his ring."],[290,"upon him be peace, performed wudu' and wiped his head with the moisture of his hands."],[292,"A man came to 'Ali b. Abi Talib and asked him about wudu', saying, 'Should I begin with the right or the left?' 'Ali broke wind at him, then called for water and began with the left before the right."],[295,"He said: 'Ali ﷺ said: I do not care, once I have completed my ablution, with which of my limbs I began."],[296,"From 'Awf, similarly."],[297,"I do not care if I began with the left before the right when I performed ablution."],[298,"There is no harm in beginning with your feet before your hands."],[311,"Upon him be peace, he performed ablution twice, twice."],[312,"Upon him be peace, he performed ablution twice, twice."],[326,"The ears are part of the head. It is mawquf. Likewise Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated it from Nafi' and 'Abd Allah b. Nafi' from his father from Ibn 'Umar as mawquf."],[327,"Ibn 'Umar used to wipe his ears and say: They are part of the head."],[328,"The ears are part of the head. The shaykh said: As for the first hadith narrated by Yahya b. al-'Uryan from Hatim from Usama b. Zayd from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar as marfu', it is a mistake. The correct version is from Usama b. Zayd from Hilal b. Usama al-Fihri from Ibn 'Umar as mawquf."],[329,"The ears are part of the head."],[330,"The ears are part of the head."],[331,"The ears are part of the head. It is also narrated from Zayd al-'Ammi from Mujahid from Ibn 'Umar as marfu'."],[334,"upon him and peace, in mursal form. As for the hadith of al-Rabi' b. Badr"],[338,"upon him and peace, the like of it"],[340,"upon him and peace, the like of it"],[344,"upon him and peace, exactly the like of it, except that he said, 'and let him snuff water into the nostrils and expel it'"],[347,"The ears are part of the head in ablution and part of the face in ihram."],[351,"Muhammad b. Ziyad narrated to us the like of it."],[352,"From Ibn Abbas as his own statement (mawquf)."],[353,"The ears are part of the head. And it is narrated from Abu Hurayrah"],[355,"The ears are part of the head. Ibn Muharrar is abandoned (matruk)."],[358,"The ears are part of the head, as his own statement (mawquf). Ibrahim b. Musa al-Farra' and others followed him from Abd al-Rahim. And it is narrated from Abu Umamah al-Bahili"],[361,"The ears are part of the head, with doubt."],[364,"He said: It is nothing. In it is Shahr b. Hawshab, and Shahr is weak, and there is doubt about the hadith being raised. And Ibn Abi Hatim said: My father said: Sinan b. Rabi'ah Abu Rabi'ah has a confused (mudtarib) hadith."],[368,"And know that the ears are part of the head."],[374,"I saw Anas b. Malik perform wudu' and wipe his ears, their outside and inside, then he said: \"Ibn Mas'ud used to command us regarding the ears.\""],[376,"That Ibn Umar, when he performed wudu', did similar to the statement of Ibn Abi al-Ishrin, except that he did not raise it, and this is the correct view."],[377,"When he wiped his head, he lifted the qalansuwah and wiped the front of his head."],[380,"Da'laj b. Ahmad narrated to us; Musa b. Harun narrated to us; Yazid b. Abdullah b. Yazid b. Maymun b. Mihran Abu Muhammad narrated to us; Ikrimah b. Ammar narrated to us with this chain the like of it. This is a sound, authentic chain."],[402,"Four things do not become junub: the human being, water, earth, and cloth."],[409,"Ja'far b. Ahmad al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us; al-Sari b. Yahya narrated to us; Abu al-Sari, meaning Hannad b. al-Sari, narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us with his chain the like of it."],[412,"If it was due to janabah, he repeats the madmadah and istinshaq and starts the prayer over. Ibn Arafah said: \"If the madmadah and istinshaq are forgotten, if it was due to janabah, he leaves, performs madmadah and istinshaq, and repeats the prayer.\" The shaykh, the hafiz, said: \"A'ishah bt. Ajrad has only this hadith. A'ishah bt. Ajrad is not a sufficient proof.\""],[413,"He repeats in janabah, but does not repeat in wudu'."],[414,"He does not repeat except if he is junub."],[415,"Regarding a junub who forgot the madmadah and istinshaq. She said: \"Ibn Abbas said: 'He performs madmadah and istinshaq and repeats the prayer.'\""],[419,"A woman may perform wudu' and ghusl from the leftover of a man's ghusl water and his purification water, but a man may not perform wudu' from the leftover of a woman's ghusl water or her purification water."],[423,"And Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Salih al-Abhari narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ja'far b. Razin narrated to us: Ibrahim b. al-Ala narrated to us: Isma'il b. Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar and Musa b. Uqba, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[426,"We were with Ali in al-Rahbah. He went out to the farthest part of al-Rahbah. By Allah, I do not know whether he urinated or defecated. Then he came and called for a jug of water and washed his palms, then clasped them together, then recited a portion of the Qur'an. Then he said: Recite the Qur'an as long as none of you is in a state of janabah. If janabah befalls him, then no, not even a single letter. It is authentic from Ali."],[435,"The menstruating woman, the one in janabah, and the woman in post-natal bleeding do not recite the Qur'an."],[438,"Peace be upon him: None but the pure may touch the Qur'an."],[439,"Peace be upon him wrote a letter containing: Do not touch the Qur'an except while pure."],[442,"Umar went out girded with a sword. It was said to him: Your sister's husband and your sister have apostatized. Umar went to them, and with them was a man from the Muhajirun called Khabbab. They were reciting Ta-Ha. He said: Give me the book that you have so I may read it. Umar could read the book. His sister said to him: You are impure, and none but the purified may touch it. So rise and perform ghusl or wudu. Umar rose and performed wudu, then took the book and read Ta-Ha."],[443,"We were with Salman al-Farisi on a journey. He relieved himself, so we said to him: Perform wudu so that we may ask you about a verse of the Qur'an. He said: Ask me, for I do not touch it. Then he recited to us what we wanted, and there was no water between us and him."],[444,"We were with Salman. He went out and relieved himself, then came back. I said: O Abu Abd Allah, if you would perform wudu, perhaps we might ask you about verses. He said: I do not touch it; none touches it except the purified. Then he recited to us whatever he wished. All of them are trustworthy."],[445,"He said: We were with him on a journey. He went off and relieved himself, then came back. I said: O Abu Abd Allah, perform wudu so that perhaps we may ask you about verses of the Qur'an. He said: Ask me, for I do not touch it; none touches it except the purified. So we asked him, and he recited to us before performing wudu. The meaning is close. All of them are authentic."],[446,"From Salman, something similar. And this is like it."],[447,"That he recited after the hadath."],[449,"From Ibn Abbas concerning semen that gets on a garment. He said: It is only like phlegm and spittle. Remove it from you with a toothpick-like stalk of idhkhir."],[456,"When he wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform the ablution he performs for prayer before sleeping. And when he wanted to eat while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would wash his hands and rinse his mouth, then eat."],[464,"For an animal whose flesh is eaten, there is no harm in its dung."],[470,"From Qatādah."],[489,"That he used to say: A man's kissing his wife requires ablution."],[494,"Upon him be peace and blessings, with this."],[496,"Upon him be peace and blessings, he used to kiss and then pray without performing ablution. It is said that al-Walīd b. Ṣāliḥ erred in his saying 'from ʿAbd al-Karīm', when it is rather the ḥadīth of Ghālib. Al-Thawrī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Karīm from ʿAṭāʾ as his own statement, and that is the correct view. It is rather the ḥadīth of Ghālib, and Allah knows best."],[497,"There is no ablution required for kissing."],[501,"He said: Indeed, Sufyān al-Thawrī was the most knowledgeable of people about this. He claimed that Ḥabīb did not hear anything from ʿUrwah."],[502,"From ʿĀʾishah: She would pray even if blood dripped onto the mat, and regarding kissing, Yaḥyā said: Report from me that they are similar: nothing is required."],[504,"Upon him be peace and blessings, he used to kiss after performing ablution and then not repeat the ablution, or she said: he would pray."],[505,"He used to kiss after performing ablution and then pray."],[507,"Upon him be peace and blessings, he used to kiss her while he was fasting. Thus said ʿUthmān b. Abī Shaybah."],[509,"Upon him be peace, he used to kiss her and then pray without performing wudu. He said: And Ata did not consider kissing to require wudu."],[510,"Abu Bakr al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Muhammad b. Shadhan narrated to us, Mualla narrated to us something similar."],[511,"Upon him be peace, he used to kiss some of his wives and then not renew wudu. His saying 'Abd Allah b. Ghalib is an error; he only meant Ghalib b. Ubayd Allah, and he is abandoned. Abu Salama al-Juhani is Khalid b. Salama, weak, and he is not the one from whom Zakariyya b. Abi Za'ida narrates."],[512,"Kissing does not require wudu."],[514,"He did not consider kissing to require wudu."],[515,"Kissing does not require wudu."],[519,"Whoever kisses his wife while he is in wudu must repeat wudu."],[520,"He said: Kissing is a form of touching, so perform wudu from it. Sahih."],[521,"Regarding a man kissing his wife and touching her with his hand, it is a form of mulamasa. Whoever kisses his wife or touches her with his hand, wudu becomes obligatory upon him."],[522,"He considered kissing to be a form of touching and commanded wudu for it."],[523,"Kissing requires wudu. Sahih."],[524,"Kissing is a form of touching."],[525,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us: Abdullah b. Umar narrated to us with his chain of narration, something similar."],[526,"Kissing is a form of touching, and it requires wudu. Al-Mu'alla and Ibn Arafah added: And touching is whatever is less than sexual intercourse."],[527,"Kissing is a form of touching. Sahih."],[528,"Kissing is a form of touching. Sahih."],[529,"And Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal b. Yasaf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, something similar, or from Abu Ubaydah."],[535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his private part with his hand with no barrier or covering between them, let him perform the wudu he performs for prayer.”"],[541,"When he touches his groin, or his testicles, or his private part, he should not pray until he performs wudu."],[548,"He said: We gathered in the mosque of al-Khayf: I, Ahmad b. Hanbal, Ali b. al-Madini, and Yahya b. Ma'in. They debated about touching the penis. Yahya said: Wudu is required because of it. Ali b. al-Madini held the view of the Kufans and adopted their position. Yahya b. Ma'in cited as evidence the hadith of Busrah bt. Safwan, while Ali b. al-Madini cited the hadith of Qays b. Talq. He said to Yahya: How can you rely on the chain of Busrah when Marwan sent a guard to bring her answer back to him? Yahya replied: People have said much about Qays b. Talq, and his hadith cannot be used as evidence. Ahmad b. Hanbal said: Both positions are as you two have stated. Yahya said: Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he performed wudu after touching the penis. Ali said: Ibn Mas'ud used to say: Wudu is not required because of it; it is only a piece of your body. Yahya said: From whom? He said: Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Hudhayl, from Abdullah. When Ibn Mas'ud and Ibn Umar are brought together and they differ, Ibn Mas'ud is more deserving of being followed. Ahmad said to him: Yes, but Abu Qays's hadith cannot be used as evidence. He said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to me: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Umayr b. Sa'id, from Ammar b. Yasir, who said: I do not care whether I touched it or my nose. Ahmad said: Ammar and Ibn Umar are equal. Whoever wishes may take this position, and whoever wishes may take that position."],[549,"I do not care whether I touched my penis, or touched my nose, or my ear while I was praying."],[550,"I do not care whether I touched my penis during prayer or touched my ear."],[551,"Umar was asked about touching the armpit, and he said: Wudu is required because of it."],[552,"When a man performs wudu and touches his armpit, he repeats the wudu."],[553,"He does not have to repeat it."],[554,"When a man touches his armpit, let him perform wudu."],[555,"Touching the armpit was mentioned in the presence of Ayyub, and he said: 'Many an armpit is such that one ought to perform ghusl from it.'"],[557,"ﷺ underwent cupping then prayed and did not perform wudu, and did no more than washing the places of his cupping. This is a hadith that Ibn Abi al-Ishrin raised as marfu, while Abu al-Mughirah stopped it at al-Awza'i, and that is the correct view."],[559,"When he performed wudu, he would rub his cheeks and sometimes intertwine his beard with his fingers, and sometimes he would leave it."],[562,"ﷺ something similar, and the mursal is the correct version."],[564,"He said: 'The sea is purifying water for the angels: when they descend they perform wudu, and when they ascend they perform wudu.'"],[568,"ﷺ the like of that."],[569,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yahya narrated to us: Muhammad b. al-Sabbah narrated to us: Ismail b. Ayyash narrated to us with these two chains together, something similar."],[571,"ﷺ the like of it."],[572,"Muhammad b. Sahl narrated to us: Ali b. Zayd al-Faraidi narrated to us: al-Rabi b. Nafi narrated to us from Ismail b. Ayyash from Abbad b. Kathir and Ata b. Ajlan from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Aishah the like of it. Abbad b. Kathir and Ata b. Ajlan are weak. Ismail b. Ayyash likewise narrated it from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Aishah, and Sulayman b. Arqam concurred with him, but he is matruk al-hadith. The precise memorizers among the companions of Ibn Jurayj narrate it from Ibn Jurayj from his father as mursal, and Allah knows best."],[574,"ﷺ the like of that."],[593,"ﷺ vomited and broke his fast. Then I met Thawban in the mosque of Damascus and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'He spoke the truth; I poured out his wudu water for him.'"],[594,"Al-Husayn b. Ismail narrated to us: Yusuf b. Musa, Ahmad b. Mansur, and Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Isa narrated to us, they said: Abu Ma'mar Abdullah b. Amr b. Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Abdul Warith b. Sa'id narrated to us: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir: Abu Amr Abd al-Rahman b. Amr al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ya'ish b. al-Walid b. Hisham, that his father narrated to him: Ma'dan narrated to me that Abu al-Darda' narrated to him. Then he mentioned from Abu al-Darda' and from Thawban, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[595,"I poured his ablution water for him."],[596,"He spoke the truth, and I poured his ablution water for him."],[599,"ﷺ slept while prostrating until he snored or breathed heavily, then he stood up and prayed. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have slept.\" He said, \"Ablution is only required for one who sleeps lying down, for when he lies down his joints relax.\""],[601,"From Abu Bakr b. Abi Maryam with his chain, the like of it."],[610,"Muhammad b. Ismail al-Farisi and Uthman b. Ahmad al-Daqqaq narrated to us, they said: Yahya b. Abi Talib narrated to us: Abdul Wahhab narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[611,"ﷺ something similar."],[612,"From Abu al-Aliyah, the like of it."],[618,"He said: I read it in the book of the son of my brother al-Zuhri, from Sulayman b. Arqam, from al-Hasan."],[619,"ﷺ commanded one who laughed in prayer to repeat the ablution and the prayer."],[622,"ﷺ commanded one who laughed in prayer to repeat the ablution and the prayer."],[630,"From Abu al-Aliyah with this."],[633,"upon him ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Abu al-'Aliyah. And likewise Matur al-Warraq narrated it from Hafsah, from Abu al-'Aliyah."],[637,"upon him ﷺ, he commanded the one who laughed to repeat the ablution and the prayer."],[639,"upon him ﷺ, something similar."],[640,"upon him ﷺ, the same as it."],[648,"from those from whom they both took their hadith."],[649,"He said: There were four who would believe whoever narrated to them, and they did not care from whom they heard hadith: al-Hasan, Abu al-'Aliyah, Humayd b. Hilal, and Dawud b. Abi Hind. The Shaykh said: He did not mention the fourth, and this is a hadith narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, so he mentioned it and mentioned its defect."],[651,"There is no ablution due to laughing."],[652,"There is no ablution due to laughing."],[653,"that he was asked about a man who laughs in prayer, and he said: He repeats the prayer but does not repeat the ablution."],[654,"When a man laughs in prayer, he repeats the prayer but does not repeat the ablution."],[655,"Regarding the one who laughs in prayer, he said: He repeats the prayer but does not repeat the ablution."],[656,"When he laughs in prayer, he repeats the prayer but does not repeat the ablution."],[657,"He was asked about laughing in prayer and said: He repeats the prayer and does not perform ablution."],[658,"He said regarding laughing in prayer: He does not have to repeat the ablution."],[659,"There is no ablution upon one who laughs in prayer."],[660,"There is no ablution for laughing."],[664,"He did not deem ablution obligatory upon one who laughs in prayer."],[665,"Smiling does not invalidate the prayer until one guffaws."],[666,"If one of you laughs in prayer, he must repeat the prayer."],[667,"Abu Musa went out in a delegation that included a one-eyed man from Abd al-Qays. Abu Musa prayed, and they bowed, then they retreated on their heels, and the one-eyed man fell into a well. Al-Ahnaf said: When I heard him falling into it, none of the people laughed except me and Abu Musa. When he finished the prayer, he said: What is the matter with these? They said: So-and-so fell into a well. He ordered them, and they repeated the prayer."],[668,"Abu Musa said when he finished his prayer: Whoever among you laughed, let him repeat the prayer."],[669,"He was leading the people in prayer when they saw something, and some of those with him laughed. Abu Musa said when he finished: Whoever among you laughed, let him repeat the prayer."],[674,"And he said: The entire earth has been made for us a place of prostration, and its dust a means of purification, if he does not find water."],[679,"Abu Mu'adh said: And Kharijah narrated to me, from Abdullah b. Ata, from Musa b. Uqbah, from Al-A'raj, from Abu Juhaym, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[682,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His statement: \"And if you are ill or on a journey\" [al-Nisa: 43], he said: When a man has a wound in the path of Allah, or sores, or smallpox, and then becomes junub, and fears that he may die if he performs ghusl, he should perform tayammum."],[683,"Concession was given to the sick person to perform tayammum with clean earth."],[690,"Tayammum is two strikes: one strike for the face and one strike for the two hands up to the elbows."],[691,"Ibn Umar used to perform tayammum up to the elbows."],[694,"In tayammum, there are two strikes: one strike for the face and one strike for the two hands up to the elbows."],[696,"He said: I was in a state of janabah and I rolled in the dust. He said: Strike. So he struck with his hand and wiped his face, then struck with his other hand and wiped his two hands up to the elbows."],[698,"When he performed tayammum, he would strike with his two hands once and wipe his face with them, then strike with his two hands another time and wipe his two hands up to the elbows, and he would not shake the dust off his hands."],[704,"upon him be peace, with this."],[706,"I heard Ammar b. Yasir giving a khutbah in Kufa and he mentioned tayammum. He struck the ground with his hand and wiped his face and his two hands."],[707,"He dipped the inner parts of his palms in the dust, then blew on them, then wiped his face and his two hands up to the wrist joint. And Ammar said: This is how tayammum is done."],[708,"Whatever ghusl is commanded for, tayammum is required for it; and whatever ghusl is not commanded for, it is left."],[709,"And that it is done for every prayer."],[710,"Amr b. al-As used to perform tayammum for every prayer, and Qatadah used to give this ruling."],[711,"Tayammum is to be performed for every prayer."],[712,"Tayammum is to be performed for every prayer."],[713,"Ibn Umar used to perform tayammum for every prayer."],[714,"It is part of the Sunnah that a man should not pray with tayammum except one prayer, then he should perform tayammum for the next prayer."],[715,"It is part of the Sunnah that no more than one prayer should be prayed with a single tayammum."],[716,"No more than one prayer should be prayed with a single tayammum."],[718,"A shackled person should not lead those who are unshackled, nor should one who has performed tayammum lead those who have performed wudu."],[719,"From Hajjaj with his chain, something similar regarding tayammum. A chapter on clarifying the place where tayammum is permissible and its distance from the town and seeking water."],[721,"Ibn Umar performed tayammum at the livestock enclosure and prayed while he was three miles from Madinah. Then he entered Madinah while the sun was still high and did not repeat [the prayer]."],[722,"From Ibn Ajlan with his chain, the same."],[723,"Ibn Umar performed tayammum at a distance of one or two miles from Madinah and prayed Asr. Then he arrived while the sun was still high and did not repeat the prayer."],[724,"When a man becomes junub during travel, he waits for whatever time remains until the end of the prayer time. If he does not find water, he performs tayammum and prays."],[729,"Indeed that is a purifier."],[732,"That two men became junub and then performed tayammum."],[735,"Al-Mahamili narrated to us: Al-Za'farani narrated to us: Al-Hakam b. Musa narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[736,"ﷺ with something similar to it until its end, like the statement of Hiql."],[738,"ﷺ something similar to it."],[739,"It has reached me from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, the like of the hadith of Al-Walid b. Mazyad."],[740,"ﷺ similar to the statement of Al-Walid b. Mazyad, and Isma'il b. Yazid b. Samā'ah and Muhammad b. Shu'ayb concurred with the two of them. Chapter on the permissibility of wiping over part of the head."],[742,"ﷺ wiped over the khuffayn, the front of his head, and over his turban."],[744,"ﷺ performed wudu and wiped over his forelock, and wiped over the khuffayn and the turban. Bakr said: I heard it from Ibn al-Mughirah. Chapter on wiping over the khuffayn."],[747,"From Al-A'mash with his chain, something similar to it."],[752,"Abu Bakr al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Ibrahim al-Harbi narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us: exactly the like of it."],[753,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you wipe over your khuffs? He said: I put them on while they were pure."],[754,"Wiping over the top of the khuffs is streaks with the fingers."],[755,"Waki' narrated to us; Fudayl narrated to us something similar."],[757,"Upon him be peace, as a mursal report, in which al-Mughirah is not mentioned."],[760,"I asked Yazid b. Abi Habib about wiping over the khuffs, and he said: Abdullah b. al-Hakam al-Balawi reported to me from Ali b. Rabah from Uqbah b. Amir that he informed him that he came as a delegate to Umar b. al-Khattab one year. Uqbah said: I was wearing two khuffs of those thick khuffs, and Umar said to me: When did you last put them on? I said: I put them on on Friday, and today is Friday. Umar said to him: You have hit upon the Sunnah. Yunus said: He said: You have hit upon it, and he did not say: the Sunnah."],[761,"He said: I went out from Syria to Madinah on Friday, and I entered Madinah on Friday, and I entered upon Umar b. al-Khattab. He said: When did you insert your feet into your khuffs? I said: On Friday. He said: Did you take them off? I said: No. He said: You have hit upon the Sunnah. Abu Bakr said: This is a gharib hadith. Abu al-Hasan said: Its isnad is sahih."],[762,"He used not to set a time limit for wiping over the khuffs."],[763,"There is no time limit for wiping over the khuffs; wipe as long as you do not take them off."],[764,"The traveler wipes over the khuffs as long as he does not take them off."],[766,"He said to me: Our companions narrated it, for al-Shafi'i has no proof stronger than this, meaning his saying: When we put them on while pure."],[770,"He narrated to him that he came to Umar at the conquest of Damascus. He said: I was wearing two khuffs, and Umar said to me: How long has it been, O Uqbah, since you took off your khuffs? I recalled from Friday to Friday, and I said: For eight days. He said: You have done well and hit upon the Sunnah."],[771,"You have hit upon the Sunnah, and he did not mention anyone between Yazid and Ali b. Rabah."],[779,"He was brought a funeral while he was not in a state of ablution, so he performed tayammum and then prayed over it."],[780,"He said: Zayd b. Thabit had become incontinent of urine, and he would try to control what overcame him of it. When it overcame him, he would let it flow, and he would pray while it was coming out of him."],[781,"Zayd b. Thabit grew old until he became incontinent of urine. He would try to control it as much as he could, but when it overcame him, he would perform ablution and pray."],[782,"Even if it flowed onto my thigh, I would not leave. Sufyan said: meaning urine, when one is afflicted."],[784,"upon him ﷺ the like of it. Ibn Sa'id said: I do not know of anyone who brought it except Asad b. Musa."],[786,"upon him ﷺ: A concession was given to the traveler for three days and their nights, and to the resident for a day and a night, if he purifies himself and puts on his leather socks, to wipe over them. Likewise Yahya b. Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab, and likewise the companions of Bundar narrated it from him, and the companions of Ibn Muhammad b. Aban al-Balkhi narrated it from him, in agreement with Ibn Khuzayma on his saying 'then he puts on his leather socks.'"],[789,"He used to wipe over splints."],[790,"Regarding a man who performs ablution and wipes over his leather socks, then removes them. They both said: He should wash his feet."],[801,"He said: Menstruation is fifteen [days]."],[802,"The maximum of menstruation is fifteen [days]."],[803,"He said: Menstruation is fifteen [days]."],[804,"The maximum of menstruation is fifteen [days]."],[805,"The minimum duration of menstruation is one day."],[806,"We have a woman who menstruates fifteen days of the month, a regular and sound menstruation."],[807,"He says: We have here a woman who menstruates in the morning and becomes pure in the evening."],[808,"The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days."],[809,"Menstruation is three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, or ten [days]. If it exceeds that, she is a woman with irregular bleeding (mustahāḍah)."],[810,"He said: The menstrual cycles (qurūʾ) are three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, and ten."],[811,"Menstruation is three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, or ten [days]."],[812,"Wakīʿ said: Menstruation is from three to ten [days]. Whatever exceeds that, she is a woman with irregular bleeding (mustahāḍah)."],[813,"Menstruation cannot be more than ten days."],[814,"The minimum duration of menstruation is three days and its maximum is ten days."],[815,"She is menstruating between that and ten days. If it exceeds that, she is a woman with irregular bleeding (mustahāḍah)."],[817,"Regarding the woman with irregular bleeding (mustahāḍah): she waits for three, five, seven, or ten [days]."],[818,"The menstruating woman waits three days, or four, or five, up to ten days. If it exceeds ten days, then she is suffering from irregular bleeding, and she should perform ghusl and pray."],[819,"A woman is not considered to have irregular bleeding in one day, nor two days, nor three days, until she reaches ten days. When she reaches ten days, she is considered to have irregular bleeding."],[820,"When the menstruating woman exceeds ten days, she is in the position of one with irregular bleeding: she performs ghusl and prays."],[821,"He said: Menstruation is thirteen."],[826,"Fatimah bt. Abu Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who experiences istihadah and do not become pure; should I stop praying? He said: \"Leave prayer during the days of your menstrual periods, then bathe and pray, even if the blood drips onto the mat.\"[1]"],[827,"Then perform ghusl, and perform wudu for every prayer, and pray, even if the blood drips onto the mat."],[830,"Yahya said: Indeed, Sufyan al-Thawri was the most knowledgeable of people about this. He claimed that Habib b. Abi Thabit did not hear anything from Urwah b. al-Zubayr."],[831,"That it contains the wudu for every prayer, and it also indicates the weakness of the hadith of Habib from Urwah, because al-Zuhri narrated it from Urwah from Aishah and said in it: She used to perform ghusl for every prayer. All of this is the statement of Abu Dawud."],[832,"Regarding the woman with irregular bleeding: she prays even if the blood drips onto her mat."],[834,"The woman with irregular bleeding prays even if the blood drips onto the mat."],[835,"From Urwah two hadiths, and they are nothing."],[837,"Indeed, the quru' are the periods of purity."],[839,"From Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Aqil with this chain, something similar."],[840,"Muhammad b. al-Qasim b. Zakariyya narrated to us: Abbad b. Ya'qub reported to us: Amr b. Thabit narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, with this chain, something similar."],[841,"Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Malik al-Iskafi narrated to us: al-Harith b. Muhammad narrated to us: Zakariyya b. Adi narrated to us: Ubayd Allah b. Amr narrated to us, from Ibn Aqil, with this, something similar."],[842,"From Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, with his chain, something similar."],[843,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh has been suffering from prolonged vaginal bleeding since such-and-such. He said: 'Glory be to Allah! This is from Satan. Let her sit in a large basin.' So she sat in it until she saw yellowishness above the water. He said: 'She should perform one ghusl for Zuhr and Asr, then one ghusl for Maghrib and Isha, then one ghusl for Fajr, and perform wudu in between those.'"],[844,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh has not prayed since such-and-such. He said: 'Glory be to Allah! That is only a vein.' Then he mentioned a word after it: 'the days of her menstrual periods.' Then she should perform ghusl and pray, and she should delay Zuhr and hasten Asr, and perform one ghusl for both; and delay Maghrib and hasten Isha, and perform one ghusl for both and pray."],[853,"Regarding the pregnant woman who sees blood, she said: 'The pregnant woman does not menstruate; she performs ghusl and prays.'"],[854,"We used not to consider the taryah after purification to be anything, and it is the yellowishness and dullness."],[855,"That she disliked her husband having intercourse with a woman suffering from prolonged vaginal bleeding."],[857,"He used to say to his wives: 'None of you should observe post-natal bleeding for less than forty days, nor exceed forty days' - meaning in post-natal bleeding."],[859,"He used to say to his wives: 'When one of you gives birth, she should not come near me for forty days, unless she sees purification before that.'"],[864,"The post-natal woman sits for forty days."],[867,"She sits after her post-natal bleeding. And this Abu Sahl is Kathir b. Ziyad al-Bursani."],[868,"Ahmad b. Hanbal was asked — while I was listening — about a woman with postpartum bleeding: how long does she remain if she sees blood? He said: Forty days, then she performs ghusl."],[876,"Upon him be peace, he passed by him while he was in the mosque wearing a burdah that had exposed his thigh, and he said: Indeed, the thigh is awrah."],[877,"Upon him be peace, the like of it."],[881,"Upon him be peace, the like of it. Abu al-Walid Khalid b. Yazid al-Makki is weak."],[883,"Said b. Salim narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us: Amr b. Khalid narrated to us with his chain of narration the like of it. Chapter: Explaining the location in which prayer is permissible and the garments that are permissible therein."],[884,"About a walled garden into which human excrement and refuse are thrown — he said: When it has been watered three times, pray in it."],[898,"Upon him be peace, something similar to it."],[899,"Upon him be peace, something similar to it."],[900,"Upon him be peace, something similar to it."],[901,"Muhammad b. Isa b. Sumay narrated to us with his chain of narration the like of it."],[903,"Ahmad b. Yusuf b. Khallad narrated to us: al-Muammari narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Ar`arah narrated to us with his chain of narration the like of it."],[906,"And I heard him performing the iqamah, saying: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar. Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah. Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah. Hayya ala al-salah. Hayya ala al-falah. Qad qamat al-salah, qad qamat al-salah. Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar. La ilaha illa Allah. And I think he was relating the iqamah as a report, just as he relates the adhan."],[909,"Upon him be peace, he cast this adhan: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to prayer. Come to success, come to success. Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. There is no god but Allah."],[911,"I reached my grandfather, my father, and my family making the iqamah, and they would say: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to success. The prayer has been established, the prayer has been established. Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. There is no god but Allah."],[912,"Upon him be peace, he called Abu Mahdhurah and taught him the adhan, and commanded him to call the adhan in the mihrabs of Makkah: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, twice; and he commanded him to make the iqamah one by one."],[913,"Upon him be peace, he taught him the adhan of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases. The adhan: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to prayer. Come to success, come to success. Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest. There is no god but Allah. And the iqamah is thus, in pairs, in pairs; he does not repeat from that point."],[920,"Umar b. al-Khattab came to us and said: When you call the adhan, chant slowly, and when you make the iqamah, be brisk."],[922,"Abu Mahdhurah was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd, and to turn around in his iqamah."],[925,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd, except for the iqamah."],[926,"Bilal used to repeat the adhan twice and make the iqamah once, except for his saying: The prayer has been established."],[927,"Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[928,"Upon him be peace, he commanded Bilal to make the adhan even and the iqamah odd."],[929,"Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us something similar."],[931,"Bilal used to repeat the adhan twice and make the iqamah once, except for his saying: The prayer has been established."],[936,"When he did not catch the prayer with the people, he would give the adhan and the iqama, and he would repeat the iqama. Mawquf."],[944,"Bilal used to repeat the adhan and repeat the iqama. He would begin with the takbir and end with the takbir."],[945,"His adhan and his iqama were twice, twice."],[946,"Sufyan heard it from him."],[948,"The mu'adhdhin said in the adhan of Fajr: 'Hayya 'ala al-falah.' He said: 'Al-salatu khayrun min al-nawm, al-salatu khayrun min al-nawm' twice. 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.'"],[949,"The tathwib was in the morning prayer. When the mu'adhdhin said in the adhan of Fajr: 'Hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah,' he should say: 'Al-salatu khayrun min al-nawm, al-salatu khayrun min al-nawm.'"],[950,"He said to his mu'adhdhin: 'When you reach \"Hayya 'ala al-falah\" in Fajr, say: \"Al-salatu khayrun min al-nawm, al-salatu khayrun min al-nawm.\"'"],[954,"The end of Bilal's adhan was: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.'"],[955,"Bilal said: 'The end of the adhan is: La ilaha illa Allah.'"],[956,"The end of Bilal's adhan was: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.'"],[957,"The end of the adhan is: 'Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.'"],[959,"From a mu'adhdhin of Umar called Masruh: he gave the adhan before dawn, so Umar ordered him."],[960,"Bilal called the adhan once at night."],[964,"Bilal called the adhan, and he did not mention Anas; the mursal is more correct."],[967,"My grandfather Abdullah b. Zayd was involved in this account, and my grandfather gave the iqamah. Abu Dawud said: Muhammad b. Amr is a Madinan, and Ibn Mahdi does not narrate from the Basran."],[970,"We used to come to Aishah before the dawn prayer. One day we came to her while she was praying, and we said to her, \"What is this prayer?\" She said, \"I overslept and missed my portion tonight, and I was not going to abandon it.\""],[978,"upon him ﷺ something similar."],[991,"He would pray Asr while the sun was white and high, a man traveling from it until he reached Dhul-Hulayfah, six miles before sunset. He also said in it: He would pray Subh and would make it very dark, then he prayed it another day and made it bright, then he did not return to making it bright until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took him."],[996,"Al-Layth narrated to us."],[999,"Upon him ﷺ: He would pray Asr, then a person would go to Quba. One of them said, \"He would come to them while they were praying,\" and the other said, \"while the sun was high.\" Da`laj b. Ahmad narrated this to us; al-Hasan b. Sufyan narrated to us; Hibban b. Musa narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak informed us from Malik with that."],[1003,"Upon him ﷺ: Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He watches the sun until when it becomes yellow and is between the two horns of Satan, he stands and pecks four times, not remembering Allah in them except a little."],[1008,"It is only called Asr because it presses."],[1009,"Al-Hasan, Ibn Sirin, and Abu Qilabah used to perform the evening with Asr."],[1010,"It is only called Asr so that one may press."],[1011,"Tawus delayed the Asr prayer greatly. He was asked about that, and he said, \"It was only called Asr because it is squeezed.\""],[1012,"Abd Allah used to delay the Asr."],[1014,"peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something similar."],[1020,"peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with this in its entirety."],[1027,"peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with something similar, in mursal form."],[1028,"peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the times of prayer. He advanced and then delayed, and said, \"Between them is a time.\""],[1031,"Then he came to him the next day and prayed Maghrib for him at one time, when the sun had set and the fasting person's breaking of the fast had become lawful."],[1035,"It used to be said that prayer has a beginning and an end."],[1036,"The beginning of the time of Asr is when the sun is white, until Maghrib arrives."],[1038,"Sa'dan b. Nasr narrated to us: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us with this, in abridged form, regarding the two times of Maghrib."],[1039,"peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, something similar."],[1040,"Then he ordered him to pray Maghrib when the sun had set. Then he ordered him the next day to pray Maghrib before the twilight disappeared."],[1043,"He performed the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set. He said: Then on the following day he delayed the Maghrib until it was near the disappearance of the twilight."],[1051,"The stranger would enter the mosque of Madinah after the call to Maghrib had been given, and he would think that the people had already prayed because of the large number of those who prayed two rak‘ahs before Maghrib."],[1053,"When they heard the call to Maghrib, they would stand and pray as if it were an obligatory prayer."],[1055,"When the call to Maghrib was given in Madinah, the people would rush to the pillars and pray two rak‘ahs, so much so that a stranger entering the mosque would think the prayer had already been performed because of the large number of those praying it."],[1058,"The twilight is of two kinds: the redness and the whiteness. When the redness disappears, prayer becomes permissible. And the dawn is of two kinds: the elongated and the spreading. When the spreading dawn breaks, prayer becomes permissible."],[1059,"The twilight is the redness."],[1061,"The twilight is the redness. A chapter on the description of the last ‘Isha’ prayer."],[1063,"On a third or fourth night."],[1067,"It was revealed specifically concerning supererogatory prayer, wherever your mount turns you."],[1071,"Ash‘ath b. Sa‘id narrated to us with this, similar to the statement of Yazid b. Harun. A chapter on mentioning the command regarding the call to prayer and leading the prayer, and who is more entitled to them."],[1073,"Pray as you have seen me pray."],[1078,"When the qiblah was changed to the Ka‘bah, a man passed by the people of Quba’ while they were praying and said to them, “The qiblah has been changed to the Ka‘bah,” so they turned around in front of them toward the Ka‘bah. A chapter on mentioning the prayer of one performing an obligatory prayer behind one performing a supererogatory prayer."],[1098,"He used to grasp his left hand with his right hand in prayer."],[1099,"She said: Three things are from prophethood: hastening the iftar, delaying the sahur, and placing the right hand over the left hand in prayer."],[1102,"Placing palm upon palm in prayer is from the Sunnah."],[1107,"Indeed, part of the Sunnah of prayer is placing the right hand over the left hand below the navel."],[1117,"He would raise [his hands], then say the takbir."],[1120,"When he began the takbir in prayer, he raised his hands when he said the takbir until he brought them level with his shoulders."],[1122,"Ibn Umar, when he saw a man praying without raising his hands each time he lowered and raised, he pelted him with pebbles until he raised [them]."],[1134,"From al-Bara' b. Azib, something similar."],[1139,"Upon him be peace, something similar, except that he did not mention the prostration."],[1140,"Abu al-Qasim Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ismail b. Ayyash Abu Utbah narrated to us, from Salih b. Kaysan, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah."],[1148,"That when he said the takbir for prayer, he said: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, and blessed is Your name, and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You."],[1150,"That he went to Umar b. al-Khattab. He said: I saw him, when he opened the prayer, say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, and blessed is Your name, and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You."],[1152,"Then he seeks refuge."],[1154,"When he began the prayer, he would say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name; exalted is Your majesty; and there is no god other than You."],[1155,"He says: Glory be to You, O Allah."],[1159,"Uthman, when he began the prayer, would say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name; exalted is Your majesty; and there is no god other than You – he would let us hear that."],[1170,"Upon him be peace and blessings, when he began the prayer, he would start with 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) [Al-Fatiha 1]. And al-Naysaburi said: he would recite."],[1174,"From Sa'id b. Abi Hilal with this chain, something similar."],[1175,"Khalid b. Yazid narrated to me with this chain, the like of it."],[1179,"Upon him be peace and blessings, he used to recite aloud 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' [Al-Fatiha 1]. The correct report is from Abu Ma'shar."],[1180,"He used to recite: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Master of the Day of Judgment. You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help. Guide us to the straight path – the path of those You have blessed, not of those who have incurred wrath, nor of those who have gone astray. He would cut it off verse by verse and count it as the bedouins count, and he counted 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' [Al-Fatiha 1] as a verse, but he did not count 'upon them' [Al-Fatiha 7]."],[1192,"He informed him, saying: Mu'awiya led a prayer in Madinah and recited aloud in it, but he did not recite 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' [Al-Fatiha 1] for the Mother of the Qur'an, nor did he recite it for the surah after it, nor did he say the takbir when he went down until he finished that prayer. When he said the salam, those who heard that from among the Muhajirun and the Ansar called out to him from every place: 'O Mu'awiya, did you steal the prayer or forget?' He said: After that, he did not pray except that he recited 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' [Al-Fatiha 1] for the Mother of the Qur'an and for the surah after it, and he said the takbir when he went down to prostrate. All of them are trustworthy."],[1197,"Upon him be peace and blessings, when he opened the prayer, he said: 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds' [Al-Fatiha 2], then he remained silent for a moment. No one raised it [to the Prophet] except Abu Dawud from Shu'ba; others stopped it as the action of Abu Hurayra."],[1203,"She said: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Alif Lam Mim. Allah – there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer. He sent down to you the Book' [Al Imran 1-2], up to His saying: 'those who follow what is ambiguous of it' up to His saying: 'we believe in it' [Al Imran 7]. So when you see those, they are the ones Allah has named, so beware of them. Chapter on mention of the difference in narration regarding reciting aloud 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' [Al-Fatiha 1]."],[1207,"For they were not reciting aloud. Ubayd Allah b. Musa followed him from Shu'bah and Hammam, from Qatadah."],[1215,"That he asked 'Umar about reciting behind the imam. He said: \"Recite the Opening of the Book.\" I said: \"Even if it is you?\" He said: \"Even if it is I.\" I said: \"Even if you recite aloud?\" He said: \"Even if I recite aloud.\" Its narrators are all trustworthy."],[1216,"I asked 'Umar about reciting behind the imam, and he commanded me to recite. He said: I said: \"Even if it is you?\" He said: \"Even if it is I.\" I said: \"Even if you recite aloud?\" He said: \"Even if I recite aloud.\" This is a sound chain."],[1217,"I asked Ubayy b. Ka'b: \"Should I recite behind the imam?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[1219,"\"It is as if you are reciting behind me.\" We said: \"Indeed, this is true, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Do not do so except with the Opening of the Book, for there is no prayer without it.\""],[1220,"He said: Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us with this."],[1221,"And he said in it: \"Indeed I see you reciting behind your imam when he recites aloud.\" We said: \"Indeed, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this is so.\" He said: \"Do not do so except with the Mother of the Qur'an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.\""],[1226,"upon him ﷺ something similar, and he said in it: \"Let none of you recite except with the Opening of the Book, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.\""],[1230,"There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book."],[1235,"He used to command or prefer that in the noon and afternoon prayers, in the first two rak'ahs, one recite the Opening of the Book and a surah, and in the last two, the Opening of the Book, behind the imam."],[1236,"Shu'bah narrated to us with its chain something similar."],[1242,"upon him ﷺ, and this is the correct view."],[1247,"From Jabir something similar, but as a statement of a Companion (mawquf)."],[1251,"Upon him be peace, with this: Abu Sa'd al-Saghani is weak."],[1259,"Upon him be peace, something similar."],[1261,"From Ibn al-Asbahani, but its chain of transmission is not sound."],[1264,"Only someone who is not upon the natural disposition recites behind the imam."],[1265,"The recitation of the imam suffices you."],[1266,"He narrates from Ali something similar."],[1268,"O Kathir, I do not think the imam has not sufficed them."],[1272,"Upon him be peace, when he said, \"not of those who have incurred anger, nor of those who are astray\" [al-Fatihah:7], he said \"Amin,\" prolonging his voice with it. Abu Bakr said: This is a sunnah in which the people of Kufa are alone. This is sound, and what follows it."],[1273,"Upon him be peace, he raised his voice with \"Amin\" when he said, \"not of those who have incurred anger, nor of those who are astray\" [al-Fatihah:7]."],[1274,"Upon him be peace, he recited, \"not of those who have incurred anger, nor of those who are astray\" [al-Fatihah:7], then he said \"Amin\" and prolonged his voice with it. Abd al-Rahman said: The most serious thing about it is that a man was asking Sufyan about this hadith, and I think Sufyan spoke part of it. Shu'bah contradicted him in its chain of transmission and its text."],[1278,"Upon him be peace, something similar. Bahr al-Siqqa is weak."],[1281,"When he began the prayer, he would remain silent for a short while, and when he recited “nor of those who go astray” [al-Fātiḥah 7], he would pause briefly. That was objected to, so he wrote about it to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, who wrote back that the matter was as Samurah had done."],[1284,"He said: I prayed behind Ibn ʿAbbās in al-Baṣrah. In the first rakʿah he recited al-Ḥamd and the first verse of al-Baqarah; then he stood for the second and recited al-Ḥamd and the second verse of al-Baqarah; then he bowed. When he finished, he turned to us and said: Allah Almighty says, “So recite what is easy of it” [al-Muzzammil 20]. This is a good isnad, and it contains evidence for those who say that the meaning of His saying “So recite what is easy of it” is only after reciting the Opening of the Book. And Allah knows best."],[1287,"He said the takbīr and raised his hands. When he bowed, he placed his hands together between his knees. That reached Saʿd, and he said: My brother spoke the truth. We used to do this; then we were commanded to do this, and he placed the palms on the knees."],[1289,"O Buraydah, when you raise your head from bowing, say: Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that."],[1294,"They said: ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAmr narrated to us with this."],[1296,"When you reach the people while they are bowing, say the takbīr and bow, for it will suffice you as one for both the takbīr and the bowing."],[1297,"He used to say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent and with His praise, three times; and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord the Most High and with His praise."],[1298,"It is part of the Sunnah that a man say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent and with His praise, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord the Most High and with His praise."],[1300,"When he bowed, he would say…"],[1305,"He used to say in his bowing: All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit."],[1306,"He used to say in his bowing and prostration…"],[1308,"Upon him be peace, when he prostrated he would place his hands before his knees."],[1310,"When one of you prostrates, let him place his hands before his knees, and let him not kneel like a camel kneels."],[1311,"When the imam says, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” those behind him say, “Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs all praise.”"],[1321,"A prayer is not valid in which a man does not straighten his back."],[1326,"It is part of the sunnah of prayer that the left foot be laid flat and the right foot be erected."],[1327,"It is part of the sunnah of prayer that the left foot be laid flat and the right foot be erected."],[1328,"It is part of the sunnah of prayer that the left foot be laid flat and the right foot be erected."],[1349,"If I were to pray any prayer in which I did not invoke blessings upon the family of Muhammad, I would not consider my prayer complete."],[1350,"I have never prayed a prayer in which I did not invoke blessings upon Muhammad except that I thought my prayer was incomplete."],[1355,"He used to say two taslims."],[1363,"When he sits for the length of the tashahhud, his prayer is complete."],[1372,"If the imam leads the people in prayer while he is not in a state of purity, the prayer of the people is valid and he repeats it."],[1375,"He led the people in prayer while he was in a state of major ritual impurity, so he repeated it, then he commanded them and they repeated it."],[1376,"That Umar prayed with the people while he was ritually impure, so he repeated and did not order them to repeat."],[1377,"That Uthman b. Affan prayed with the people while he was ritually impure; when morning came he looked at his garment and saw a wet dream, and he said: 'I have grown old, by Allah. Do I not see myself becoming ritually impure and then not knowing?' Then he repeated and did not order them to repeat."],[1378,"Concerning a man who prayed with a group while not in a state of ablution, he said: 'He repeats and they do not repeat.'"],[1379,"That Ibn Umar prayed with his companions, then he remembered that he had touched his private part, so he performed ablution and did not order them to repeat. Ibn Mahdi said: I said to Sufyan: 'Do you know of anyone who said they should repeat?' He said: 'No, except Hammad.'"],[1384,"Abu Dawud said: 'And everyone who narrated this hadith did not say \"so they gestured\", except Hammad b. Zayd.'"],[1389,"It used to be said: 'Nothing interrupts the prayer of a Muslim.'"],[1390,"Upon him be peace: 'A woman, a dog, and a donkey do not interrupt a person's prayer, and ward off from in front of you what you can.'"],[1399,"That he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness on the day Dhu al-Yadayn came to him after the taslim."],[1414,"When one of you doubts in prayer, let him strive for what is correct, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[1425,"He says: They did not criticize Jabir in his hadith; they only criticized it for his opinion. Abu Dawud said: 'And Jabir in my view is not reliable in his hadith and his opinion. Chapter: The lawful exit from prayer is the taslim.'"],[1431,"Ismail b. Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, Abbas b. Muhammad narrated to us, Ali b. al-Hasan b. Shaqiq narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Ibn Buraydah, from Imran b. Husayn, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. Abu al-Hasan said: Al-Bukhari transmitted it from Abdan, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibrahim b. Tahman."],[1433,"Al-Basur said."],[1435,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am not able to find a guide who suits me at every hour, and between me and the mosque are rivers and trees, so is it permissible for me to pray in my house? He said: Do you hear the iqamah? He said: Yes. He said: Then come to it."],[1450,"We said: Shall we not pray it tomorrow? He said: Allah forbids you from usury and takes it."],[1451,"upon him be peace with this, and he said: Allah forbids you from usury and accepts it from you. Chapter on the amount of distance for which prayer is shortened and the length of the period."],[1463,"upon him be peace something similar to it, and he said after the twilight had disappeared by an hour. Ibn Wahb concurred with him."],[1466,"upon him be peace similar to the statement of al-Naysaburi."],[1468,"from Hisham b. Sa'd with this, something similar to it, and he did not mention in it al-Mufaddal b. Fadalah."],[1469,"upon him be peace: During the expedition of Tabuk, when he departed before the sun had declined, he delayed Zuhr until Asr, then combined them and prayed them together. When he departed after the sun had declined, he prayed Zuhr and Asr, then set out. When he departed before Maghrib, he delayed Maghrib until he prayed it with Isha. When he departed after Maghrib, he prayed Isha early and prayed it with Maghrib. Abu Dawud said: No one narrated this except Qutaybah."],[1470,"al-Layth narrated to us with this, the like of it."],[1474,"upon him be peace something similar to it."],[1476,"Chapter on the description of prayer during travel, combining between two prayers without an excuse, and the description of prayer on a ship. Muhammad b. Harun Abu Hamid narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, Abdullah b. Dawud narrated to us from a man of the people of hadith from Ja'far b. Burqan from Maymun b. Mihran from Ibn Abbas with the like of the hadith."],[1477,"upon him be peace, he ordered him to pray standing unless he feared drowning. Al-Daraqutni said: That is, on a ship. In it is an unknown man."],[1485,"Usayd b. Hudayr had complained of sciatica and was our imam. He would come out to us and gesture to us with his hand: Sit down. So we sat, and he prayed with us sitting while we were sitting."],[1486,"The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, except the one sitting cross-legged."],[1494,"Whoever prompts the imam has spoken."],[1495,"It is speech — meaning prompting the imam."],[1496,"When the imam seeks to be fed by you, feed him."],[1501,"Al-Hasan b. al-Khadir narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Yunus narrated to us: Muhammad b. Adam narrated to us: Asad b. Amr narrated to us with this. No one reports it from al-Zuhri except Rawh b. Ghutayf, and he is matruk al-hadith."],[1502,"When the imam gives salam, give salam to your right and to your left, and let him not face any part of his prayer after it."],[1503,"Whatever you catch with the imam is the beginning of your prayer, and make up what he preceded you with of the Quran."],[1504,"From Said b. al-Musayyib similar to the statement of Ali."],[1505,"They both said: He should not make what he caught of the imam’s prayer the beginning of his prayer."],[1509,"That he said concerning recitation behind the imam: The recitation of the imam suffices you."],[1513,"Aisha led us as imam and stood among them during the prescribed prayer."],[1514,"Umm Salama led us as imam in the afternoon prayer and stood among us."],[1516,"May peace and blessings be upon him. He prayed Zuhr and recited “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.” He said, “Which of you is the reciter?” The man said, “I am.” He said, “I thought one of you was contending with me in it.” Shu‘bah said: I said to Qatādah, “Did he dislike that?” He said, “Had he disliked it, he would have forbidden it.”"],[1517,"I saw ‘Umar praying while his wound was gushing blood."],[1519,"May peace and blessings be upon him. He prostrated in Ṣād. Ibn Abī Dāwūd said: None narrated it except Ḥafṣ."],[1520,"He used to say in the prostration of recitation: My face has prostrated to the One who created it and split open its hearing and sight by His might and power."],[1522,"May peace and blessings be upon him. Regarding the prostration in Ṣād: Dāwūd prostrated it in repentance, while we prostrate it in gratitude."],[1523,"I saw ‘Umar recite Ṣād on the pulpit, then he descended and prostrated, then he climbed back onto the pulpit."],[1524,"‘Uthmān b. ‘Affān recited Ṣād on the pulpit, then he descended and prostrated."],[1527,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, in Sūrat al-Ḥajj there are two prostrations.” He said, “Yes, if you do not prostrate them, then do not recite them.”"],[1528,"I saw ‘Umar prostrate twice in al-Ḥajj. I said, “In the morning prayer?” He said, “In the morning prayer.”"],[1539,"One of them said, “O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me.” He said, “May Allah forgive you.”"],[1541,"From al-Thawrī."],[1543,"From Ḥajjāj with that."],[1544,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Ja'far b. Muhammad al-Khaffaf narrated to us: al-Haytham b. Jamil narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah and Mubarak b. Fadalah narrated to us, from Ya'la b. 'Ata', from Jabir b. Yazid, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of the statement of Hushaym."],[1546,"Ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us: 'Umar b. Hafs al-Wusabi narrated to us (h) And al-Husayn b. Isma'il and Muhammad b. Sulayman al-Nu'mani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad b. 'Amr b. Hannan narrated to us, they said: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Dhi Himayah narrated to me: 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr narrated to me, from Jabir b. Yazid, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Shu'bah. Chapter on repeating the prayer."],[1549,"Husayn narrated to us with this."],[1560,"Whoever is a neighbor of the mosque and hears the caller calling, but does not answer him without excuse, there is no prayer for him."],[1562,"The shaykh said: Hushaym raised it, and Qurad is an unknown shaykh from the Basrans."],[1565,"When one of you forgets his prayer and does not remember it except while he is with the imam, let him pray with the imam; then when he finishes his prayer, let him pray the prayer he forgot, then let him repeat his prayer that he prayed with the imam."],[1569,"Abu Bakr narrated to us: 'Abbas b. Muhammad narrated to us: Ja'far narrated to us with this, and he did not say 'voluntarily.'"],[1585,"That in every three there is an imam, or in every forty and above that: Friday, and Adha, and Fitr; and that is because they are a congregation."],[1591,"He said: I was the guide of my father when he lost his sight. When I took him out to Friday prayer and he heard the call to prayer, he would invoke blessings upon Abu Umamah and ask forgiveness for him. He remained doing that for a time, never hearing the call to Friday prayer without doing so. I said to him: Father, what is this asking forgiveness for Abu Umamah every time you hear the call to Friday prayer? He said: My son, he was the first to hold Friday prayer in Madinah, in a depression of the Harrah of Banu Bayadah called Naqi' al-Khadamat. He said: I said: How many were you that day? He said: Forty men."],[1592,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq with this."],[1593,"In the depression of al-Nabit of the Harrah of Banu Bayadah, in a Naqi' called Naqi' al-Khadamat."],[1597,"ﷺ the like of it, and he said: the call to prayer. Chapter: Friday prayer is upon the people of the village."],[1622,"When one of you comes while the imam is delivering the khutbah, let him pray two rak'ahs."],[1627,"ﷺ , when he ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, he paused the khutbah until he finished his two rak'ahs, then he returned to his khutbah. This is mursal; it cannot be used as proof. Abu Ma'shar's name is Najih, and he is weak."],[1628,"ﷺ , when he ordered him to pray, he paused the khutbah until he finished. This is also mursal, and Abu Ma'shar is weak; his name is Najih. Chapter: The Friday prayer before midday."],[1629,"He said: I attended Friday with Abu Bakr, and his prayer and khutbah were before midday. Then I attended it with Umar, and his prayer and khutbah were until one could say the day had reached its midpoint. Then I attended it with Uthman, and his prayer and khutbah were until one could say the sun had declined. I did not see anyone criticize or disapprove of that."],[1631,"We did not take a midday nap or eat lunch except after Jumu'ah."],[1632,"We used to eat lunch and take a midday nap after Jumu'ah."],[1633,"Al-Husayn narrated to us: Muhammad b. Hassan narrated to us: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl b. Sa'd, the like of it, exactly."],[1642,"Ibn Umar used to pray voluntarily on his mount, and when he wanted to perform Witr, he would dismount and perform Witr on the ground."],[1644,"ﷺ , it was said to him: One of us wakes up in the morning without having prayed Witr. He said: Then let him pray Witr when he wakes up."],[1651,"From al-Zuhri with this, similarly."],[1653,"From al-Zuhri."],[1676,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas prayed Isha, then performed Witr with a single rak'ah. A man said to him: O Abu Ishaq, did I not see you perform Witr with only one rak'ah? He said: O one-eyed, are you teaching me my religion?"],[1677,"You teach me my prayer"],[1678,"upon him be peace, he performed Witr with one rak'ah"],[1679,"I said: Tonight no one will beat me to the Maqam. Then a man came and placed his hand between my shoulders. I turned and it was the Commander of the Faithful, Uthman. I stepped aside, and he began the Quran and recited it in one rak'ah. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, you prayed only one rak'ah. He said: It is my Witr."],[1680,"A man said to Ibn Abbas: Are you not amazed at Mu'awiyah? He performs Witr with one rak'ah. He said: He did well; indeed he is a faqih."],[1681,"upon him be peace, he used to recite in the two rak'ahs after which he performed Witr: Sabbih isma rabbika al-a'la and Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun, and in the Witr: Qul huwa Allahu ahad, Qul a'udhu bi rabbi al-falaq, and Qul a'udhu bi rabbi al-nas."],[1684,"Witr is one; separate between the two and the one."],[1688,"He used to pray two light rak'ahs after Witr. Al-Mahamili added: while seated."],[1690,"upon him be peace, he performed Qunut in the Fajr and Maghrib prayers. Abu Bakr said to us: No one said in it from Shu'bah from Abu Ishaq except Baqiyyah."],[1691,"upon him be peace, he used to perform Qunut in Fajr and Maghrib."],[1699,"upon him be peace, he performed Qunut for a month, supplicating against them, then he left it. As for Fajr, he did not cease performing Qunut until he departed this world. Wording of al-Naysaburi."],[1706,"Regarding one who forgot Qunut in the Fajr prayer, he said: He owes two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[1707,"Regarding one who forgot Qunut in the Fajr prayer, he said: He prostrates two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[1710,"I bear witness that I heard Ibn Abbas say: Indeed, the qunut in the dawn prayer is an innovation."],[1713,"A sick person prays lying on his back, with his feet facing the qiblah."],[1715,"It is from the Sunnah that he should not go out until he has eaten and given the zakat al-fitr."],[1716,"He should not go out on the day of Eid al-Fitr until he has eaten and given the zakat al-fitr."],[1717,"I saw Ali on the day of Adha, he did not cease saying takbir until he came to the cemetery."],[1718,"He used to go out for the two Eids from the mosque, and he would say takbir until he came to the prayer place, and he would say takbir until he came to the imam."],[1719,"They used to be more intense in takbir on Eid al-Fitr than on Eid al-Adha."],[1721,"He would not go out on the day of Eid al-Fitr until he had eaten, and he would not eat anything on the day of Nahr until he returned and ate from his sacrificial animal."],[1722,"When he went out in the morning on the day of Eid al-Adha and the day of Eid al-Fitr, he would raise his voice with takbir until he came to the prayer place, then he would say takbir until he came to the imam."],[1728,"upon him be peace, similar to the hadith of Muhammad b. Uthman b. Thabit."],[1731,"upon him be peace, he did not pray before it or after it, meaning the Eid prayer."],[1732,"upon him be peace, he said takbir in Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha seven and five times, besides the two takbirs of ruku, in the wording of Abu al-Tahir."],[1737,"He used to say the takbir in the two Eid prayers: seven takbirs in the first and five in the last."],[1740,"ﷺ used to recite aloud in the obligatory prayers: Bismillāhir-Raḥmānir-Raḥīm, al-Fātiḥah 1; and he used to perform the qunūt in the Fajr prayer; and he used to say the takbir on the Day of ʿArafah from the Fajr prayer, and stop it after the ʿAṣr prayer on the last of the Days of Tashrīq."],[1742,"ﷺ said the takbir on the Day of ʿArafah and stopped on the last of the Days of Tashrīq."],[1745,"The takbir during the Days of Tashrīq is after the Ẓuhr prayer from the Day of Sacrifice, and it ends with the morning prayer on the last of the Days of Tashrīq."],[1746,"From his father."],[1747,"He said: And Abū Marwān ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Farwah narrated to us, from Isḥāq b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Farwah, from Abū Salamah al-Ḥaḍramī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī."],[1748,"From Ibn ʿUmar that they used to say the takbir in the Ẓuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the Ẓuhr prayer of the last of the Days of Tashrīq; they would say the takbir in the morning prayer but not in the Ẓuhr prayer."],[1749,"He said: ʿUthmān, while he was besieged, led us in saying the takbir in the Ẓuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until he prayed the Ẓuhr prayer of the last of the Days of Tashrīq; he said the takbir in the morning prayer and did not say it in the Ẓuhr prayer."],[1750,"ʿUmar and ʿUthmān used to pray the Ẓuhr prayer on the Day of Departure at al-Muḥaṣṣab and they did not say the takbir."],[1751,"He heard him saying the takbir in the prayers during the Days of Tashrīq: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar, three times."],[1761,"There is nothing between a servant and disbelief except abandoning the prayer."],[1769,"ﷺ the like of it exactly."],[1773,"Pray over every deceased person from the people of the qiblah."],[1778,"From al-Zuhri with his chain, similar to it."],[1779,"Al-Zubaydi narrated to us with his chain, similar to it."],[1784,"Peace be upon him, similar to it. Authentic."],[1793,"From al-Zuhri, exactly the same as it."],[1796,"Peace be upon him recited a long recitation, reciting aloud—meaning in the eclipse prayer. Ibn Abi Dawud said: This is a Sunnah in which the people of Madinah alone recited aloud."],[1801,"He said: Our Mahdi will have two signs that have not occurred since Allah created the heavens and the earth: the moon will be eclipsed on the first night of Ramadan, and the sun will be eclipsed in the middle of it, and they have not occurred since Allah created the heavens and the earth."],[1811,"Peace be upon him, similar to it."],[1816,"Sufyan narrated to us the same as it. Chapter: The Muslim is not impure."],[1818,"He said: Jibril ﷺ prayed over Adam ﷺ , saying the takbir over him four times. Jibril led the angels in prayer that day. He was buried in the mosque of al-Khayf, taken from the direction of the qiblah, a lahd was made for him, and his grave was raised. Abd al-Rahman b. Malik b. Mighwal is abandoned. Abu Ismail al-Mu'addib narrated it from Ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hazrah, from Urwah, as his statement, part of this speech."],[1820,"From Ubayy with this, as a mawquf report."],[1821,"Al-Qasim b. Ismail, Uthman b. Ahmad al-Daqqaq, and others narrated to us. They said: Abd Allah b. Rawh narrated to us. Shababah narrated to us. Kharijah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy b. Ka'b, from the Prophet ﷺ, with this."],[1825,"Ibn Abbas prayed over a funeral and recited the Opening of the Book (Surat al-Fatihah). I said to him, and he said, \"It is from the Sunnah\" or \"from the completion of the Sunnah.\""],[1826,"We used to wash the deceased, and among us were those who performed the ritual bath and among us those who did not."],[1827,"I prayed behind Zayd b. Arqam over a funeral, and he said the takbir five times."],[1829,"He used to say the takbir over the people of Badr six times, over the Companions of Muhammad five times, and over the rest of the people four times."],[1832,"Sahl b. Hunayf led us in prayer over a funeral. When he said the first takbir, he recited the Mother of the Quran until those behind him could hear. He then continued his takbirs until one takbir remained, then he recited the tashahhud of the prayer, then said the takbir and departed."],[1834,"And he said in it: I washed you and shrouded you."],[1835,"And he said in it: I washed you. Chapter: Placing the right hand over the left and raising the hands at the takbir."],[1836,"He ﷺ prayed over a funeral and placed his right hand over his left hand."],[1839,"A Christian woman died with a Muslim child in her womb, so Umar ordered that she be buried with the Muslims because of her child."],[1846,"He ﷺ passed by a grave that had been recently dug, so he prayed over it and said the takbir four times. I said, \"Who narrated this to you?\" He said, \"A trustworthy person who witnessed it, Abdullah b. Abbas.\""],[1847,"He ﷺ prayed over an abandoned grave and said the takbir over it four times. Muslim b. Ibrahim also narrated it from Shu'bah, Abu Hudhayfah from Za'idah, and Abdullah b. Ja'far from Abu Mu'awiyah from al-Shaybani; Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad and Abdul Wahid b. Ziyad from al-Shaybani concurred with them, all saying he said the takbir four times."],[1852,"He ﷺ prayed over a deceased person three days after his death."],[1853,"He, ﷺ , prayed over a grave after a month. Bishr b. Adam was alone in narrating it, and others differed from him on the authority of Abu Asim."],[1856,"He, ﷺ , said: 'Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them something that preoccupy them, or a matter that preoccupies them.'"],[1857,"Fatimah bequeathed that her husband Ali and Asma should wash her, so they washed her."],[1858,"Ibn Umar prayed over seven funerals, men and women. He placed the men nearest to him and the women nearest to the qiblah, and arranged them in a single row. And he said: He placed the funeral of Umm Kulthum bt. Ali, the wife of Umar b. al-Khattab, and a son called Zayd b. Umar. The imam that day was Sa'id b. al-'As, and among the people that day were Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, Abu Sa'id, and Abu Qatadah. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'The Sunnah.' Chapter on the Duha prayer in congregation."],[1865,"Ammar b. Yasir lost consciousness during Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha, then regained consciousness at midnight and prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha."],[1867,"He lost consciousness for a day and a night and did not make them up."],[1868,"He lost consciousness for more than two days and did not make it up."],[1869,"Ibn Umar lost consciousness for three days and their nights and did not make them up. Chapter on turning during the prayer due to an excuse."],[1875,"He used to gesture during the prayer."],[1880,"He, ﷺ , prayed the morning prayer and recited sixty verses. Then he heard the voice of a child, so he bowed, then stood and recited two verses, then bowed."],[1884,"Whoever prays four rak'ahs after Isha, recites in them, and does their bowing and prostrating well, his reward will be like the reward of one who prayed them on the Night of Decree."],[1897,"Harithah narrated to us the like of it exactly."],[1899,"There is no zakat on wealth until a year passes over it."],[1900,"The same was narrated from Aisha."],[1901,"There is no zakat on wealth until a year passes over it in the sight of its Lord."],[1902,"When a man acquires wealth, zakat is not due on it until a year passes over it. Chapter on the obligation of zakat on gold, silver, livestock, fruits, and grains."],[1903,"He used to take from every twenty dinars half a dinar, and from forty dinars one dinar."],[1919,"There is no zakat on vegetables."],[1924,"Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Buhlul narrated to us: my grandfather narrated to us: my father narrated to me: al-Hasan b. 'Umarah narrated to us from al-Hakam, 'Amr b. 'Uthman, and 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, from Musa b. Talhah, from Mu'adh b. Jabal, the like of it."],[1925,"Abu Talib Ahmad b. Nasr al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad b. Nasr b. Hammad narrated to us: my father narrated to us from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Musa b. Talhah, from Mu'adh, from the Prophet ﷺ, with this."],[1927,"From Mu'adh b. Jabal, the like of it."],[1937,"He said: Mu'adh b. Jabal said to the people of Yemen, \"Bring me khums or worn garments; I will take from you for the zakat, for it is easier on you and better for the emigrants in Madinah.\" 'Amr said, \"Bring me a display of clothes.\" This is mursal; Tawus did not meet Mu'adh."],[1938,"The cucumbers were not included in what Mu'adh brought; he only took zakat from wheat, barley, dates, and raisins, and there is nothing on cucumbers. We used to have a cucumber field that produced ten thousand, and there was nothing due on it."],[1943,"Ma'mar said: Halimah."],[1948,"There is no sadaqah on working oxen."],[1949,"Nothing of zakah is taken from oxen used for plowing."],[1952,"He said: Upon them is one sheep. And if one has thirty-nine and the other one sheep, he said: Upon the two of them is one sheep."],[1953,"A man came to al-Hasan with a page containing questions he was asking him about, and he did not stammer in any of them until he came to forty sheep between two people, and he said: In them is one sheep upon both of them."],[1960,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any right in wealth other than zakah? He said: Yes. Then he recited: “And gives wealth, in spite of love for it.”"],[1962,"There is no zakah on jewelry."],[1963,"There is no harm in wearing jewelry when its zakah has been given."],[1964,"He used to write to his treasurer Salim to take out the zakah of his daughters’ jewelry every year."],[1966,"The wife of Ibn Mas‘ud asked about jewelry of hers. He said: If it reaches two hundred, then zakah is due on it. She said: In my care are the sons of a brother of mine; should I place it among them? He said: Yes."],[1970,"The wife of Ibn Mas‘ud asked him about a necklace of hers containing twenty mithqals of gold, and she said: Should I pay zakah on it? He said: Yes. She said: How much? He said: Five dirhams. She said: Should I give it to so-and-so, the son of her brother, an orphan in her care? He said: Yes, if you wish."],[1971,"The wife of Ibn Mas‘ud had jewelry, and she said to Ibn Mas‘ud: Should I give its zakah? He said: Yes. She said: Should I give it to my brother’s son, an orphan? He said: Yes."],[1972,"I asked Anas b. Malik about jewelry, and he said: There is no zakah on it."],[1973,"A woman from the daughters of Abdullah b. Umar would be given a dowry of a thousand dinars, and she would have jewelry made for her from that worth four hundred dinars, and no zakah was considered due on it."],[1974,"There is no zakah on jewelry."],[1975,"Ibn Umar used to adorn his daughters with jewelry worth four hundred dinars and would not pay zakah on it."],[1976,"She used to adorn her daughters with gold and not pay zakah on it, about fifty thousand. Chapter: The Obligation of Zakah on the Wealth of a Minor and an Orphan"],[1981,"Their wealth was with Ali. When he returned it to them, they found it had decreased, so they calculated it along with the zakah and found it complete. They came to Ali and he said, \"Did you think I had wealth that I did not pay zakah on?\""],[1983,"Ibn Umar had the wealth of an orphan and he would borrow from it, and sometimes he would guarantee it, and he would pay zakah on the orphan's wealth when he was its guardian."],[1985,"Ibn Umar would pay zakah on the orphan's wealth, borrow from it, and give it out as a speculative partnership (mudarabah)."],[1988,"Zakah is not obligatory on the wealth of a minor until prayer becomes obligatory upon him."],[1998,"Al-Husayn b. Yahya b. Ayyash narrated to us: Ali b. Muslim narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Qays and Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Husayn with this, the like of it."],[1999,"Upon him, peace, the like of it, except that he said, \"and for one possessing strength, powerful.\""],[2005,"From Zayd b. Aslam, similar to it with its chain. Chapter: The Rich Person Who Is Forbidden to Beg"],[2010,"Fifty dirhams. The shaykh said: The first is a mistake; his saying \"from Abu Ishaq\" is actually Hakim b. Jubayr, who is weak, abandoned by Shu'bah and others."],[2012,"Charity is not lawful for one who has fifty dirhams or their equivalent in gold."],[2024,"upon him be peace, the like of it."],[2025,"I used to sell leather and quivers. Umar b. al-Khattab passed by me and said, 'Pay the zakah on your wealth.' I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, it is only in leather.' He said, 'Estimate its value, then pay its zakah.'"],[2034,"upon him be peace, the like of it."],[2042,"He says: al-baʿl is that whose roots reach the water."],[2043,"On what the sky, rivers, and springs water, a tenth; and on what is watered by a camel-drawn bucket, half a tenth."],[2047,"Sa'id b. Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us with his chain the like of it."],[2053,"upon him be peace, commanded the estimation of grapes as date palms are estimated, so its zakah is taken as raisins, just as the sadaqah of date palms is taken as dates. Muhammad b. Salih al-Tammar and the nephew of al-Zuhri followed them. Al-Waqidi narrated it from Abd al-Rahman b. Abd al-Aziz, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, from al-Miswar b. Makhramah, from Attab b. Usayd."],[2056,"He used to send someone to the people to estimate their vines and fruits."],[2059,"upon him be peace, commanded that grapes be estimated as raisins, just as dates are estimated."],[2061,"I was informed from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from A'ishah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2064,"from this hadith."],[2065,"Feed the hungry, give drink to the thirsty, enjoin what is right, and forbid what is wrong."],[2070,"He said: Zakah is not to be taken out of a land except to a relative. [This is] mawquf."],[2073,"People from the people of Syria came with horses and slaves, and they said to Umar b. al-Khattab, \"Take its sadaqah.\" He said, \"I do not know anyone who did that before me, until I ask.\""],[2074,"What Allah has made lawful in His Book is lawful, and what He has made unlawful is unlawful, and what He has been silent about is an exemption. So accept from Allah His exemption, for Allah is never forgetful. Then he recited this verse: 'And your Lord is never forgetful.'"],[2078,"Muhammad b. Ismail al-Farisi narrated to us, Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah and Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, exactly like the hadith of Ibn Zanjawayh. Likewise, Said b. Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated it from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, and he said in it: 'from the Muslims.' Likewise, Malik b. Anas, al-Dahhak b. Uthman, Umar b. Nafi, al-Mualla b. Ismail, Abd Allah b. Umar al-Umari, Kathir b. Farqad, and Yunus b. Yazid narrated it. And it was narrated from Ibn Shawdhab, from Ayyub, from Nafi, likewise."],[2085,"Upon him ﷺ, he obligated zakat al-fitr upon the young and the old, the male and the female, among those whom you support."],[2087,"He used to give sadaqat al-fitr on behalf of all his family, their young and their old, on behalf of those he supported, and on behalf of his slaves and the slaves of his wives."],[2088,"Upon him ﷺ, he sent a caller to announce in the mountain passes of Makkah: 'Indeed, zakat al-fitr is obligatory upon every Muslim, upon every male and female, free and slave, young and old: two mudds of wheat or a sa' of other food.'"],[2089,"Upon him ﷺ, he sent a crier to shout in the heart of Makkah: 'Indeed, sadaqat al-fitr is like it.' And he added in it: 'a present (resident) or a nomad.'"],[2093,"He said: Ata said: 'Two mudds of wheat, or a sa' of dates or barley; the free and the slave are equal in it.'"],[2098,"Upon him ﷺ, he urged sadaqat Ramadan upon every person: a sa' of dates, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of wheat. Bakr b. al-Aswad is not strong."],[2099,"We were commanded to give sadaqat Ramadan on behalf of the young and the old, the free and the slave: a sa' of food. Whoever gives wheat, it is accepted from him; whoever gives barley, it is accepted from him; whoever gives raisins, it is accepted from him; whoever gives sult (a kind of barley), it is accepted from him. He said: And I think he said: 'Whoever gives flour, it is accepted from him; and whoever gives sawiq (parched barley), it is accepted from him.'"],[2106,"a sa' of food"],[2110,"Muhammad b. Bakr narrated to us something similar with his chain of narration"],[2114,"And he said, \"As for the poor person, Allah will enrich him\""],[2118,"Zakat al-Fitr is due upon the rich and the poor"],[2120,"that he heard Ali b. Abi Talib commanding Zakat al-Fitr, saying, \"It is a sa' of dates, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of wheat, or of sult, or of raisins\""],[2122,"and that is what is correct"],[2123,"regarding Sadaqat al-Fitr: two mudds of wheat, or a sa' of barley, or dates, or raisins. Whoever does not have aqit but has milk, then two sa's of milk"],[2128,"that he used to give Sadaqat al-Fitr on behalf of every free person and slave, young and old, male and female, disbeliever and Muslim, to the extent that he would give it on behalf of his mukatab slaves. Uthman is al-Waqqasi, abandoned."],[2129,"A man feeds on behalf of his slave, even if he is a Magian"],[2130,"He said, \"If you were to give hulaylij for Sadaqat al-Fitr, it would suffice\""],[2133,"Sadaqat al-Fitr is due upon every Muslim, young and old, slave or free: two mudds of wheat, or a sa' of dates or barley"],[2134,"He said, \"Two mudds of wheat, or a sa' of dates and barley\""],[2135,"upon whomever you are responsible for supporting: half a sa' of wheat or a sa' of dates"],[2136,"he paid to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq half a sa' of wheat"],[2137,"that a sa' of wheat was paid to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq on behalf of two men"],[2144,"it is part of the Sunnah that he should not go out until he eats and gives the zakat al-fitr"],[2155,"they both said: Marwan b. Muhammad narrated to us with this"],[2163,"upon him be peace, something similar"],[2165,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have seen the crescent. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. So he announced to the people that they should fast. Shu'bah also narrated it from al-Thawri as mursal."],[2170,"Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us, Asbat b. Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad b. Amr narrated to us with this, then break your fast, and this too"],[2171,"upon him be peace, the like of it. These are sound chains of transmission."],[2179,"from Sufyan al-Thawri with his chain, something similar, and this is like it"],[2187,"fast at its sighting, then he mentioned the like of it to its end, and he did not mention 'the month is twenty-nine.' Rawh b. al-Qasim is among the trustworthy narrators."],[2189,"the fast is the day you all fast, the breaking of the fast is the day you all break the fast, and the sacrifice is the day you all sacrifice"],[2194,"He said: I was in the care of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. One night he prayed as long as Allah willed, then he said: “Go out and see whether dawn has risen.” He said: I went out, then returned and said: “White light has risen in the sky.” He prayed as long as Allah willed, then he said: “Go out and see whether dawn has risen.” I went out, then returned and said: “Redness has spread across the sky.” He said: “Now, bring me my pre-dawn meal.”"],[2195,"I said: “Redness has spread across the sky and turned red.” He said: “Now bring me my drink.” He said: And on another day he said: “Stand at the door between me and the dawn.”"],[2203,"That Umar accepted the testimony of a single man for sighting the crescent moon for breaking the fast or for the sacrificial feast."],[2204,"Umar's letter came to us while we were at Khanqin. In his letter he said: “The crescents are some larger than others. If you see the crescent during the day, do not break your fast until two witnesses testify.”"],[2205,"Umar's letter came to us at Khanqin: “The crescents are some greater than others. If you see the crescent from the beginning of the day, do not break your fast until two witnesses testify that they saw it yesterday.”"],[2206,"I was with Umar when a rider came to him and claimed that he had seen the crescent. So he ordered the people to break their fast."],[2207,"Umar's letter came to us while we were at Khanqin: “The crescents are some greater than others. If you see the crescent at the beginning of the day, do not break your fast until two upright men testify that they sighted it yesterday evening.”"],[2208,"He said: Umar's letter came to us while we were at Khanqin: “The crescents are some larger than others. If you see the crescent during the day, do not break your fast until evening, unless two Muslim men testify that they sighted it yesterday evening.”"],[2209,"Sufyan narrated to us with his chain, the like of the hadith of Abd al-Rahman."],[2214,"Whoever sees the crescent of Ramadan alone should fast, and whoever sees the crescent of Shawwal alone should break his fast, and should conceal that."],[2215,"Malik said concerning the one who sees the crescent of Ramadan alone: he should fast, because it is not proper for him to break his fast while he knows that that day is from the month of Ramadan. And whoever sees the crescent of Shawwal alone should not break his fast, because people are suspected: some of them may break their fast who are not trustworthy, and then they say, when it becomes known to them: we had seen the crescent."],[2223,"For one who has not made the intention at night."],[2225,"There is no fast for one who does not resolve to fast before dawn."],[2228,"He saw the new moon of Shawwal during the day, and Ibn Umar said, \"It is not permissible for you to break your fast until you see the new moon from where it is seen.\""],[2229,"I asked al-Zuhri about the new moon of Shawwal when it is seen early in the day. He said, \"I heard Sa'id b. al-Musayyib say: If the new moon of Shawwal is seen after dawn until the afternoon or until the sun sets, it is from the coming night.\""],[2231,"Upon him be peace, a drink was brought to him on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and he drank, then he handed it to me and I drank. Then I said, 'O Prophet of God, I was fasting.' He said to her, 'Were you making up anything for yourself?' She said, 'No.' He said, 'Then it does not harm you.' There is disagreement from Simak."],[2233,"Shu'bah said, \"Simak used to say: The two sons of Umm Hani' narrated to us, and I narrated it from the better of them.\" Abu Dawud connected its chain from Shu'bah."],[2237,"The voluntary faster is the trustee or commander of himself: if he wishes, he fasts; and if he wishes, he breaks his fast."],[2238,"He did not see any harm in the voluntary faster breaking his fast."],[2239,"Upon him be peace, he would enter the morning from the night intending to fast, and he would say to us, 'Do you have anything? Has anything come to you?' She said, 'We would say: Have you not entered the morning fasting?' He would say, 'Yes, but there is no harm in my breaking my fast as long as it is not a vow or making up Ramadan.' Muhammad b. Ubayd Allah is al-Arzami, weak in hadith."],[2242,"When a man fasts voluntarily, he may break his fast whenever he wishes."],[2253,"Upon him be peace, the like of it. Ammar is weak."],[2258,"And Yahya b. Hamzah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir and al-Qa'qa' b. Hakim from Ata' b. Yasar from Abu Hurayrah the like of that. And al-Hakam b. Abdullah is Ibn Sa'd al-Ayli, weak in hadith."],[2260,"Whoever eats or drinks out of forgetfulness should not break his fast, for it is only provision that God has provided him."],[2269,"Concession was given for the fasting person regarding cupping."],[2271,"Concession was given for the fasting person regarding cupping and kissing."],[2275,"He ﷺ had cupping done while fasting after he said, \"The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.\""],[2279,"From Isra'il with his chain, the like of it. This is not established, and Abu Yazid al-Dabbi is not well-known."],[2282,"From 'Isa b. Yunus with this."],[2283,"He ﷺ said: \"If the fasting person is overcome by vomiting, he does not have to break his fast or make it up, but if he vomits intentionally, he must make it up.\" 'Abd Allah b. Sa'id is not strong."],[2289,"No concession was given for fasting these days except for one who could not find the sacrificial animal."],[2290,"Shu'ba narrated to me something similar. This chain is sound."],[2292,"No concession was given for fasting the days of tashriq except for a mutamatti' who could not find the sacrificial animal."],[2296,"He ﷺ something similar."],[2299,"I went to Anas b. Malik in Ramadan when he wanted to travel. His mount had been prepared and he had put on his travel clothes, and the sun was close to setting. He called for food and ate some of it, then mounted. I said to him, \"Is this a sunnah?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[2300,"\"Have I not been informed that when you go out, you go out fasting, and when you enter, you enter fasting? So when you go out, go out not fasting, and when you enter, enter not fasting.\""],[2303,"He said: I entered upon A'ishah while a man was with her. He said, \"O our mother, what obligates ghusl?\" She said, \"When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory.\""],[2304,"My father used to send me to A'ishah so I could ask her. When it was the year I had a wet dream, I came to her and entered. She said, \"O you little mischievous one, you did it,\" and she dropped the screen between me and her."],[2314,"ﷺ commanded the one who broke his fast one day of Ramadan to offer the expiation for zihar."],[2323,"She said: \"'A number of other days' (al-Baqarah 184) was revealed with 'consecutive' (mutatabi'at), then 'consecutive' was dropped. This is a sound chain, and the one after it also.\""],[2324,"He said: A'ishah said, \"'A number of other days' (al-Baqarah 184) was revealed with 'consecutive' (mutatabi'at), then 'consecutive' was dropped.\" It was dropped; no one said it except Urwah."],[2326,"He said: \"Allah has not given you a concession to break its fast, and He does not want to make it difficult for you in making it up. So count the number and do as you wish.\""],[2327,"He was asked about making up Ramadan separately, and he said: \"Count the number and fast however you wish.\""],[2328,"Regarding making up Ramadan: \"Fast it however you wish.\" Ibn Umar said: \"Fast it in the same manner as you broke it.\""],[2329,"There is no harm in making up Ramadan separately."],[2330,"\"Count the number and fast however you wish.\""],[2331,"Abu Hurayrah saw no harm in making up Ramadan consecutively."],[2332,"He saw no harm in making up Ramadan intermittently."],[2333,"Separate it when you have counted it."],[2334,"He was asked about making up Ramadan, so he said: 'Count the number and fast however you wish.'"],[2335,"Separate the making up of Ramadan and count the number."],[2336,"He said: Mu'adh b. Jabal said: 'Count the number and do as you wish.'"],[2338,"upon him ﷺ the like of it."],[2339,"Separate the making up of Ramadan. Indeed Allah said: 'a number of other days.'"],[2344,"upon him ﷺ the like of it."],[2346,"He said: 'The debt owed to Allah is more deserving.'"],[2348,"Sa'id b. Yazid asked — 'Anbasah said, and he is the brother of Yunus b. Yazid — Nafi', the freed slave of Ibn 'Umar about a man who fell ill and his illness lasted long until two or three Ramadans passed by him. Nafi' said: 'Ibn 'Umar used to say: Whoever is overtaken by Ramadan and had not fasted the previous Ramadan, let him feed in place of each day a poor person a mudd of wheat, then there is no making up upon him.'"],[2349,"Whoever is overtaken by Ramadan while owing something from Ramadan, let him feed in place of each day a poor person a mudd of wheat."],[2350,"About a man who fell ill in Ramadan, then recovered but did not fast until another Ramadan overtook him. He said: 'He fasts the one that overtook him and feeds for the first, for each day a mudd of wheat for each poor person. Then when he finishes this one, he fasts the one in which he was negligent.' [A sound chain of narration, stopped at the Companion.]"],[2351,"About one who was negligent in making up Ramadan until another Ramadan overtook him. He said: 'He fasts this one with the people and fasts the one in which he was negligent, and feeds for each day a poor person.'"],[2353,"He says regarding a man who falls ill in Ramadan and does not fast until he recovers, or does not fast until another Ramadan overtakes him: He fasts the one that has come upon him, fasts the other, and feeds a poor person for each night. A sound isnad."],[2354,"Whoever has been negligent in fasting the month of Ramadan until another Ramadan overtakes him, let him fast this one that has overtaken him, then let him fast what he missed, and feed a poor person for each day."],[2355,"If he does not recover between the two Ramadans, he fasts for this one and feeds for the past one, and there is no making up for it upon him. If he recovers and does not fast until another Ramadan overtakes him, he fasts this one and feeds for the past one, and when he breaks his fast, he makes it up."],[2365,"The person in i'tikaf attends the Friday prayer, follows the funeral procession, and visits the sick."],[2366,"The person in i'tikaf visits the sick, attends the funeral procession, comes to the Friday prayer, and comes to his family but does not sit with them."],[2369,"He used to observe i'tikaf in the last ten days of Ramadan, and he continued doing that until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took his soul."],[2373,"I asked 'Asim al-Ahwal: Does the fasting person use siwak? He said: Yes. I said: With a fresh siwak or a dry one? He said: Yes. I said: At the beginning of the day or at its end? He said: Yes. I said: From whom? He said: From Anas b. Malik, from the Prophet."],[2376,"From 'Asim b. 'Ubayd Allah with his isnad, something similar."],[2379,"When you fast, use siwak in the morning, but do not use siwak in the evening, for there is no fasting person whose lips become dry in the evening except that it will be light between his eyes on the Day of Resurrection."],[2380,"Upon him be peace, something similar. Kaysan Abu 'Umar is not strong, and those between him and 'Ali are unknown. Chapter on breaking the fast in Ramadan due to old age, breastfeeding, excuse, or other than that."],[2381,"When an elderly man is unable to fast, he feeds for each day one mudd, one mudd."],[2383,"They both said: Abu Usamah narrated to us with this."],[2384,"that he cannot bear it—a sound and established chain"],[2385,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: “And upon those who can bear it, a ransom of feeding a poor person” [al-Baqarah 184]. He said: They can bear it, meaning they are burdened with it. A ransom of feeding one poor person. “Then whoever volunteers good” [al-Baqarah 184]—so he adds another poor person. It is not abrogated; “that is better for him. And that you fast is better for you” [al-Baqarah 184]. No concession is given in this except for the elderly who cannot bear fasting, or a sick person who knows he will not recover. And this chain is sound."],[2386,"“And that you fast is better for you” [al-Baqarah 184]. No concession is given except for the elderly who cannot bear fasting, or a sick person who knows he will not recover. And this is a sound chain."],[2387,"Concession was given to the very old man to break the fast and feed a poor person for each day, with no makeup due upon him."],[2388,"that the two should fast or feed a poor person for each day instead. And this is sound."],[2389,"that Ibn Abbas said to a slave woman of his who was pregnant or nursing: You are among those who cannot bear fasting. Upon you is the compensation, and there is no makeup upon you."],[2390,"The one afflicted with tuberculosis who has despaired of recovery and cannot bear fasting may break the fast and feed a poor person for each day."],[2391,"that he had a slave woman who was nursing; she suffered a miscarriage, so Ibn Abbas commanded her to break the fast—meaning and to feed—and not to make up."],[2392,"The pregnant and the nursing woman may break the fast and not make up."],[2393,"He says: It is the very old man who cannot bear fasting, so he breaks the fast and feeds a poor person for each day half a saa of wheat."],[2394,"that he used to recite: “And upon those who can bear it” [al-Baqarah 184], and he would say: It has not been abrogated."],[2395,"that his wife asked him while she was pregnant, so he said: Break the fast and feed a poor person for each day, and do not make up."],[2396,"A daughter of Ibn Umar was married to a man from Quraysh, and she was pregnant. She suffered from thirst in Ramadan, so Ibn Umar ordered her to break her fast and feed a poor person for each day."],[2397,"He became weak and unable to fast one year, so he prepared a large bowl of tharid and invited thirty poor people and fed them until they were full."],[2398,"That they feed a poor person in place of each day. Hisham said in his hadith: So he fed thirty poor people."],[2399,"For the month of Ramadan, a person may ransom it by feeding a poor person for each day on his behalf, so feed two poor people on my behalf."],[2400,"Whoever reaches old age and is unable to fast Ramadan, then for each day he must give a mudd of wheat."],[2408,"From Abu Salamah."],[2412,"Whoever breaks his fast one day in Ramadan must fast twelve days, because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, accepted from His servants one month out of twelve months."],[2416,"He prohibited fasting on five days of the year: the day of Fitr, the day of sacrifice, and the three days of Tashriq."],[2418,"He said: Do not buy milk while it is still in the udders, nor wool while it is still on the backs of the animals."],[2420,"He said: When this verse was revealed: \"And [due] to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House—for whoever is able to find a way\" (Al Imran 97), a man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the way? He said: Provision and a mount."],[2422,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what makes Hajj obligatory? He said: Provision and a mount."],[2423,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the way? He said: Provision and a mount."],[2424,"From ʿAlqamah."],[2430,"ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar came to us and told us that a man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the means (al-sabīl) to Hajj?\" He said: \"Provision and a mount.\""],[2432,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year?\" He said: \"No, rather once.\" It was said: \"Then what is the means to it?\" He said: \"Provision and a mount.\""],[2433,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the means to it?\" He said: \"Provision and a mount.\""],[2434,"The means is provision and a mount."],[2436,"He ﷺ passed by Ḍubāʿah while she was ill and said: \"Do you intend to perform Hajj?\" She said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj and stipulate a condition, and say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[2440,"It is part of the Sunnah to perform ghusl when one intends to enter ihram and when one intends to enter Makkah."],[2442,"ʿUthmān b. al-Yamān, Abū Bakr b. Abī Shaybah and Ibrāhīm b. al-Mundhir narrated to us; they said: Abū Ghaziyyah narrated to us with his chain of transmission the like of it."],[2447,"He ﷺ said: \"Where have you alighted?\" He said: \"At so-and-so's.\" He said: \"Has she closed her door upon you? A woman must not perform Hajj unless she has a maḥram with her.\""],[2454,"He said: \"Al-Fiṭr is the day when the people break their fast, and al-Aḍḥā is the day when the people offer sacrifice.\""],[2459,"The months of Hajj are Shawwāl, Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijjah."],[2460,"The months of Hajj are Shawwāl, Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijjah."],[2461,"The months of Hajj are Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."],[2462,"I asked Ibn Umar about the months of Hajj, and he said: Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."],[2463,"He said: Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah."],[2464,"From Ibn Abbas, the like of it."],[2465,"From Ibn Abbas, the like of it exactly."],[2467,"From Ibn Umar regarding His, Mighty and Majestic, saying: \"And whoever undertakes the Hajj in them\" (al-Baqarah 197), he said: He entered into ihram."],[2468,"The obligation of Hajj is ihram."],[2469,"The obligation of Hajj is ihram."],[2472,"From Amr, the like of it."],[2475,"Upon him, peace, the like of it."],[2484,"Upon him, peace, the like of it."],[2487,"The muhrim may smell sweet basil, enter the bathhouse, extract his tooth, lance an abscess, and if his nail breaks, remove the harm from it."],[2488,"There is no harm in the money belt and the ring for the pilgrim in ihram."],[2489,"Concession was granted to the pilgrim in ihram regarding the ring and the money belt."],[2490,"There is no harm in the ring for the pilgrim in ihram."],[2491,"From Ataʾ something similar, and he did not mention Ibn Abbas."],[2493,"Indeed, part of the Sunnah of Hajj is that one should not enter ihram for Hajj except in the months of Hajj."],[2494,"From Ibn Abbas regarding a man who entered ihram for Hajj outside the months of Hajj: he said, \"That is not from the Sunnah.\""],[2495,"I said, \"Should I enter ihram for Hajj before the months of Hajj?\" He said, \"No.\""],[2496,"Allah, the Exalted, said: \"Hajj is [during] well-known months\" [al-Baqarah 197], so that Hajj should not be undertaken outside them."],[2501,"Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Tawus and Ikrimah informed him from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[2502,"Abu al-Zubayr informed me with his chain of narration something similar."],[2505,"ﷺ something similar."],[2508,"ﷺ fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah as Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Yemen as Yalamlam, for the people of Sham and Egypt as al-Juhfah, and for the people of Iraq as Dhat Irq."],[2512,"ﷺ something similar to it."],[2515,"ﷺ performed Hajj ifrad. He said: And Abdul Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Alqamah b. Abi Alqamah, from his mother, from Aishah, something similar to it."],[2518,"I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr, and he performed ifrad; with Umar, and he performed ifrad; and with Uthman, and he performed ifrad."],[2524,"ﷺ something similar to it."],[2527,"By Allah, tamattu was only for us in particular, and for the one who is prevented."],[2528,"He said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is the cancellation of Hajj for us or for those after us?' He said, 'No, rather for us.'"],[2529,"He was asked about the tamattu of Hajj, and he said, 'By Allah, it is for us, the companions of Muhammad, in particular, and not for the rest of the people, except for the one who is prevented.'"],[2531,"That anyone should enter ihram declaring Hajj, then cancel his Hajj for an Umrah before the Hajj."],[2533,"Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us. H, and Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Sadan b. Nasr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Sa'd b. Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, from Aishah, that she drove two sacrificial camels, and they went astray. Ibn al-Zubayr sent her two camels in their place. He said, so she slaughtered them, then found the first two camels and slaughtered them, and said, 'This is the sunnah for sacrificial camels.'"],[2536,"ﷺ drove on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah seventy sacrificial camels on behalf of seven hundred men."],[2538,"From Ata, other than him."],[2541,"Whoever forgets something of his rites or leaves it, let him shed blood."],[2542,"From Ibn Abbas, something similar."],[2543,"Whoever omits any of his rites must shed blood (offer a sacrifice)."],[2545,"Expiation is only for intentional acts, and they were strict about unintentional ones merely to prevent them from happening again."],[2554,"It was ruled regarding a hyena that a ram is due."],[2555,"Regarding the pigeons of the sanctuary: for a pigeon, a sheep; for two eggs, a dirham; for an ostrich, a camel; for a cow, a cow; and for a wild donkey, a cow."],[2557,"May peace and blessings be upon him ruled regarding ostrich eggs that a pilgrim in the state of ihram destroys, according to their value."],[2558,"And he said, 'according to its value.'"],[2560,"May peace and blessings be upon him, something similar."],[2565,"Muhammad b. Ismail al-Farisi narrated to us; Abbas b. Ahmad b. al-Azhar narrated to us; Duhaym narrated to us; al-Walid narrated to us with his chain, something similar."],[2568,"May peace and blessings be upon him ruled regarding ostrich eggs that a pilgrim in the state of ihram breaks: fasting a day for each egg."],[2569,"Regarding ostrich eggs that a pilgrim in the state of ihram damages: their value is due."],[2570,"Regarding a group of people who killed a hyena: he said, 'A ram is due upon them, which they share among themselves.'"],[2571,"That the freedmen of Ibn al-Zubayr entered ihram when a hyena passed by them, and they threw their staffs at it and hit it. They felt uneasy about that, so they came to Ibn Umar and mentioned that to him. He said, \"You owe a ram.\" They said, \"Each one of us owes a ram?\" He said, \"Indeed you are being dealt with strictly; all of you together owe one ram.\" The philologists said: His saying \"you are being dealt with strictly\" means \"it is made hard for you then.\""],[2575,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Yunus b. Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik informed him from Ibn Shihab with its isnad, and he mentioned something similar."],[2585,"Al-Sari b. Yahya informed us: Qabisah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us exactly the same thing."],[2586,"Upon him be peace, when he drew near al-Safa, he recited, \"Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah\" [al-Baqarah:158], then he said, \"Begin with what Allah began with,\" so he began with al-Safa."],[2588,"Upon him be peace, when he entered Makkah, he touched the Black Stone and the Yamani Corner, and he did not touch any of the other corners."],[2595,"Regarding the bald-headed person: the razor passes over his head."],[2597,"And al-Saghani narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Yunus al-Hafari and Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah b. Umar narrated to us something similar, as a mauquf report."],[2621,"He said: And Sulayman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir something similar to that; and from Ata something similar to that; and from Abd al-Karim from Tawus and Mujahid something similar to that."],[2622,"Upon him be peace, he only performed one tawaf for his Hajj and his Umrah, and one sa'i, then he came to Makkah and did not perform sa'i between them after the ifadah."],[2623,"Upon him be peace, he combined the Umrah and the Hajj, and performed one tawaf for them."],[2624,"Upon him be peace and his companions performed one tawaf for his Hajj and his Umrah."],[2625,"Upon him be peace, he combined the Hajj and the Umrah, and performed one tawaf around the House for them, and one tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah."],[2631,"They both said: Qabisah narrated to us with his chain of transmission, something similar to it."],[2637,"He was performing qiran, so he performed two tawafs and two sa'ys."],[2641,"I met Ali while I had entered ihram for Hajj, and he had entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah. I said: 'Can I do as you have done?' He said: 'That is if you had started with Umrah.' I said: 'How should I do if I want that?' He said: 'Take a vessel of water and pour it over yourself, then enter ihram for both of them together, then perform two tawafs for them and two sa'ys for them, and no ihram becomes permissible for you before the Day of Sacrifice.'"],[2642,"I chose ifrad, and tamattu' is good; we do not dislike it."],[2645,"O Banu Abd Manaf, if you have any authority over the matter, then I would not recognize anyone preventing someone from praying at this House at any hour he wishes, night or day."],[2649,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah, so he sent for him and called him, and said: 'Have you ever performed Hajj?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.'"],[2650,"He said: 'Have you performed Hajj?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'This is on your behalf, and perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.'"],[2652,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Nubayshah, so he said: 'O you who are reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Nubayshah, this is on behalf of Nubayshah, and perform Hajj for yourself.' This is unique to al-Hasan ibn Umarah, who is abandoned in hadith; the preserved report from Ibn Abbas is the hadith of Shubrumah."],[2654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Nubayshah, so he said: 'O you who are reciting the talbiyah on behalf of Nubayshah, have you performed Hajj?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then this is on behalf of Nubayshah, and perform Hajj for yourself.'"],[2657,"From Amr ibn Dinar, exactly the same as it."],[2658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying: 'Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah.' So he said: 'Have you performed Hajj for yourself?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then for yourself, so recite the talbiyah.'"],[2659,"Abbas al-Tarqufi narrated to us; al-Firyabi narrated to us something similar to it."],[2662,"He ﷺ [heard] a man saying, “Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah.” He said, “Have you performed Hajj for yourself?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.”"],[2664,"From Ibn Abbas, similar to the hadith of Ibn Abi Layla."],[2666,"Make this one for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."],[2667,"Yahya b. Ma‘in said to me: I heard it from ‘Abdah as marfu‘."],[2668,"He ﷺ [heard] a man saying, “Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah,” and similar."],[2670,"He ﷺ [heard] a man saying the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah. He said, “Have you performed Hajj?” He said, “No.” He said, “Say the talbiyah for yourself, then say the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah.”"],[2671,"That he heard a man saying the talbiyah on behalf of Shubrumah."],[2672,"From Ibn Abbas, as mawquf, similar to the wording of Abu Yusuf."],[2675,"Regarding the woman in ihram who takes from her hair an amount like the forefinger."],[2676,"He used to say: It is from the Sunnah for a woman to rub her head with some henna on the evening of entering ihram, and to cover her head with a wash that has no perfume, and not to enter ihram unadorned."],[2678,"He used to give fatwas to women that they should cut the two khuffs, until Safiyyah said to him: Aishah used to order them not to cut. Mawquf."],[2679,"A man had intercourse with his wife before performing tawaf of the House on the Day of Sacrifice. He said: They should slaughter a camel between them, and they are not obligated to perform Hajj next year."],[2690,"He says the like of it."],[2696,"And from al-Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[2699,"I was sitting with Abdullah b. Umar, and he was asked about that – meaning the menstruating woman who departs. He said: She should stay until her last visit is to the House. Tawus said: I do not know whether Ibn Umar forgot it or did not hear what his companions heard. Then, a year or two after that, I witnessed him being asked about her, and he said: I have been informed that a concession was granted for them."],[2708,"Peace be upon him, something similar."],[2709,"Abd al-Jalil b. Humayd al-Yahsibi narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Sinan, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[2717,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this Umrah of ours for this year of ours or for all time? He said: No, rather for all time; Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."],[2724,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there jihad upon women? He said: Upon them is a jihad in which there is no fighting: Hajj and Umrah."],[2727,"Zayd b. Thabit was asked about Umrah before Hajj, and he said: They are two prayers; it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin."],[2728,"There is no one among God's creation but that Hajj and Umrah are obligatory upon him, if he is able to find a way to that. Whoever adds anything after them, it is good and voluntary. He said: And I did not hear him say anything about the people of Makkah."],[2729,"Umrah is obligatory like the obligation of Hajj, for whoever is able to find a way to it."],[2730,"He said: Umrah is obligatory like the obligation of Hajj, and it is the lesser Hajj."],[2731,"The greater Hajj is the Day of Sacrifice, and the lesser Hajj is Umrah."],[2732,"He ﷺ wrote to the people of Yemen a letter and sent it with Amr b. Hazm, in which [he said]: 'The 'umrah is the lesser Hajj, and none but the pure may touch the Qur'an.'"],[2735,"From al-Hajjaj with his chain, the like of it."],[2736,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is 'umrah obligatory, its obligation like the obligation of Hajj?' He said, 'No, but that you perform 'umrah is better for you.'"],[2739,"The one performing 'umrah does not stop the talbiyah until he begins the tawaf."],[2740,"Regarding the one who performs tamattu' with 'umrah to Hajj, he said: He circumambulates the House seven times and goes between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then on the Day of Sacrifice he circumambulates the House alone and does not go between al-Safa and al-Marwah."],[2747,"When Ibn Abbas drank from Zamzam he would say: 'O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, abundant provision, and healing from every disease.'"],[2751,"I saw Abu Sa'id, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn Umar, and Jabir b. Abdullah: when they touched the Stone, they kissed their hands. I said, 'And Ibn Abbas?' He said, 'And Ibn Abbas, I think, many times.'"],[2754,"He ﷺ the like of it."],[2755,"He ﷺ something similar."],[2756,"He ﷺ the like of it."],[2757,"He ﷺ something similar. Al-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Ibn Abi Yahya is more retentive than al-Darawardi, and along with Ibn Abi Yahya is Sulayman b. Bilal. Someone who heard Sulayman informed me from Amr something like the hadith of Ibn Abi Yahya."],[2759,"He performed 'umrah with Uthman in a group, and a bird was gifted to him. He ordered them to eat it but refused to eat it himself. Amr b. al-As said to him, 'Shall we eat from what you are not eating?' He said, 'I am not in this matter like you. It was only hunted for me and killed in my name.'"],[2761,"Upon him be peace, something similar, and he said: \"You are pilgrims.\""],[2762,"Upon him be peace, something similar."],[2764,"Upon him be peace, similar to the first hadith."],[2766,"None of you should say: \"Indeed I am a ṣarūrah.\""],[2775,"Women are not required to perform ramal around the House, nor between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah."],[2776,"A woman should not ascend above al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, nor raise her voice with the talbiyah."],[2777,"Women are not required to perform sa'y around the House, nor between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah."],[2779,"And do not cover his head."],[2781,"Regarding a muḥrim who dies, he said: \"Cover them and do not imitate the Jews.\""],[2784,"And Abū al-Zubayr informed me from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, similar to the hadith of ʿAmr, addressing me. Ibn Ṣāʿid said: \"Likewise al-Bursānī narrated it from Ibn Jurayj with both chains together.\""],[2786,"Abū al-Zubayr informed me from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, similar to the hadith of ʿAmr, addressing me."],[2793,"Regarding a muḥrim who clips his nails, he said: \"He feeds for each hand a ṣāʿ of food.\""],[2795,"He said: 'Whoever consumes the rent of the houses of Makkah consumes fire.'"],[2796,"The pebbles were only made to count the takbir with."],[2797,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, these are the Jamarat that are stoned every year, and we think that they decrease.' He said: 'Whatever is accepted from them is raised, and were it not for that, you would see them like mountains.'"],[2812,"From Ibrahim, the like of it exactly."],[2813,"If it is not as he described it to him, then it is binding upon him."],[2820,"Ibn Umar said: 'When we used to engage in a transaction, each one of us had the option as long as the two parties had not separated.' He said: 'So Uthman and I made a transaction, and I sold him my property in the valley for property of his in Khaybar.' He said: 'When I sold it to him, I began walking backwards, fearing that Uthman would cancel the sale with me before I parted from him.'"],[2830,"Do not sell it until you have taken possession of it."],[2837,"ﷺ the like of it."],[2839,"ﷺ something similar to it."],[2847,"Do not buy milk in the udders of animals, nor wool on their backs."],[2851,"He forbade the sale of uncertainty and the sale of pebbles."],[2853,"If I were to commit adultery thirty-three times, it would be dearer to me than to consume a dirham of usury, while Allah Almighty knows that I consumed it or took it, and it is usury."],[2855,"ﷺ sold a free man who became bankrupt."],[2859,"ﷺ with the like of it."],[2860,"ﷺ something similar."],[2861,"ﷺ something similar."],[2872,"Ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Muhammad b. 'Awf narrated to us; al-Mughirah narrated to us; Isma'il b. 'Ayyash narrated to us with his chain of narration, the like of it."],[2896,"Ishaq b. Muhammad al-Zayyat narrated to us; Yusuf b. Musa narrated to us; Hajjaj b. Minhal narrated to us; Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us with his chain of narration, something similar."],[2898,"ﷺ passed by him while he was detaining a debtor of his, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, a debtor of mine. So he said: Would you take half? and he gestured with his hand. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he took a share and left a share, or he said: half."],[2913,"And any man who dies while he has the property of another man with him in its essence, whether he collected something from him or did not collect, he is on equal footing with the creditors."],[2914,"Abu Bakr al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Rahman al-Asadi narrated to us; 'Amr b. 'Uthman narrated to us; al-Yaman b. 'Adi narrated to us from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. Al-Yaman b. 'Adi is weak in hadith."],[2920,"ﷺ commanded the reduction of losses due to natural disasters and prohibited the sale of years (of produce in advance)."],[2921,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab said concerning a man whose pledged item is lost while in the possession of the pledgee: If it was less than what was due on it, he returns to him the remainder of his right; and if it was more, then he is a trustee."],[2922,"ﷺ mentioned losses due to natural disasters with something. Sufyan said: I do not know how much that reduction was."],[2923,"A freed slave of Umm Habibah became bankrupt, so he was brought to Uthman b. Affan. Uthman ruled regarding him that whoever had collected any of his due before the bankruptcy, it is his; and whoever recognized his goods exactly, he has more right to them."],[2932,"Upon him be peace, something similar."],[2950,"Upon him be peace, he went out on a journey of his, and there was a crop swaying. He said, 'Whose crop is this?' They said, 'Rafiʿ b. Khadij's.' He sent for him—he had taken the land for half or a third—and said, 'Consider your expenditure on this land, take it from the owner of the land, and return his land and crop to him.'"],[2953,"He employed the people of Khaybar for half of what came out of fruit or crop."],[2962,"O Messenger of Allah, is it a guaranteed loan or an entrusted loan? He said, 'Rather an entrusted loan.'"],[2972,"He said, 'There is no liability upon the borrower unless he misappropriates, nor upon the custodian unless he misappropriates.'"],[2977,"Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ahmad b. Sinan narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us with this same report."],[2984,"From Ibrahim b. Ismail with his chain, exactly the same."],[2990,"When you have paid in advance, do not sell it until you take possession of it."],[2992,"Upon him be peace, when he ordered the expulsion of Banu al-Nadir from Madinah, some of them came to him and said, 'We have debts that are not yet due.' He said, 'Put down and hasten.'"],[2993,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Umar narrated to us, Muslim b. Khalid narrated to us with this."],[2997,"He forbade the stud fee of the stallion."],[3011,"From his father Shuʿayb, and Shuʿayb’s hearing from his grandfather ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr is sound."],[3012,"A man came to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr asking him about a pilgrim in ihram who had intercourse with a woman. He pointed to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar and said, “Go to that one and ask him.” Shuʿayb said: The man did not recognize him, so I went with him. He asked Ibn ʿUmar, who said, “Your Hajj is invalidated.” The man said, “Should I then stay put?” He said, “Rather, you go out with the people and do what they do. When the next year comes, perform Hajj and offer a sacrifice.” He returned to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr and informed him. Then he told him, “Go to Ibn ʿAbbas and ask him.” Shuʿayb said: I went with him, and he asked him, and he said to him the like of what ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar had said. He returned to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr and informed him of what Ibn ʿAbbas had said. Then he said, “What do you say?” He said, “I say the like of what they both said.”"],[3013,"He said: They say that ʿAmr b. Shuʿayb is more prolific, or something like this."],[3018,"Whatever the sale comprehends alive and gathered together belongs to the wealth of the buyer."],[3029,"The one who consumes the rent of the houses of Makkah only consumes fire into his belly."],[3030,"Those who consume the wages of the houses of Makkah."],[3042,"He said: It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, where will you stay tomorrow, if Allah wills?” That was at the time of the conquest. He said, “Has ʿAqil left us any inheritance?” Then he mentioned something similar."],[3043,"O Messenger of Allah, will you stay in your house in Makkah? He said, “Has ʿAqil left us any dwellings or houses?” ʿAqil and Talib inherited Abu Talib, while Jaʿfar and ʿAli did not inherit anything from him because they were Muslims, and ʿAqil and Talib were disbelievers."],[3044,"We are staying at the valley of Banu Kinanah where Quraysh swore together on disbelief."],[3048,"upon him be peace, something similar, and Shuʿbah differed with him."],[3068,"upon him be peace, he commanded him to equip an army. The camels ran out, so he commanded us to take one camel for two camels on credit from the camels of zakah."],[3071,"He forbade selling animals for animals on credit."],[3073,"He forbade selling a deferred payment for a deferred payment."],[3076,"He forbade the price of a cat."],[3084,"upon him be peace, the like of it, exactly."],[3085,"A settled person should not sell on behalf of a nomad; do not intercept merchandise before it reaches the market; do not engage in najash (bid driving); a man should not bid against his brother's bid; nor propose to a woman when his brother has proposed unless he marries or declines; a woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty her plate, for she will have only what is decreed for her; do not sell the milk-stored camel or sheep; whoever buys it has the option, if he wishes to return it and a sa' of dates; and the pledge is ridden and milked."],[3101,"He said: No."],[3102,"He says: Ibrahim b. Tahman was reliable in hadith."],[3104,"Al-A'mash said: I narrated it to Ibrahim, and he narrated to me from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, the like of it."],[3106,"Al-Aswad narrated it to me from A'ishah."],[3107,"Abd al-Rahman narrated both of these hadiths together: the hadith of Masruq from Abdullah and the hadith of Ibrahim from al-Aswad."],[3108,"The blood of a Muslim man from this ummah is not lawful except for one of three: a man who kills and is killed for it, a previously married adulterer, and one who abandons the community – or he said: one who departs from the community."],[3109,"From A'ishah, similar to it, mawquf (stopped at the companion)."],[3112,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Uqbah b. Amir al-Juhani said: If a punishment becomes doubtful to you, avert it as much as you can."],[3117,"He said: There was qisas (retaliation) among the Children of Israel, but there was no diyah (blood money) among them. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to this ummah: \"Qisas is prescribed for you in the case of the murdered\" (al-Baqarah 178) — the verse. \"But if any remission is made to anyone by his brother\" (al-Baqarah 178). He said: The pardon is that he accepts diyah in the case of deliberate killing. \"Then follow-up with propriety\" (al-Baqarah 178): the claimant should be followed up with propriety, and the defendant should pay to him with kindness. \"That is a concession from your Lord and a mercy\" (al-Baqarah 178) compared with what was prescribed upon those before you. 'Abd al-Razzaq said: And Ibn 'Uyaynah informed us with it, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[3119,"He used to say: We do not deem an escaped slave who steals to be subject to amputation."],[3120,"He used not to deem a slave subject to punishment (hadd), nor the people of the land — the Jew and the Christian — subject to punishment (hadd)."],[3126,"He said: And Baqiyyah informed us, from Abu Mu'adh, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, the like of it. Abu Mu'adh is Sulayman b. Arqam, who is matruk (abandoned)."],[3129,"And he said: That retaliation (mutilation) be inflicted on the offender."],[3131,"Upon him be peace, something similar."],[3133,"From Muhammad b. Talhah, the like of it."],[3138,"From Yahya — and all of them are trustworthy and exacting memorizers."],[3149,"Upon him be peace, the like of it, but Hamzah did not mention him. Ibn Sa'id said: Isma'il b. Muslim and Sulayman b. Kathir narrated it from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas."],[3154,"Whoever is killed in a blind dispute or a thrown missile — with a stone, a whip, or a stick — its blood money is the blood money of accidental killing. And whoever kills deliberately, it is retaliation. Whoever prevents that (retaliation), upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither an obligatory act nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him."],[3157,"He said: Whoever is killed in a blind dispute, thrown missile — with a stone, a stick, or a whip — for it there is a multiplied (heavier) diyah."],[3160,"Then indeed you, O tribe of Khuza'ah, have killed this slain man of Hudhayl, and I am paying his blood money. But whoever is killed henceforth, the heirs of the slain have a choice between two options: if they wish, they may kill; and if they wish, they may take the blood money."],[3164,"They both said: Al-Walid b. Muslim narrated to us, Al-Awza'i narrated to us with his chain of transmission something similar."],[3167,"That their statements differ in wording concerning the thing, but as for the meaning, it is one."],[3175,"Umar said to him: You have stoned her."],[3179,"Peace be upon him, something similar."],[3180,"When a thief steals, his right hand is cut off. If he returns, his left foot is cut off. If he returns, prison takes charge of him until he speaks well. I would be ashamed before Allah to leave him with no hand with which to eat and cleanse himself, and no foot on which to walk."],[3184,"Peace be upon him, when he conquered Makkah, said: There is no god but Allah alone. He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Surely every inherited boast that was counted or claimed is under these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the Kaaba and the watering of the pilgrims. Surely the one killed by mistake, resembling intentional killing — the one killed by whip and stick — bears a heavy blood money, of which forty are pregnant camels with their young in their bellies, meaning one hundred camels."],[3193,"Peace be upon him, similar to it."],[3199,"That Abdullah b. Sahl and Muhayyisa came to Khaybar."],[3202,"Muhammad b. Ismail al-Farisi narrated to us, Ahmad b. Sa'id al-Jammal narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sa'id b. Ubayd narrated to us with his chain of transmission something similar."],[3206,"From Amr, as a mursal report."],[3211,"Every prescribed punishment that is referred to me has become binding."],[3215,"Peace be upon him, similar to it."],[3217,"From Umar likewise."],[3219,"He killed a sorcerer who was with al-Walid b. Uqbah, then said: 'Do you commit sorcery while you see?' (Quran 3: al-Anbiya)."],[3226,"Regarding the woman who apostatizes, he said: She is to be compelled and not killed."],[3227,"The female apostate from Islam is to be imprisoned and not killed."],[3230,"Ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ubayd b. Utbah narrated to us, Ma'mar b. Bakkar narrated to us with his chain, likewise."],[3233,"Regarding the woman who disbelieves after her Islam, he said: She is asked to repent; if she repents, otherwise she is killed."],[3234,"Regarding the woman who apostatizes, he said: She is asked to repent; if she repents, otherwise she is killed."],[3235,"If she becomes Muslim; otherwise she is killed."],[3236,"Every apostate from Islam is to be killed if he does not return, whether male or female."],[3237,"When the prescribed punishment becomes doubtful to you, avert it as much as you can."],[3249,"Regarding the virgin found committing sodomy, he said: He is stoned."],[3253,"Ali said to him: 'Will you pray over her when she has committed adultery?'"],[3261,"He said: The blood money for a Jew or a Christian is four thousand, and for a Magian eight hundred."],[3262,"Umar used to set the blood money for a Jew or a Christian at four thousand, four thousand, and for a Magian at eight hundred."],[3267,"He said: Ali and Ibn Masud said: When a free man kills a slave intentionally, it is retaliation for him. This cannot be used as proof because it is mursal."],[3268,"It is part of the Sunnah that a believer is not killed for a disbeliever, and it is part of the Sunnah that a free man is not killed for a slave."],[3270,"From his grandfather, the same exactly."],[3274,"Upon him be peace, he exacted retaliation for a Muslim who killed a Jew. Al-Ramadi said: He exacted retaliation for a Muslim on behalf of a dhimmi. And he said: I am the most entitled of people to fulfill his protection."],[3276,"From Hajjaj, the same."],[3280,"He said: This verse was revealed concerning the muḥārib: \"The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger\" (al-Ma'idah 33). When he transgresses and cuts off the road, and kills and takes property, he is crucified. If he kills but does not take property, he is killed. If he takes property but does not kill, his hand and foot are cut off on opposite sides. If he flees and eludes them, then that is his banishment."],[3286,"That he ruled accordingly."],[3294,"From Amr b. Dinar with its chain, the same: A parent is not subjected to retaliation for a child."],[3299,"And from Ishaq b. Abdullah b. Abi Farwah, from Amr b. Shuaib, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, the same."],[3303,"A Muslim man killed a man from the people of the covenant intentionally, and the case was brought to Uthman. He did not execute him, but imposed a heavy blood money on him, like the blood money of a Muslim."],[3304,"He narrated it to me."],[3305,"He said: The blood money for a Jew and a Christian is four thousand, and for a Magian eight hundred."],[3306,"From Umar something similar."],[3308,"Whoever associates partners with Allah is not muhsan (protected from the hadd of adultery)."],[3312,"A Jewish man was killed treacherously, and Umar b. al-Khattab ruled for him twelve thousand dirhams."],[3313,"Regarding the blood money of every covenanted person, Magian or otherwise, the blood money is complete."],[3314,"The blood money of a covenanted person is like the blood money of a Muslim."],[3315,"ﷺ said: The injury caused by a dumb animal is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is one-fifth. The questioner said to him: O Abu Muhammad, is Abu Salamah with him? He said: If he was with him, then he is with him."],[3316,"ﷺ something similar."],[3320,"Because the trustworthy narrators whose hadiths we have presented contradicted him and did not mention that. Likewise Abu Salih al-Samman, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, Muhammad b. Sirin, Muhammad b. Ziyad, and others narrated it from Abu Hurayrah and did not mention in it 'the man is without liability,' and that is the preserved version from Abu Hurayrah."],[3322,"He says regarding the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq in the hadith of Abu Hurayrah: 'and the fire is without liability' is nothing; it was not in the books; it is false and not authentic."],[3323,"He says: The people of Yemen write 'al-nar' (fire) as 'al-nir' and write 'al-bir' meaning the same, and Abd al-Razzaq was merely prompted with 'the fire is without liability.'"],[3325,"The animal is without liability, the mine is without liability, the well is without liability, and the foot is without liability; and in buried treasure, one-fifth is due."],[3329,"A she-camel belonging to al-Bara' entered a walled garden."],[3332,"A she-camel belonging to them"],[3335,"Khalid b. al-Walid sent me to Umar. I came to him while Uthman b. Affan, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, Ali, Talhah, and al-Zubayr were with him, reclining in the mosque. I said, 'Khalid b. al-Walid sent me to you; he conveys his greetings to you and says: The people have become engrossed in wine and dispute about the punishment for it.' Umar said, 'These are here with you, so ask them.' Ali said, 'We think that when he drinks, he raves, and when he raves, he fabricates, and the fabricator is liable to eighty lashes.' Umar said, 'Convey to your companion what he said.' He said: So Khalid lashed eighty lashes, and Umar lashed eighty. He said: When a weak man who had been abased was brought to Umar, he lashed him forty. He said: And Uthman also lashed eighty and forty."],[3336,"Upon him be peace, the like of that"],[3337,"Upon him be peace, the like of that"],[3344,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi and others narrated to us; they said: Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Yahya b. Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[3346,"Upon him be peace, the like of it"],[3347,"Upon him be peace, with that"],[3349,"Muhammad b. Muslim b. Abdullah b. Shihab narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah b. Abdullah b. Utbah, from Zayd b. Khalid and Abu Hurayrah, the like of that."],[3350,"When the slave woman of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes clear, he should lash her the prescribed punishment and not rebuke her, until he said that three times. Then he said on the third or fourth time: Then he should sell her, even for a rope of hair."],[3351,"Even for a strand of hair"],[3354,"Four cases in which there is no li'an between them and their husbands: a Jewish woman under a Muslim man, a Christian woman under a Muslim man, a free woman under a slave, and a slave woman under a free man."],[3359,"That he was present when Umar b. al-Khattab was flogging a man from whom he detected the smell of wine."],[3360,"That he flogged a man from whom he detected the smell of wine with the full hadd punishment."],[3363,"And the Jew confessed."],[3369,"That Umar set the blood money for a Jew and a Christian at four thousand, and for a Magian at eight hundred."],[3370,"Umar used to set the blood money for a Jew and a Christian at four thousand, four thousand, and the blood money for a Magian at eight hundred."],[3375,"The blood money for accidental killing is in fifths: twenty jadha'ahs, twenty hiqqahs, twenty bint labuns, twenty male b. labuns, and twenty bint makhads."],[3376,"The blood money for accidental killing is five fifths: twenty hiqqahs, twenty jadha'ahs, twenty bint makhads, twenty bint labuns, and twenty male b. labuns."],[3377,"From Abdullah something similar."],[3384,"They both said regarding the blood money for accidental killing: thirty hiqqahs, thirty bint labuns, twenty bint makhads, and twenty male b. labuns. Umar b. Ahmad al-Marwazi narrated that to us; Sa'id b. Mas'ud narrated to us; al-Nadr narrated to us from Sa'id b. Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, and from Abd Rabbih, from Abu Iyad, that Uthman b. Affan and Zayd b. Thabit said that."],[3385,"That he said: The blood money for accidental killing is in quarters: twenty-five jadha'ahs, twenty-five hiqqahs, twenty-five bint labuns, and twenty-five bint makhads."],[3386,"From Ali that same."],[3387,"And from al-Hajjaj, from al-Sha‘bi and Ibrahim al-Nakha‘i, the like of it."],[3388,"He used to make the blood money for accidental killing in quarters: twenty-five hiqqahs, twenty-five jadha‘ahs, twenty-five bint labūns, and twenty-five bint makhāḍs."],[3390,"Intentional killing, the slave, the settlement, and the confession: the ‘āqilah does not pay for them."],[3391,"He said: The ‘āqilah does not pay for intentional killing, nor for a slave, nor for a settlement, nor for a confession."],[3394,"‘Abd al-Malik b. Ahmad al-Zayyāt narrated to us; Ḥafṣ b. ‘Amr narrated to us; ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Mahdī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[3396,"Upon him ﷺ, the like of it."],[3398,"Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Aḥmad b. Manṣūr narrated to us; Nu‘aym b. Ḥammād narrated to us; Muḥammad b. Yazīd al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; from Sufyān b. Ḥusayn with this chain, the like of it. No one narrated it other than Sufyān b. Ḥusayn, and the ḥuffāẓ disagreed with him from al-Zuhrī, among them Mālik, Ibn ‘Uyaynah, Yūnus, Ma‘mar, Ibn Jurayj, al-Zubaydī, ‘Uqayl, Layth b. Sa‘d, and others. All of them narrated it from al-Zuhrī and said: The dumb animal is junub, the well is junub, and the mine is junub, and they did not mention the foot, and that is the correct version."],[3401,"A thief who had stolen was brought to ‘Alī, and he cut off his hand. Then he was brought again having stolen, and he cut off his foot. Then he was brought a third time having stolen, and he ordered him to prison and said: Leave for him a foot to walk on and a hand to eat and clean himself with."],[3404,"Upon him ﷺ, similar to it."],[3405,"Abū Bakr al-Abharī narrated to us; Muḥammad b. Khurayim narrated to us; Hishām b. ‘Ammār narrated to us; Sa‘īd b. Yaḥyā narrated to us; Hishām b. ‘Urwah narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[3412,"In my book: Sa‘īd b. Ibrāhīm is unknown, and al-Miswar b. Ibrāhīm did not meet ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. ‘Awf. If its chain is sound, it is mursal."],[3415,"A man with a severed hand and foot stayed with Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, and he used to pray at night. He said: Abū Bakr said to him, “Your night is not the night of a thief. Who cut you?” He said, “Ya‘lā b. Umayyah, unjustly.” He said: Abū Bakr said to him, “I will write to him,” and he threatened him. While they were thus, they missed some jewelry belonging to Asmā’ bt. ‘Umays. He said: He began to say, “O Allah, expose to me its possessor.” He said: It was found with a goldsmith, and he was pressed until he was forced to point to the one with the severed limbs. Abū Bakr said, “By Allah, his deception of Allah is more severe to me than what he did. Cut off his foot.” ‘Umar said, “Rather, we cut off his hand, as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said.” He said, “Do it.”"],[3416,"Abu Bakr only cut off the leg of the one whose hand Ya'la b. Umayyah had cut off, and he had already had his hand cut off before that."],[3417,"There was a black man who used to come to Abu Bakr, and he would draw him near and teach him the Qur'an, until he sent out a tax collector—or he said an expedition—and the man said, 'Send me with him.' He said, 'Rather, stay with us.' But he refused, so he sent him with him and enjoined him to treat him well. Only a little while passed before he came back with his hand cut off. When Abu Bakr saw him, his eyes overflowed. He said, 'What happened to you?' He said, 'I did nothing more than that he entrusted me with something of his work, and I betrayed him in a single obligatory duty, so he cut off my hands.' Abu Bakr said, 'Do you find that the one who cut this off betrays more than twenty obligatory duties? By Allah, if you are truthful, I will surely exact retribution for you from him.' He said, 'Then he drew him near and did not change the position he had with him.' He said, 'The man would stand at night reciting, and when Abu Bakr heard his voice, he would say, \"By Allah, a man whose hand was cut off is this.\"' He said, 'Only a little while passed before the family of Abu Bakr missed jewelry and goods of theirs. Abu Bakr said, \"The neighborhood was raided tonight.\" The one-armed man stood up, faced the qiblah, and raised his healthy hand and the other that had been cut off, and said, \"O Allah, expose against me the one who stole from them,\" or something like this. Ma'mar sometimes said, \"O Allah, expose against me the one who stole from the people of this righteous household.\"' He said, 'Barely half the day had passed before they found the goods with him. Abu Bakr said to him, \"Woe to you! You have little knowledge of Allah.\" So he ordered that his leg be cut off.'"],[3418,"When Abu Bakr heard his voice at night, he would say, 'Your night is not the night of a thief.'"],[3419,"I bear witness that I saw 'Umar cut off the leg of a man after a hand and a leg; he stole a third time."],[3420,"He ﷺ cut off for the value of five dirhams."],[3421,"From 'Isa b. Abi 'Azzah likewise."],[3422,"The five are not cut off except for five."],[3423,"The five are not cut off except for five."],[3436,"He said: The price of the shield on that day was ten dirhams."],[3437,"The price of the shield on that day was ten dirhams."],[3441,"From Ayman, and Ayman has no companionship."],[3443,"The thief is not cut off for less than the price of a shield, and the price of a shield was ten dirhams."],[3445,"Muhammad b. Makhlad narrated to us, Muhammad b. Harun al-Harbi Abu Ja'far, who is Abu Nashit, narrated to us, Ahmad b. Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us with his chain something similar."],[3446,"The thief is not to have his hand cut off for less than ten dirhams."],[3447,"Upon him be peace, he cut off for five dirhams."],[3449,"He said: 'Ata' and Mujahid had related from his father."],[3464,"He said: Among the Children of Israel there was retaliation, but there was no blood money among them. So Allah, Exalted is He, said to this community: \"Retaliation is prescribed for you in the case of the murdered: the free for the free, the slave for the slave, and the female for the female. But if anyone is pardoned by his brother, then let there be a suitable follow-up\" (al-Baqarah 178). He said: Pardon is that he accepts blood money in the case of intentional killing. \"That is a concession and a mercy from your Lord\" (al-Baqarah 178): that they accept blood money in the case of intentional killing. \"Then let there be a suitable follow-up\" (al-Baqarah 178): the one follows the other with propriety, and the one pays with goodness."],[3466,"The hand is not cut off except for ten dirhams, and the dowry is not less than ten dirhams."],[3467,"Upon him be peace, he sent to a man who had married his father's wife that his neck be struck."],[3468,"The female apostate is granted a reprieve and is not killed."],[3469,"Regarding a woman who apostatizes, he said: She is to be given respite."],[3470,"He says: Al-Thawri used to criticize Abu Hanifah for a hadith that he narrated and no one other than Abu Hanifah narrated it from 'Asim from Abu Razin."],[3471,"From Ibn 'Abbas regarding a woman who apostatizes, he said: She is imprisoned and not killed."],[3472,"Women are not to be killed when they apostatize from Islam."],[3473,"Regarding a woman who apostatizes, he said: She is to be spared (i.e., not executed)."],[3474,"For the damiyah (a wound that bleeds but does not cut deep), one camel; for the badi'ah (a wound that cuts the flesh), two camels; for the mutalahimah (a wound that reaches the flesh), three camels; for the simhaq (a wound that reaches the periosteum), four; for the mudihah (a wound that exposes the bone), five; for the hashimah (a wound that fractures the bone), ten; for the munaqqilah (a wound that dislocates the bone), fifteen; and for the ma'mumah (a wound that reaches the brain membrane), one-third of the full blood money. And regarding a man who is beaten until he loses his mind, the full blood money is due; or beaten until he becomes unconscious and cannot understand, the full blood money is due; or until he is incapacitated and cannot understand, the full blood money is due. And for the eyelid, one-quarter of the blood money; and for the nipple of the breast, one-quarter of the blood money."],[3477,"A person was killed in Sana'a, and Umar executed seven men for him, saying: 'If the people of Sana'a had conspired against him, I would have executed them all for him.'"],[3478,"There was a man from the people of Sana'a who would outrun people every year. When he arrived, he found seven men drinking wine with his slave woman. They seized him and killed him, then threw him into a well. The one who came after him was asked about him and was told that he had gone on before him. He said: The men went to the privy, and he saw flies entering through the hole of a millstone and then coming out of it. He knew that there was flesh in it, so he lifted the millstone and sent for the man's concubine, and she told him about the group. Then Umar wrote to him: 'Strike all their necks and kill her with them, for if the people of Sana'a had shared in his blood, I would have killed them all.'"],[3482,"They brought a thief to al-Zubayr, and he interceded for him. They said: 'O Abu Abd Allah, do you intercede for a thief?' He said: 'Yes, it is fine as long as he has not been brought to the ruler. But if he is brought to the ruler, then may Allah not forgive him if he forgives him.'"],[3485,"A slave of Ibn Umar ran away and passed by the slaves of A'ishah. He stole from them a sack containing dates and rode a donkey belonging to them. He was brought to Ibn Umar, who sent him to Sa'id b. al-As, who was governor of Madinah. Sa'id said: 'We do not cut off the hand of a runaway slave.' A'ishah sent to him: 'My slaves are your slaves, and he was only hungry and rode the donkey to convey himself on it, so do not cut him.' But Ibn Umar cut off his hand."],[3490,"Umar b. al-Khattab used to flog for the hadd (prescribed punishment) in cases of indirect accusation (ta'rid)."],[3491,"Umar used to inflict the full hadd punishment for indirect accusation (ta'rid)."],[3492,"A man said to another man: 'O son of the woman with the fleshy vulva.' So the latter appealed to Uthman b. Affan against him. The man said: 'I only meant such-and-such by it.' Uthman b. Affan ordered him to be flogged with the hadd punishment."],[3493,"Two men exchanged insults. One of them said: 'My mother is not an adulteress, nor is my father an adulterer.' Umar consulted the people, and they said: 'He praised his father and mother.' But Umar said: 'They have praise other than this,' and he flogged him."],[3495,"He ﷺ wrote for him when he sent him to Yemen: For the nose, if it is completely cut off, the full blood money is due; for the eye, half the blood money; for the leg, half the blood money; for the ma'mumah (skull fracture reaching the brain), one-third of the blood money; for the munaqqilah (fracture that dislocates bone), fifteen camels; for the mudihah (wound exposing bone), five camels; and for every finger of those (i.e., hands and feet), ten camels."],[3496,"He ﷺ wrote for them a document: For the mudihah (wound exposing bone), five camels; for the ma'mumah (skull fracture reaching the brain), one-third of the blood money; for the munaqqilah (fracture that dislocates bone), fifteen; for the eye, fifty camels; for the nose, if it is completely cut off, the full blood money; for the tooth, five camels; for the leg, fifty; and for every finger of the fingers of the hands and feet, ten each."],[3497,"—ﷺ— ruled regarding head wounds: five, five camels; regarding teeth: five, five camels; and regarding fingers: ten, ten camels."],[3502,"—ﷺ— ruled regarding fingers: ten, ten."],[3506,"‘Ali used to cut off the foot and leave the heel so that one could lean upon it."],[3510,"From Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah al-Makhrami; and Sufyan mentioned at the end of it just as Ibrahim mentioned."],[3516,"For a paralyzed hand, one-third of the blood money; and for a protruding eye (that is) gouged out, one-third of the blood money."],[3528,"He said: ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi used to affirm the hadith of Isra’il from Abu Ishaq, and he would say, “The only hadith of Sufyan from Abu Ishaq that I missed, I missed because I relied on the hadith of Isra’il.”"],[3529,"Isra’il, from Abu Ishaq, is more beloved to me than Sufyan and Shu‘bah."],[3530,"He said: Isra’il would preserve the hadith of Abu Ishaq as one preserves Surah al-Hamd. Salih said: Isra’il is more precise in Abu Ishaq specifically."],[3537,"Ma‘qil b. Yasar married off a sister of his, then the man divorced her, and then he began to propose to her. He said, “I married my noble one to you, then you divorced her, and now you start proposing to her.” He refused to marry her to him, but the woman desired him, so Allah Almighty sent down this verse: “And when you divorce women and they have reached their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands.”"],[3538,"He said concerning the words of Allah Almighty, “Do not prevent them from marrying their husbands, when they have mutually agreed among themselves with what is right” (al-Baqarah 232). He said: Ma‘qil b. Yasar al-Muzani narrated to us that it was revealed concerning him. He said: I had married a sister of mine to a man, and he divorced her until her waiting period ended. Then he came to propose to her. I said to him, “I married her to you, gave you a bed and honored you, then you divorced her, and now you come proposing to her. No, by Allah, she will never return to you ever.” He said: The man was blameless, and the woman wanted to return to him. He said: Then Allah Almighty sent down these verses, and I said, “Now I will do it, O Messenger of Allah.” So he married her to him. Likewise it was narrated by ‘Abbad b. Rashid from al-Hasan, and Sa‘id from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Ma‘qil."],[3539,"I had a sister, and she was proposed to me, but I kept her away from men. Then a paternal cousin of mine came and proposed to her, so I married her to him. He lay with her as Allah Almighty willed, then he divorced her with a revocable divorce, then he left her until her waiting period ended. Then he proposed to her along with the other suitors. I said, “I kept her away from men and I married her to you, then you divorced her with a revocable divorce, then you left her until her waiting period ended. Now when she is proposed to me, you come proposing to her along with the suitors. I will never marry her to you.” So Allah Almighty sent down — or he said: it was sent down — “And when you divorce women and they have reached their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands” (al-Baqarah 232). So I atoned for my oath and married her to him. The meaning is close."],[3540,"I had a sister married to a man, and he divorced her, then he let her go until when her waiting period ended, then he came to propose to her. Ma‘qil was protective of that and said: He let her go while he was able to have her, and he came between him and her. So Allah Almighty sent down, “And when you divorce women and they have reached their term, do not prevent them” (al-Baqarah 232), the verse."],[3543,"The road gathered a group of riders, and a woman among them who had been previously married placed her affair in the hands of a man who was not her guardian, and he married her off. That reached Umar, so he flogged the one who married her and the one who gave her in marriage, and he rejected her marriage."],[3550,"Abu Wahb Yahya b. Musa b. Ishaq narrated to us in al-Ubulla: Jamil b. al-Hasan narrated to us: Muhammad b. Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us with his first chain of transmission something exactly like it."],[3551,"We used to say that the woman who gives herself in marriage is the fornicatress."],[3552,"He said: A woman may not give a woman in marriage, nor may a woman give herself in marriage. The fornicatress is the one who gives herself in marriage without her guardian's permission."],[3554,"A woman may not give a woman in marriage, nor may a woman give herself in marriage. Abu Hurayrah said: It used to be said that the fornicatress gives herself in marriage."],[3555,"A woman may not be married except with the permission of her guardian or a man of sound judgment among her family or the ruler."],[3557,"There is no marriage without the guardian's permission. Whoever marries or gives in marriage without the guardian's permission, his marriage is invalid."],[3572,"That a man gave his daughter in marriage."],[3577,"Muhammad b. Ismail al-Farisi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Juti narrated to us: my father narrated to us with his chain of transmission something like it."],[3578,"Upon him be peace, exactly the same."],[3581,"And from Zayd b. Habban, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[3585,"Ali ﷺ said: You consider what she has done. If she married a suitable match, we allow that for her; but if she married someone who is not a suitable match for her, we leave that matter to you."],[3595,"He said: The previously married woman."],[3603,"We used to marry a woman for a handful or two handfuls of flour."],[3615,"He said: Ali said: A dowry should not be less than ten dirhams."],[3616,"No dowry less than ten."],[3617,"He said: No dowry less than five dirhams."],[3618,"From Ali: No dowry less than ten dirhams, and so it became a hadith."],[3622,"Sufyan said: Dawud, this has always been disapproved of him. I said: Shu'bah narrated from him. He struck his forehead and said: Dawud, Dawud."],[3624,"I have married her to you for what you have with you of the Quran."],[3636,"Upon him be peace: Look at her, for there is something in the eyes of the women of the Ansar."],[3648,"Upon him be peace: the like of it exactly."],[3654,"Upon him be peace: He permitted the temporary marriage of women in the year of Awtas for three days, then he forbade it."],[3658,"That he separated between them, meaning a man who married while he was in ihram."],[3659,"I asked Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib about a muḥrim who marries. He said: They are to be separated."],[3665,"ﷺ married Maymūnah while he was not in iḥrām."],[3673,"ﷺ married Maymūnah while he was not in iḥrām. Thus he said. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān was alone in narrating it from his father, from Sallām Abū al-Mundhir, and it is gharīb from Maṭar. And Maṭar also has this statement from Rabīʿah, from Sulaymān b. Yasār, from Abū Rāfiʿ. Abū al-Aswad, the orphan of ʿUrwah, narrated it from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, similar to the narration of Maṭar from him."],[3675,"ﷺ married Maymūnah while they were both in iḥrām."],[3677,"They both said: Ayyūb narrated to us with his chain the like of it exactly."],[3682,"From ʿĀʾishah regarding the saying of Allah, exalted is He: “If you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls, then marry what is pleasing to you of women” (al-Nisāʾ 4:3), the verse. She said: It is the orphan girl who is with a man who is her guardian, and he marries her for her wealth, and treats her badly, and does not deal justly with her wealth. So let him marry what is pleasing to him of women, two, three, or four."],[3684,"Any woman whom a man deceives regarding that she has insanity, leprosy, or vitiligo, she is entitled to her dowry because of what he attained from her, and the man's ṣadāq is the responsibility of her guardian who deceived him."],[3685,"He said: ʿUmar ruled regarding the woman with vitiligo, leprosy, or insanity: when consummation has occurred, they are to be separated, and the ṣadāq is hers because of his intimacy with her, and it is for him against her guardian. He said: I said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes."],[3686,"Four conditions are not permissible in a sale or a marriage: the insane woman, the leprous woman, the woman with vitiligo, and the uncircumcised woman."],[3687,"Any man who marries a woman who is insane, or leprous, or has vitiligo, or has a horn (uterine protrusion), she is his wife; if he wishes, he may keep her, and if he wishes, he may divorce her."],[3688,"That ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ wrote to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb concerning a man with insanity about whom he feared for his wife. So ʿUmar wrote to him to give him a delay of one year; if he recovered, fine, otherwise he was to separate between him and his wife."],[3693,"Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about a man and a woman each of whom attained the other unlawfully, then they later decide to marry. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Its beginning was fornication and its end is marriage."],[3694,"Allah does not look at a man who looked at the private part of a woman and her daughter."],[3701,"Ghaylan b. Salamah became Muslim."],[3709,"Muhammad b. Makhlad narrated to us; Muhammad b. Abduk al-Qazzaz narrated to us; Musa b. Dawud narrated to us with his chain of transmission the like of it."],[3712,"Upon him and his family, and he gave him the choice, I would say: he keeps the first."],[3713,"He said: When he becomes Muslim and has two sisters as wives, he is given the choice of whichever of them he wishes. If he chooses one, her marriage is confirmed and the marriage of the other is annulled, whether he married them in one contract or in separate contracts."],[3719,"The Sunnah has established regarding the two who have sworn mutual cursing that they may never come together."],[3720,"The Sunnah has established that the two who have sworn mutual cursing may not come together."],[3722,"Ahmad b. Isa al-Hawwad narrated to us; Muhammad b. Sa'd al-Awfi narrated to us; al-Waqidi narrated to us with this chain of transmission something similar to it."],[3725,"Ali b. Abi Talib said to me: The one in whose hand is the knot of marriage. I said: The guardian of the woman? He said: No, rather it is the husband."],[3726,"Jubayr b. Mut'im married a woman from Banu Nasr and divorced her before consummating the marriage with her. He sent her the full dowry and said: I am more entitled to forgiveness than she is. Allah, Exalted is He, said: 'Unless they forgive or the one in whose hand is the knot of marriage forgives' [al-Baqarah 237]. And I am more entitled to forgiveness than she is."],[3727,"From Jubayr b. Mut'im something similar to this."],[3728,"Before consummating the marriage with her, he recited the verse: 'Unless they forgive or the one in whose hand is the knot of marriage forgives' [al-Baqarah 237]. He said: I am more entitled to forgiveness than she is. So he delivered the full dowry to her and gave it to her."],[3729,"The one who holds the marriage knot is the husband. Sufyan said: Ibn Shubrumah used to say: He is the husband."],[3731,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: 'unless they forgo [it]' (al-Baqarah 237), he said: meaning the woman forgoes or the one who holds the marriage knot, the guardian, forgoes."],[3732,"He is the husband."],[3733,"He is the husband."],[3734,"That his father married a woman, then divorced her before consummating the marriage. He sent the dower and said: I have more right to forgo."],[3735,"The one who holds the marriage knot is the husband."],[3736,"He is the husband; if he wishes, he completes the dower for her."],[3738,"That he was asked about a woman and her daughter from those whom one's right hand possesses: may one of them be taken in intercourse after the other? Umar said: I would not like to permit them both together, and he forbade him."],[3740,"May a man lie with a slave girl and her daughter when both are owned by him? He said: One verse forbade them and another verse permitted them, but I would not do it."],[3748,"And he said in his hadith: he may kiss and touch without intercourse."],[3751,"ﷺ freed Safiyyah, made her emancipation her dower, and married her."],[3752,"ﷺ freed Safiyyah, married her, and made her emancipation her dower."],[3769,"The husband of Barirah was a slave belonging to the family of Abu Ahmad."],[3770,"The husband of Barirah was a free man on the day she was manumitted."],[3773,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[3774,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[3775,"She said: And she was given the choice—meaning Barirah—and her husband was a slave."],[3778,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[3779,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[3780,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[3782,"The husband of Barirah was a slave."],[3783,"The husband of Barirah was a black slave belonging to Banu al-Mughirah on the day she was manumitted. By Allah, it is as if I can see him in the streets and districts of Madinah, his tears streaming down onto his beard as he followed her, seeking to please her so that she might choose him, but she did not."],[3785,"When she was given the choice, the husband of Barirah was a slave belonging to Banu al-Mughirah. It is as if I am looking at him in the streets of Madinah, following her and seeking to please her, while his tears were streaming down onto his beard, and she was saying: I have no need of you."],[3793,"He said concerning a man who is unable to provide maintenance for his wife: If he is unable, they are to be separated."],[3794,"Concerning a man who cannot find anything to spend on his wife, he said: They are to be separated."],[3795,"upon him ﷺ with the like of it."],[3796,"He said: It was said to Abdullah b. Abi Rawwad: Does a man marry his precious daughter to a man of religion even if he is not his equal in lineage? He said: Mis'ar narrated to me from Sa'd b. Ibrahim, from Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Talha, who said: Umar said: I shall indeed prevent the marriage of women of noble descent except to suitable matches."],[3800,"Compatibility is in lineage and religion."],[3801,"I said to Sufyan: Does a man marry his precious daughter to a man of religion even if the status is not the same? He said: Yes."],[3802,"I asked Waki' about compatibility, and he said: Al-Hasan b. Salih narrated to me from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Compatibility is in religion and status."],[3808,"I saw the sister of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf married to Bilal."],[3811,"He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the verse is shared. He said: Which verse? I said: \"And those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden\" (al-Talaq 65:4) - the divorced woman and the woman whose husband has died. He said: Yes."],[3817,"A man's nobility is his religion, his manliness is his character, and his origin is his intellect."],[3818,"Courage and cowardice are innate dispositions in men, as are generosity and noble lineage. A man's generosity is his religion, and his noble lineage is his character, even if he is Persian or Nabataean."],[3822,"The impotent man is granted a delay of one year."],[3823,"From Ma'mar, exactly the like of it."],[3824,"Regarding the one who is unable to have intercourse with his wife, he said: He is given a delay of one year."],[3825,"He is given a delay of one year. If he has intercourse with her, [fine]; otherwise, they are separated."],[3826,"He said: I went to al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah regarding the impotent man, and he said: He is given a delay of one year."],[3827,"The impotent man is given a delay of one year."],[3828,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah gave him a delay of one year from the day she brought the case against him."],[3829,"When the door is closed and the curtains are let down, the dower becomes due."],[3831,"Whoever closes a door and lets down a curtain, the dower becomes due."],[3833,"Something similar from Ibn 'Umar."],[3834,"When he closes a door and lets down a curtain, the dower becomes due to her, the waiting period is incumbent upon her, and she is entitled to inheritance."],[3836,"Al-Harith b. al-Hakam married a woman, closed the door upon her, then came out and divorced her, saying: \"I did not have intercourse with her.\" The woman said: \"He did have intercourse with me.\" They brought their dispute to Marwan, who summoned Zayd b. Thabit and said: \"What do you think? For al-Harith is believed, in our view.\" Zayd said: \"Would you have stoned her if she became pregnant?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Likewise, the woman is believed in a case like this.\""],[3837,"He used to see no harm, when he had finalized the divorce of his wife, in marrying a fifth, whether his wife was pregnant or not."],[3838,"From Bakr al-Muzani that they said: If he divorces his wife while she is pregnant, he may, if he wishes, marry her sister during her waiting period."],[3839,"He said: Hammad reported to us, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, something similar."],[3840,"They both used to say regarding a man who has four wives and divorces one of them irrevocably: he may marry whenever he wishes, and he does not need to wait for her waiting period to end."],[3841,"A slave may marry two women and may divorce twice. A slave woman's waiting period is two menstrual cycles; if she does not menstruate, then two months or a month and a half."],[3843,"When he buys a slave woman, then has intercourse with her, then finds a defect in her after having intercourse with her, he may take the value of the defect."],[3844,"He does not return her, but its value is deducted, and he returns to him the value of the defect."],[3846,"When he has intercourse with her, it becomes binding on him; and if he sees a defect before having intercourse with her, he may either keep her or return her if he wishes."],[3847,"Amr ibn al-As was asked about the waiting period of an umm walad, and he said: Do not confuse our religion for us. If she is a slave woman, her waiting period is the waiting period of a free woman."],[3848,"Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet for us: her waiting period is the waiting period of a woman whose husband has died, four months and ten days."],[3849,"He heard it from Amr, and the correct wording is: Do not confuse our religion for us, as a mawquf report."],[3850,"Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet for us: her waiting period is the waiting period of a woman whose husband has died, regarding the waiting period of an umm walad."],[3851,"From Amr ibn al-As something similar."],[3852,"The waiting period of an umm walad when her master dies is four months and ten days; and if she is freed, her waiting period is three menstrual cycles."],[3853,"He said: Indeed, we do not play with our religion. The free woman is a free woman, and the slave woman is a slave woman—meaning regarding the mother of the child, she must observe the waiting period of a free woman."],[3854,"The waiting period of the mother of the child is the waiting period of a free woman."],[3855,"The waiting period of the mother of the child is the waiting period of a free woman."],[3859,"A woman came to Umar b. al-Khattab and said that the jinn had made off with her husband. He ordered her to wait four years, then he ordered the guardian of the one whom the jinn had made off with to divorce her, then he ordered her to observe a waiting period of four months and ten days."],[3862,"Abu Talib al-Hafiz Ahmad b. Nasr narrated to us: Ubayd b. Muhammad b. Musa al-Sadafi narrated to us: Abd al-Malik b. Shuayb b. al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated to us: My father narrated to me from his father, from Sa'id b. Abi Hilal, from Zayd b. Aslam, regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"That is more likely that you may not be unjust\" (Qur'an 4:3). He said: That is more likely that you may not have many dependents."],[3867,"He ﷺ ordered him to go to the tribe of so-and-so, take from them a wasq of dates, and give it to sixty poor people."],[3868,"Regarding the one who has made zihar (likening his wife to his mother) and has intercourse before atoning: he owes two expiations."],[3869,"He owes two expiations."],[3871,"Regarding the one who has made zihar and has intercourse before atoning, he said: One expiation."],[3872,"Whoever wishes, I will invoke mutual cursing with him that there is no zihar from a slave woman."],[3873,"There is no zihar from a slave woman."],[3874,"He said: There is no zihar in a slave woman."],[3876,"If a man has four wives and does zihar from them, one expiation suffices him."],[3877,"If I marry Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr, he is to me like the back of my father. She asked about that, and she was commanded to free a slave and marry him."],[3878,"Abd Allah b. Jafar married the daughter of Ali and the wife of Ali, al-Nahshaliyya."],[3879,"A man from the people of Egypt who had companionship was called Jabala. He combined a man's wife and a daughter from another. Ayyub said: Al-Hasan disliked that."],[3880,"Khul' is a separation and not a divorce."],[3881,"He joined a man and his wife after two divorces and a khul'."],[3883,"She obtained khul' from her husband in the time of Uthman b. Affan. Uthman said: It is one divorce, unless they specify something, then it is according to what they specified."],[3884,"Umar said concerning the woman who obtains khul': she ransoms herself with less than her head braid."],[3886,"Pregnancy does not last more than two years, as much as the shadow of a spindle moves."],[3887,"I was away from my wife for two years, and I came and she was pregnant. Umar consulted the people about stoning her. Muadh b. Jabal said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you have a way against her, you have no way against what is in her belly. Leave her until she gives birth. So he left her, and she gave birth to a boy whose two front teeth had come out. The man recognized the resemblance in him and said: My son, by the Lord of the Kaaba. Umar said: Women are incapable of giving birth to one like Muadh. Were it not for Muadh, Umar would have perished."],[3888,"A woman does not increase in her pregnancy beyond two years, the measure of the shadow of a spindle. He said: Glory be to Allah, who says this? This is our neighbor, the wife of Muhammad b. Ajlan, a truthful woman, and her husband is a truthful man. She carried three pregnancies in twelve years, carrying each pregnancy four years."],[3889,"Well-known among us: the wife of Muhammad b. Ajlan used to carry and give birth in four years, and she was called the carrier of the elephant."],[3890,"While Malik b. Dinar was sitting one day, a man came to him and said, “O Abu Yahya, supplicate for a woman who has been pregnant for four years and has come to be in severe distress.” Malik became angry, closed the scriptures, and said, “Do the people think we are prophets?” Then he recited, then he supplicated, then he said, “O Allah, if there is wind in this woman’s belly, remove it from her this very hour; and if there is a girl in her belly, replace it for her with a boy, for You erase what You will and confirm, and with You is the Mother of the Book.” Then Malik raised his hand and the people raised their hands. The messenger went to the man and said, “Catch up with your wife.” The man went, and Malik had not lowered his hand before the man appeared at the door of the mosque carrying on his shoulders a boy with thick, curly hair, four years old, whose teeth had fully grown, whose umbilical cord had not been cut."],[3891,"He says: Here among us is a woman who menstruates in the morning and becomes pure in the evening."],[3892,"I encountered among us—meaning the Mahaliba—a woman who became a grandmother while she was eighteen years old. She gave birth at the age of nine to a daughter, and her daughter gave birth at the age of nine, so she became a grandmother while she was eighteen years old."],[3893,"I married myself to al-Qa‘qa‘ b. Shawr, and he spent one night with me. Then my father came from the Bedouins and appealed to ‘Ali, and his messengers came, so they took him to him. He said, “Did you consummate the marriage with her?” He said, “Yes.” So he permitted the marriage."],[3895,"If a woman’s guardian is obstructive, and she appoints a man who gives her in marriage, then his marriage is valid."],[3896,"There was among us a woman called Bahriyya. Her mother gave her in marriage while her father was absent. When her father arrived, he objected to that, so it was referred to ‘Ali b. Abi Talib, and he permitted the marriage."],[3897,"That ‘Ali ruled concerning her in that way."],[3899,"He said, “O Messenger of Allah, did not Allah, Exalted is He, say: ‘Divorce is twice’ (al-Baqarah 229)? So why has it become three?” He said, “Then either retain [her] with honorable treatment or release [her] with kindness (al-Baqarah 229).”"],[3901,"He says: Divorce is of four types: two types are lawful and two types are unlawful. As for the lawful, it is that he divorce her while she is pure without having had intercourse with her, and that he divorce her while she is clearly pregnant. As for the unlawful, it is that he divorce her while she is menstruating, or that he divorce her when he has had intercourse with her, not knowing whether the womb has conceived a child or not."],[3902,"The divorce according to the Sunnah is that he divorce her in every period of purity one divorce. Then the last of that is the waiting period that Allah commanded."],[3903,"Without intercourse, and he should call witnesses."],[3909,"That he divorce her while she is pure without intercourse, or with a pregnancy that has become evident."],[3912,"Da'laj narrated to us; al-Hasan b. Sufyan narrated to us; Habban narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us with this."],[3917,"He said: It was said to Ibn Umar, \"Did you count that divorce?\" He said, \"And why would I not count it, even if I was incapable and acted foolishly?\""],[3918,"I stayed for twenty years, then someone I do not suspect told me that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating with three divorces, and he was commanded to take her back. I said, \"I neither suspect them nor know the hadith,\" until I met Abu Allab Yunus b. Jubayr al-Bahili, who was reliable, and he told me that he asked Ibn Umar, and he told him that he divorced her once while she was menstruating and was commanded to take her back. He said: I said to him, \"Was it counted against him?\" He said, \"And what else? Even if he was incapable.\""],[3919,"He asked Ibn Umar, \"How many times did you divorce your wife?\" He said, \"Once.\""],[3922,"Abdullah divorced his wife that time only once."],[3928,"The Prophet ﷺ disapproved of that for him. And Abd al-Rahman b. Awf divorced his wife three times, and no one disapproved of that."],[3931,"She was married to a man from Banu Makhzum, and she informed me that he divorced her three times and went out on one of the campaigns."],[3932,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf divorced his wife Tumadir bt. al-Asbagh al-Kalbiyyah, the mother of Abu Salamah, with three pronouncements of divorce in one statement, and we have not heard that any of his companions disapproved of that."],[3934,"Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us; Muhammad b. Bishr b. Matar narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us; Muhammad b. Rashid narrated to us with his chain the like of it in both cases together."],[3935,"A man divorced his wife a thousand times, and he said, \"Three suffice you from that, and you may leave nine hundred and ninety-seven.\""],[3936,"I heard Mahan asking Sa'id b. Jubayr about a man who divorced his wife three times. Sa'id said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who divorced his wife a hundred times, and he said, \"Three make your wife forbidden to you, and the rest are a sin. You have taken the signs of Allah in mockery.\""],[3937,"He was asked about a man who divorced his wife a hundred times. He said, \"You disobeyed your Lord and parted from your wife. You did not fear Allah, so that He might make for you a way out.\""],[3938,"A man from Quraysh came to Ibn Abbas and said, \"O Ibn Abbas, I divorced my wife three times while I was angry.\" He said, \"Ibn Abbas cannot make lawful for you what has been made unlawful to you. You disobeyed your Lord, and your wife is forbidden to you. You did not fear Allah so that He would make a way out for you.\" Then he recited: \"When you divorce women, divorce them at their prescribed periods\" (Quran 65:1), \"while she is pure, without having had intercourse.\" Sayf said: \"The phrase 'while she is pure, without having had intercourse' is not in the recitation, but it is his explanation.\""],[3939,"A man came to Ibn Abbas and said, \"I divorced my wife a thousand times.\" He said, \"As for three, they make your wife unlawful to you, and the rest are a sin. You have taken the verses of Allah in mockery.\""],[3940,"Ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ya'qub b. Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us with his chain of narration, something similar to it."],[3957,"A man came to Ali b. Abi Talib and said, \"I divorced my wife a thousand times.\" Ali said, \"Three of them make her unlawful to you, and the rest of them distribute among your wives.\""],[3958,"He was asked about a man who divorced his wife with the number of stars. He said, \"He has gone against the Sunnah, and his wife is forbidden to him.\""],[3959,"A man divorced his wife with the number of stars. He said, \"He has gone against the Sunnah, and his wife is forbidden to him.\""],[3966,"Umar said, when the statement of Fatimah bt. Qays reached him, \"We do not accept the statement of a woman over the Muslims.\" Thus he would assign to the woman divorced three times the right to lodging and maintenance."],[3969,"Lodging and maintenance are only for the one whose husband has the right to return to her."],[3970,"When the statement of Fatimah bt. Qays reached him, he said, \"We do not abandon the Book of Allah for the statement of a woman; perhaps she forgot.\""],[3973,"From Abu Ishaq, similar to the statement of Yahya b. Adam, exactly alike."],[3975,"We do not abandon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of our Prophet for the statement of a woman. The woman divorced three times is entitled to lodging and maintenance."],[3976,"From Umar, and I have already written his wording before this."],[3986,"Whoever divorces his wife three times, his wife becomes irrevocably separated from him, and he has disobeyed his Lord, Exalted is He, and has contravened the Sunnah."],[3987,"The khaliyyah (divorce by saying \"you are free\"), the bariyyah (divorce by saying \"you are innocent\"), the battah (divorce by saying \"it is final\"), the ba'in (divorce by saying \"you are irrevocably separated\"), and the haram (divorce by saying \"you are forbidden\") are threefold; she is not lawful for them until she marries another husband."],[3991,"upon him and peace with this"],[3996,"Yazid b. Harun said to me: \"Which hadith! If only Humayd b. Malik al-Lakhmi were well-known.\" I said: \"He is my grandfather.\" Yazid said: \"You have delighted me, you have delighted me. Now it has become a hadith.\""],[4001,"Divorce is of four types: two types are lawful and two types are unlawful. As for the two that are lawful: that a man divorces his wife while she is pure without having had intercourse, or that he divorces her while she is pregnant with her pregnancy evident. As for the two that are unlawful: that he divorces her while she is menstruating, or that he divorces her at the time of intercourse, not knowing whether the womb has conceived a child or not."],[4006,"They both said: Umar b. Shabib narrated to us with his chain something similar. Umar b. Shabib was alone in narrating it as marfu', and he was weak. The authentic report from Ibn Umar is what Salim and Nafi' narrated from him as his own statement."],[4007,"Regarding a slave who has a free wife, or a free man who has a slave wife, he said: Whichever of them is enslaved, the divorce is reduced by his slavery, and the waiting period is according to the women."],[4008,"The divorce of a slave to a free woman is two pronouncements, and her waiting period is three menstrual cycles. The divorce of a free man to a slave woman is two pronouncements, and her waiting period is the waiting period of a slave woman: two menstrual cycles."],[4009,"When a free woman is under a slave, her divorce is two pronouncements and her waiting period is three menstrual cycles. When a slave woman is under a free man, her divorce is two pronouncements, and the waiting period is according to the women."],[4010,"If a slave divorces his wife twice, she becomes forbidden to him until she marries another husband, whether she is free or a slave. The waiting period of a free woman is three menstrual cycles, and the waiting period of a slave woman is two menstrual cycles."],[4016,"upon him and peace regarding this, he said: No."],[4020,"When a man declares his wife forbidden to himself, it is only an oath which he must expiate. Ibn Abbas said: \"Indeed you have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example.\""],[4021,"Regarding the prohibition (al-haram), there is an expiation for an oath. Then Ibn Abbas said: 'Indeed, you have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example.'"],[4023,"Regarding the prohibition (al-haram), it is an oath that requires expiation."],[4026,"Regarding a man who says to his wife: 'You are unlawful to me,' or 'You are divorced irrevocably (al-battah),' or 'You are divorced with the divorce of hardship (talaq haraj),' he said: 'As for his saying, \"You are unlawful to me,\" it is an oath that he expiates. As for his saying \"irrevocably\" and \"divorce of hardship,\" he is to be judged according to his intention (yadeenu fihi).'"],[4027,"He said: 'You have lied; she is not unlawful to you.' Then he recited: 'O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you?' (At-Tahrim 1). Upon you is the most severe of expiations: freeing a slave."],[4033,"He said: 'Whoever divorces his wife while she is menstruating with three divorces, she is irrevocably separated from him, he has disobeyed his Lord, and he has contradicted the Sunnah.'"],[4034,"From Ibn Umar with the same meaning."],[4035,"I asked Ja'far ibn Muhammad about a man who divorced his wife three times. He said: 'She is irrevocably separated from him and is not lawful to him until she marries another husband.' I said to him: 'Should I give this fatwa to the people?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[4036,"Upon him be peace, he made khul' a single irrevocable divorce."],[4038,"That the wife of Thabit, with the same meaning, without mentioning Ibn Abbas."],[4045,"I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Abbas one day when a man came to him and said: 'O Ibn Abbas, I have divorced my wife three times.' Ibn Abbas said: 'You have disobeyed your Lord, and your wife has become unlawful to you. You did not fear Allah so that He might make for you a way out. You divorce and then act foolishly, then you say: O Ibn Abbas, Allah the Exalted said: \"O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them at their waiting period\" (At-Talaq 1), that is, at the beginning of their waiting period.' He said: 'And Ismail ibn Umayyah informed us from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid that he was in the gathering with Ibn Abbas and heard from him what Mujahid narrated in this hadith.'"],[4046,"That a man asked Ibn Abbas, saying that he had divorced his wife three times."],[4047,"From Ibn Abbas with the same meaning."],[4048,"Regarding ila' he said: He is to be made to wait after the four months, then either he returns or he divorces."],[4049,"He is to be made to wait after the four months, then either he returns or he divorces."],[4052,"That Uthman used to make the one who had sworn ila' wait."],[4053,"That Uthman did not consider ila' to be of any consequence until the four months had elapsed, then he would make him wait."],[4054,"When four months have elapsed, it is one pronouncement of divorce."],[4055,"From Uthman and Zayd b. Thabit that they used to say: When four months have elapsed, it is an irrevocable pronouncement of divorce."],[4056,"From Uthman: He made the one who had sworn ila' wait."],[4057,"When four months have elapsed, it is one pronouncement of divorce, and he has the most right to take her back as long as she is in her waiting period."],[4058,"I said to Sa'id b. Jubayr: Did Ibn Abbas say that when four months have elapsed, it is one irrevocable pronouncement of divorce, and there is no waiting period upon her, and she may marry if she wishes? He said: Yes."],[4060,"I asked Abdullah b. al-Zubayr about a man who divorces his wife irrevocably and then dies while she is in her waiting period. Ibn al-Zubayr said: Abd al-Rahman b. Awf divorced his wife Tumadir bt. al-Asbagh al-Kalbiyya and then died while she was in her waiting period, and Uthman made her inherit."],[4061,"I met Ibn al-Zubayr while he was coming from Qu'ayqi'an on a horse, and I said: What do you think about a man who divorced his wife three times? He said: As for Uthman, he made her inherit."],[4062,"That Uthman b. Affan made Tumadir bt. al-Asbagh inherit from Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Abd al-Rahman had divorced her, and that was the last of his divorces to her, during his illness."],[4063,"Idha ma abatha tallaqa anhu waliyyuhu ya'ni al-majnun"],[4064,"Idha abatha al-majnun bi-impra'atihi tallaqa anhu waliyyuhu"],[4065,"Idha abatha al-ma'tuh bi-impra'atihi umira waliyyuhu an yutalliqa"],[4066,"Na Muhammad b. Makhlad na Sulayman b. Tawbah na Abu Hudhayfah"],[4067,"Abqat amatun li-ba'd al-Arab fa-waqa'at bi-Wadi al-Qura fa-intahat ila al-hayy al-ladhi abqat minhum fa-tazawwajaha rajulun min Bani Udhrah fa-natharat lahu dhata batniha thumma athara alayha sayyiduha ba'du fa-istaqaha wa-waladaha fa-qada Umar lil-Udhri bi-gharar waladihi al-ghurrah li-kull wasif wasif wa-li-kull wasifah wasifah wa-ja'ala thaman al-ghurrah idh lam yujad ala ahl al-qura sittin dinaran aw sab'a mi'at dirham wa-ala ahl al-badiyah sitt fara'id"],[4068,"Fi al-haram yaminun tukaffiru"],[4069,"Fi al-haram yaminun tukaffiru"],[4074,"Fi ibnatayni wa-abawayni wa-impra'atin qala sara thamanuha tis'an"],[4086,"Ana al-Hasan b. Salih bi-isnadihi mithlahu Muhammad b. Sa'id al-Ta'ifi thiqah"],[4087,"Annahu kana la yuwarrithu mayyitan min mayyit wa-yuwarrithu al-ahya'a min al-amwat"],[4088,"Qusimat mawarith ashab al-Harrah fa-waritha al-ahya'u min al-amwat wa-lam yarith al-amwat min al-amwat"],[4089,"Anna Umm Kulthum wa-ibnaha Zayd b. Umar b. al-Khattab halaka fi sa'ah wahidah lam yudra ayyuhuma halaka qablu fa-lam yatawaratha"],[4090,"A house fell on some people, and they inherited from one another."],[4091,"He was asked about a house that collapsed on people and they died. He said: 'They inherit from one another.'"],[4093,"Neither a Jew nor a Christian inherits from a Muslim, nor does a Muslim inherit from them, unless it be a man's slave or his female slave. This is what is preserved."],[4094,"We do not inherit from the People of the Book, nor do they inherit from us, unless a man inherits his slave or his female slave. Their women are lawful to us, but our women are not lawful to them."],[4099,"The killing of Ashyam was accidental."],[4103,"The blood money is divided according to the obligations of Allah, and every heir inherits from it."],[4105,"He ﷺ gave the wife one-eighth, the two daughters two-thirds, and what remained went to the full brother."],[4109,"From Abu Qays al-Awdi with his chain, similarly."],[4110,"It was read to Ibn Sa'id while I was listening: Ibn Zanjawayh narrated to you: Muhammad b. Yusuf narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Qays with his chain, the like of it."],[4113,"Umm Kulthum bt. Ali and her son Zayd fell on the same day, and the two cries met, and it was not known which of them died first. So she did not inherit from him, and he did not inherit from her. The people of Siffin did not inherit from one another, and the people of al-Harrah did not inherit from one another."],[4114,"About a newborn that is neither male nor female, having neither the share of a male nor the share of a female. It excretes from its navel like urine and feces. Amir was asked about its inheritance, and he said: 'Half the share of a male and half the share of a female.'"],[4117,"He said: I said to Sufyan al-Thawri: 'If you were appointed judge, whose shares of inheritance would you follow?' He said: 'The shares of inheritance of Zayd b. Thabit.'"],[4119,"Umar b. al-Khattab gave the daughter half and gave the sister what remained."],[4127,"Ibn Mani' narrated to us, Muhammad b. Sinan narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us as a mawquf report."],[4129,"From Miqdam b. Ma'di Karib."],[4130,"Ibn Jurayj narrated to us with his chain of transmission the like of it as a mawquf report."],[4131,"Allah and His Messenger, the like of it. Al-Naysaburi said: Rawh erred in it, and the correct version is Amr b. Muslim."],[4134,"From Abd al-Malik regarding a son's daughter and a sister's daughter: the property is between them, half and half. The correct version is from the statement of Alqamah."],[4140,"A woman secures three inheritances: her freed slave, her foundling, and her child by li'an."],[4141,"Upon him be peace, the like of it."],[4144,"Two grandmothers came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: the mother's mother and the father's mother. He gave the inheritance to the mother's mother, to the exclusion of the father's mother. Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl, a brother of Banu Harithah, said to him: 'O khalifah of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, you have given to the one who, if she had died, would not inherit from her.' So Abu Bakr divided it between them."],[4146,"Upon him be peace, he gave the grandmother one-sixth."],[4148,"He used to make three grandmothers inherit, if they were equal: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side."],[4149,"He used to make three grandmothers inherit: two from the mother's side and one from the father's side."],[4150,"I bear witness regarding Abu Bakr al-Siddiq that he treated the grandfather as a father."],[4152,"That Umar ruled that the grandfather shares with full brothers (through both father and mother) as long as"],[4153,"That Umar b. al-Khattab ruled that the grandfather shares with full brothers and paternal brothers as long as sharing is better for him than a third of the estate. If the brothers are numerous, he gives the grandfather a third, and the brothers get what remains, with the male receiving the share of two females. He also ruled that the children of the same father and mother are more entitled to that than the paternal brothers, their males, and that the paternal brothers share with the grandfather alongside the full brothers and refer back to them, and the paternal brothers get nothing with the full brothers unless the paternal brothers refer back to the daughters of the same father and mother. If anything remains after the fixed shares of the daughters of the same father and mother, it goes to the paternal brothers, with the male receiving the share of two females."],[4156,"And from Sufyan, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4167,"Upon him be peace, rode to Quba seeking guidance regarding the inheritance of the paternal aunt and maternal aunt, and Allah revealed that there is no inheritance for them."],[4172,"Ziyad b. Abi Sufyan said to a companion of his: Do you know how Umar ruled regarding the paternal aunt and maternal aunt? He said: No. He said: I know best of Allah's creation how Umar ruled concerning them. He made the maternal aunt take the status of the mother and the paternal aunt take the status of the father."],[4178,"My father narrated to me: Ibn Numayr narrated to us something similar."],[4184,"From al-Zuhri with this chain of narration, something similar."],[4186,"And for each horse, two shares."],[4194,"Abu Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ali al-Warraq narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from him."],[4195,"Upon him be peace, allotted two shares to the horseman and one share to the foot soldier. Thus he said, and al-Nadr b. Muhammad differed from him, from Hammad, and its mention has preceded."],[4201,"Upon him be peace, allotted al-Zubayr four shares: a share for his mother among the near kin, a share for himself, and two shares for his horse."],[4217,"And he placed idhkhir (a fragrant grass) over his feet, and he did not pray over any of the martyrs other than him, and he said, 'I am a witness over you today,' and he used to bury two or three in a single grave."],[4218,"That the martyrs of Uhud were not washed, and they were buried with their blood, and no funeral prayer was offered over them."],[4221,"He said: Every people inherit from one another, except those whose deaths are obscured, some before others, in a collapse, a fire, a battle, or other similar circumstances; for some of them do not inherit from others, but each person among them is inherited by the closest of the living people to him, as though there were no kinship between him and the one whose death was obscured along with him."],[4222,"There was an umm walad belonging to the brother of Shurayh b. al-Harith who bore him a girl, and she was married off and bore a boy. Then the umm walad died. He said: Shurayh b. al-Harith and the son of her daughter disputed over her inheritance before Shurayh. Shurayh b. al-Harith kept saying to Shurayh, 'He has no inheritance in the Book of Allah; he is only her daughter's son.' He said: So Shurayh ruled her inheritance to her daughter's son and said, 'And those of kinship are more entitled to one another in the Book of Allah' [al-Ahzab 6]. So Maysarah b. Yazid rode to Ibn al-Zubayr and informed him of what Shurayh had done. Ibn al-Zubayr wrote to Shurayh: 'Maysarah b. Yazid mentioned to me such-and-such, and that you said at that time, \"And those of kinship are more entitled to one another in the Book of Allah\" [al-Ahzab 6]. But that verse was about the matter of the agnatic relatives: a man would make a pact with another man and say, \"You inherit from me and I inherit from you.\" When it was revealed, that was abandoned.' Maysarah b. Yazid brought the letter to Shurayh, but when he read it, he refused to reverse his ruling and said, 'He only freed her as the recompense for her womb's offspring.'"],[4232,"Upon him be peace, similar to the statement of Shu'bah, but he did not mention al-Nadr b. Anas."],[4238,"A man called Salih came with his brother and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I want to free this brother of mine.' He said, 'Allah freed him when you took possession of him.'"],[4239,"When I buy a freed person, do not stipulate freedom for anyone regarding him, for that is a bond of slavery."],[4249,"Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Sa'dan narrated to us; Shu'ayb b. Ayyub narrated to us; Abu 'Asim al-Dahhak b. Makhlad narrated to us from Abu Bakr b. Abi Sabrah with its chain, something similar."],[4250,"Ibn Mubashshir narrated to us; Ahmad b. Sinan narrated to us; Shababah narrated to us; Abu Bakr b. Abi Sabrah narrated to us something similar."],[4253,"Muhammad b. Ahmad narrated to us; Sa'id b. Abi Maryam narrated to us; Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us with its chain, something similar."],[4254,"Upon him be peace, something similar; thus said Bukayr b. 'Abd Allah b. al-Ashajj."],[4257,"He ruled that an umm walad is not to be sold, nor given as a gift, nor inherited; her master may enjoy her as long as he lives, and when he dies, she is free."],[4258,"He ﷺ forbade selling umm walads (slave women who bore their master's child) and said: They are not to be sold, not to be given as gifts, and not to be inherited. Their master enjoys them as long as he lives, and when he dies, she is free."],[4259,"From 'Umar, something similar, but not raised to the Prophet."],[4260,"He forbade selling umm walads: they are not to be given as gifts, nor inherited. Their master enjoys them during his lifetime, and when he dies, she is free."],[4267,"I was with Zayd b. Thabit when a young man from the Ansar came to him and said: A cousin of mine, of whom I am the guardian, manumitted a slave-girl as a mudabbara (to be freed upon her death), and she has no property other than her. Zayd said: She may take from her own mercy (i.e., enjoy her services) as long as she lives. Abu Bakr said: This is a gharib (rare) hadith."],[4268,"The children of a mudabbara (slave-girl whose freedom is contingent on her owner's death) are freed when she is freed, and remain slaves while she remains a slave."],[4276,"He disliked the sale of a mudabbar (slave whose freedom is contingent on his owner's death)."],[4278,"'A'ishah fell ill, and some of her nephews mentioned her complaint to a man from the Zutt who practiced medicine. He said to them: You are describing a woman who has been bewitched; a slave-girl of hers bewitched her, and in the girl's lap now is a boy who has urinated in her lap. They mentioned that to 'A'ishah, and she said: Call such-and-such woman for me, one of her slave-girls. They said: In her lap now is a boy of theirs who has urinated in her lap. She said: Bring her to me. So she was brought. She said: Did you bewitch me? She replied: Yes. She asked: Why? She said: I wanted to be freed. 'A'ishah had made her a mudabbara. She said: I swear by Allah that you will never be freed. Find the worst Arab who owns slaves and sell her to them. Then she bought a slave-girl with her price and freed her."],[4279,"He saw no harm in a man setting up his wife's slave-girl for himself (i.e., arranging her as a surrogate or for sex)."],[4280,"He said: There is no harm; the pregnant and the nursing women may break the fast in Ramadan, day by day, and there is no makeup fasting required of them."],[4283,"Hudhayfah decided to fast after the sun had declined from its zenith, so he fasted."],[4291,"Beware of the people of opinion, for they are enemies of the Sunan. They were unable to memorize the hadiths, so they spoke by opinion and went astray and led others astray."],[4293,"He ﷺ said something similar to the hadith of al-Sahmi from Malik, and in it he said: I do not shake hands with women. My word to one woman is like my word to a hundred women."],[4304,"A man should write in his will: If the event of death occurs to me before I change this will of mine."],[4310,"Upon him ﷺ the like of it."],[4313,"He said: They used to write at the beginning of their wills: This is what so-and-so b. so-and-so has enjoined. He enjoins that he bears witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, and that the Hour is coming, no doubt about it, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves. And he enjoins those of his family whom he leaves behind to fear Allah with the fear due to Him and to set things right among themselves and to obey Allah and His messenger, if they are believers. And he enjoined them with what Ibrahim enjoined his sons and Ya'qub: O my sons, Allah has chosen the religion for you, so do not die except as Muslims. [al-Baqarah 132] 22. The Book of Agency."],[4316,"Abu Talha and Ubayy b. Ka'b and Suhayl b. Bayda' were with Abu Talha drinking from a drink of dates and unripe dates—or he said ripe dates—while I was serving them drink until it nearly took effect on them. A man from the Muslims passed by and said: Do you not know that wine has been forbidden? They said: O Anas, pour out what is in your vessel. They did not say: Wait until we ascertain. He said: So I overturned it."],[4318,"Ibn Mujahid narrated to us: al-Hasan b. Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us: Amir b. Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman b. Abd Allah b. Umar narrated to us: Hisham b. Urwa narrated this and its like."],[4325,"Abd Allah b. Muhammad narrated to us, dictating from his wording: Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: Hushaym narrated with his chain its like."],[4326,"Al-Husayn b. Ismail narrated to us: Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Hushaym narrated with his chain its like exactly."],[4327,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub b. Ibrahim, Ziyad b. Ayyub, and Muhammad b. Amr b. Sulayman narrated to us. And Ahmad b. Ali b. al-Ala' narrated to us: Ziyad b. Ayyub narrated to us. They said: Hushaym narrated to us: Abd Allah b. Abi Salih narrated with his chain its like exactly. 24. Vows."],[4328,"Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub b. Ibrahim, Ziyad b. Ayyub, and Muhammad b. Amr b. Sulayman narrated to us. And Ahmad b. Ali b. al-Ala' narrated to us: Ziyad b. Ayyub narrated to us. They said: Hushaym narrated to us: Abd Allah b. Abi Salih narrated with his chain its like exactly. 24. Vows."],[4334,"A man asked Sa'id b. al-Musayyib: I said, I must walk to the Kaaba. Sa'id said: Did you say, I have a vow upon me? The man said: No. He said: Nothing is upon you."],[4337,"And from al-Hasan b. Umara, from Amr b. Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it."],[4340,"He said: Oaths are four: two oaths that are expiated and two oaths that are not expiated. A man swears: By Allah, I will not do such and such, then he does it; and a man says: By Allah, I will certainly do it, then he does not do it. As for the two oaths that are not expiated: a man swears: I did not do such and such, when he had done it; and a man swears: I certainly did such and such, when he had not done it."],[4341,"Every exception that is not connected, its utterer is perjured."],[4343,"That his mistress wanted to separate him from his wife. She said: “One day she is a Jewess, one day a Christian, and every slave she owns is free, and all her wealth is for the sake of Allah, and upon her is the walking to the House of Allah, if she does not separate them.” So she asked ʿĀʾishah, Ibn ʿUmar, Ibn ʿAbbās, Ḥafṣah, and Umm Salamah, and all of them said to her: “Do you want to be like Hārūt and Mārūt?” And they ordered her to expiate her oath and leave them be."],[4344,"My mistress said: “I will surely separate you from your wife, and all her wealth is for the covering of the Kaʿbah, and she is one day a Jewess, one day a Christian, and one day a Magian, if I do not separate you from your wife.” He said: So I went to the Mother of the Believers, Umm Salamah, and said: “My mistress wants to separate me from my wife.” She said: “Go to your mistress and tell her that this is not lawful for you.” He said: So I returned to her. He said: Then I came to Ibn ʿUmar and informed him. He came until he reached the door and said: “Here is Hārūt and Mārūt.” She said: “I have made all my wealth for the covering of the Kaʿbah.” He said: “Then what will you eat?” She said: “And I said: I am one day a Jewess, one day a Christian, and one day a Magian.” He said: “If you become a Jewess, you will be killed; if you become a Christian, you will be killed; if you become a Magian, you will be killed.” She said: “What do you command me?” He said: “Expiate your oath and reunite your young man and your young woman.”"],[4345,"A man from the people said: “Glory be to Allah! An expiation for disobedience to Allah, the Exalted?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Yes. Allah mentioned ẓihār and commanded expiation.”"],[4346,"He said: “The expiation of an oath is a mudd of wheat for each poor person.”"],[4347,"For each poor person is a mudd of wheat, with its seasoning as its condiment."],[4348,"Regarding the expiation of an oath, he said: “A mudd of wheat for each poor person.”"],[4349,"He said: I heard Abū Hurayrah in this mosque say: “Three things in which there is a mudd: a mudd in the expiation of an oath, in the expiation of ẓihār, and the ransom of feeding a poor person.”"],[4350,"For each poor person is a mudd of wheat, with its condiment."],[4351,"When the elderly man is unable to fast, he feeds one mudd for each day."],[4355,"Abū al-Zubayr informed me that ʿAdī ibn ʿAdī informed him from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4358,"Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us with this chain of transmission, something similar."],[4366,"He said: “Yes.”"],[4367,"They both said: breastfeeding makes forbidden what is forbidden by lineage, whether small or large."],[4374,"He said: 'My wife's breast swelled and I sucked it, and something entered my throat before I could stop it.' Abu Musa was stern with him, so he went to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and said: 'Did you ask anyone other than me?' He replied: 'Yes, Abu Musa, and he was stern with me.' So he went to Abu Musa and said: 'Is this a suckling?' Abu Musa replied: 'Do not ask me as long as this scholar is among you.'"],[4375,"There is no breastfeeding after two full years."],[4377,"There is no breastfeeding except within the two years, in infancy."],[4383,"He said: 'The daughter of Abu Ihab got married,' and he narrated the hadith."],[4389,"Ibn Umar was asked about something concerning breastfeeding, and he said: 'I do not know except that Allah, exalted is He, has forbidden the sister through breastfeeding.' It was said to him: 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr says that one or two sucklings do not make it forbidden.' Ibn Umar replied: 'The decree of Allah, exalted is He, is better than your decree and the decree of Ibn al-Zubayr.'"],[4390,"Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who has a wife and a concubine; one of them gave birth to a boy and the other breastfed a girl. Is it valid for the boy to marry the girl? He replied: 'No, the milk is one.'"],[4396,"In the Quran, ten known sucklings were revealed, and she intended what makes breastfeeding forbidden. Then afterwards, or five known sucklings, were revealed."],[4402,"He said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: 'Four things have been decreed: creation, character, provision, and lifespan. No one earns from another, and charity is valid whether it is taken or not.'"],[4405,"Less than five known sucklings do not make it forbidden."],[4406,"Ibn Umar said: 'The decree of Allah is better than your decree and the decree of the Commander of the Faithful.'"],[4407,"From Ibn Umar and Ibn al-Zubayr, something similar."],[4427,"Its principal is not to be sold, nor given as a gift, nor inherited."],[4428,"So he kept its principal: it is not sold, nor given as a gift, nor inherited. He gave it as charity to the poor, the near relatives, the slaves, the needy, the wayfarer, and the guest."],[4430,"I acquired a piece of land from the land of Khaybar. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I acquired a piece of land and I have never acquired wealth dearer to me than it, nor more precious in my estimation. He said: If you wish, you may give it as charity and keep its principal. He said: So Umar gave it as charity on condition that it is not sold, nor given as a gift, for the poor, the near relatives, the guest, the slaves, and the wayfarer. There is no blame on the one who administers it to eat from it in a reasonable manner, without accumulating wealth."],[4433,"He said: When it was revealed, \"You will never attain righteousness until you spend from what you love\" (Aal Imran 92) and \"Who is it that would lend Allah a goodly loan\" (al-Baqarah 245), Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, my garden in such-and-such a place is a charity for Allah Almighty, and if I could keep it secret I would not make it public. He said: Make it for the poor of your household and your relatives."],[4434,"He said: So he assigned it to Ubayy b. Kab and Hassan b. Thabit, and they were closer to him than I."],[4435,"From Anas."],[4445,"Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I have property at Thamgh which I dislike being sold after me. He said: So retain it and give its fruit in charity."],[4457,"When Uthman was besieged in his house, the people gathered around his house, and he looked out at them."],[4460,"Four things have been settled: creation, character, provision, and term. So no one acquires anything from anyone; and charity is valid whether it is taken possession of or not."],[4470,"upon him and peace, similarly, except that he made in place of wages, good deeds."],[4483,"He said: Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ashari: Now then, verily judging is a definitive obligation and a followed sunnah. So understand when a proof is presented to you, and enforce the truth when it becomes clear, for speaking truth with no enforcement is of no benefit. Treat people equally in your countenance, your gathering, and your justice, so that the weak does not despair of your justice and the noble does not aspire to your injustice. The proof is upon the claimant, and the oath is upon the one who denies. Settlement is permissible between Muslims, except a settlement that makes lawful what is unlawful or makes unlawful what is lawful. Let not a judgment you made yesterday, in which you reconsidered and were guided to your right course, prevent you from returning to the truth, for the truth is ancient, and returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood. Understand, understand what stirs in your heart of matters that have not reached you in the Book or the Sunnah. Recognize the precedents and the similarities, then analogize matters accordingly. Then aim for the most beloved to Allah and the most similar to the truth in your view. Set for the claimant a time limit to which he should adhere; if he presents evidence, he obtains his right, otherwise you direct judgment against him, for that is clearer for removing blindness and more effective in the excuse. Muslims are just witnesses against one another, except one who has been flogged for a prescribed punishment, or is known for false testimony, or is suspect in loyalty or kinship. Indeed Allah has taken charge of your secrets and warded off from you by evidence. Beware of agitation, vexation, annoyance with people, and harshness toward litigants in stations of truth which Allah makes a means of reward and a goodly store, for whoever sets his intention right between himself and Allah, even against himself, Allah will suffice him in what is between him and the people. And whoever adorns himself for people with what Allah knows is otherwise, Allah will disgrace him. What is your expectation of the reward of other than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in His immediate provision and treasuries of mercy? And peace be upon you."],[4484,"This is the letter of Umar. Then it was read to Sufyan from here: to Abu Musa al-Ashari. Now then, verily judging is a definitive obligation and a followed sunnah. So understand when a proof is presented to you, for speaking truth with no enforcement is of no benefit. Treat people equally in your gathering, your countenance, and your justice, so that the noble does not aspire to your injustice and the weak does not fear your oppression. The proof is upon the claimant, and the oath is upon the one who denies. Settlement is permissible between Muslims, except a settlement that makes lawful what is unlawful or makes unlawful what is lawful. Let not a judgment you made yesterday, in which you reconsidered and were guided to your right course, prevent you from returning to the truth, for the truth is ancient, and nothing invalidates the truth, and returning to the truth is better than persisting in falsehood. Understand, understand what stirs in your heart; then aim for the most beloved to Allah and the most similar to the truth in your view. Set for the claimant a time limit to which he should adhere; if he presents evidence, then otherwise you direct judgment against him, for that is clearer for removing blindness and more effective in the excuse. Muslims are just among themselves, some against others, except one who has been flogged for a prescribed punishment, or is known for false testimony, or is suspect in loyalty or kinship. Indeed Allah has taken charge of your secrets and warded off from you by evidence. Then beware of vexation, agitation, annoyance with people, and harshness toward litigants in stations of truth in which reward is made obligatory and remembrance is made good, for whoever makes his intention sincere between himself and Allah, Allah will suffice him in what is between him and the people. And whoever adorns himself for people with what Allah knows is otherwise, Allah will disgrace him."],[4487,"For I say what is recognized and not rejected, and I do not say what is rejected and not recognized."],[4491,"Upon him be peace, the like of it."],[4493,"Yazid b. al-Had narrated to me with both chains together, the like of al-Qawariri's statement."],[4496,"Whether they like it or dislike it."],[4498,"Upon him be peace, he made the claimant of the right swear with the single witness."],[4501,"Upon him be peace, he judged by the oath with the witness."],[4502,"Upon him be peace, he returned the oath to the claimant of the right."],[4514,"From al-Husayn, meaning the teacher, with his chain, the like of it regarding the woman who is killed if she apostatizes."],[4516,"Umar b. Ahmad al-Darbi narrated to us, Ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah b. Musa narrated to us with his chain, the like of it."],[4547,"Whoever does in his wealth something not in the Book of Allah, it is rejected."],[4555,"When the wicked man claims against the righteous man something that people regard as false and that there was no transaction between them, he is not made to swear for him."],[4562,"And any person who perishes while having another person's property in his possession, whether he collected something from it or not, he is on equal footing with the creditors."],[4564,"Abd Allah b. Ja'far came to al-Zubayr and said, \"I bought such-and-such a sale, and 'Ali wants to go to the Commander of the Faithful to ask him to place me under interdiction concerning it.\" Al-Zubayr said, \"Then I am your partner in the sale.\" 'Ali then came to 'Uthman and said, \"Ibn Ja'far bought such-and-such a sale, so place him under interdiction.\" Al-Zubayr said, \"I am his partner in the sale.\" 'Uthman said, \"How can I place a man under interdiction in a sale in which al-Zubayr is his partner?\" Ya'qub said: I adhere to interdiction and consider it valid; I place under interdiction and invalidate the sale and purchase of the one interdicted. If he buys or sells before interdiction, then if it is sound I allow it, and if there is a reason that warrants interdiction I place him under interdiction and reject his sale. If he is not someone who warrants interdiction, I allow his sale. Ya'qub b. Ibrahim said: Abu Hanifa would not place under interdiction and did not adhere to interdiction."],[4568,"The Prophet ﷺ allowed the testimony of the midwife. Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Malik did not hear it from al-A'mash; between them is an unknown man."],[4570,"The testimony of the midwife is admissible concerning the cry of the newborn."],[4587,"And from Sufyan, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[4588,"He appointed a freed slave of his called Hani' over the protected pasture. He said to him, \"O Hani', fold your wing away from the Muslims, and beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it is answered. Allow in the owner of the small herd and the small flock. But keep away from me the camels of Ibn 'Affan and Ibn 'Awf, for if their livestock perish, they will return to farming and palm trees, whereas the owner of the small herd and the small flock, if his livestock perishes, will come to me with his children and say, 'O Commander of the Faithful, shall I leave them? No, by your father.' Water and pasture are easier for me than dinars and dirhams. By Allah, they think that we have wronged them. It is their land for which they fought in the pre-Islamic era and upon which they embraced Islam. By the One in whose hand is my soul, were it not for the wealth that I carry in the cause of Allah, I would not have protected a single span of their land from the people.\""],[4593,"Whoever I judge in favor of by an argument that I deem valid, and he cuts with it a piece wrongfully..."],[4604,"Ibn Shihab informed me with this chain of transmission."],[4607,"He said: There was a dispute between 'Umar b. al-Khattab and Mu'adh b. 'Afra' over something, so they made Ubayy b. Ka'b an arbitrator. 'Umar told him his story, and Ubayy said, \"Pardon, O Commander of the Faithful.\" He said, \"No, do not excuse me from it if it is against me.\" He said: Ubayy said, \"Then it is against you, O Commander of the Faithful.\" He said: Then 'Umar swore an oath, then said, \"Do you think I deserve it by my oath? Go now, for it is yours.\""],[4608,"They claimed that Hudhayfa recognized a camel of his that had been stolen, so he brought a dispute concerning it to the judge of the Muslims. An oath was required of Hudhayfa in the judgment, and he wanted to buy his oath. He said, \"You shall have ten dirhams,\" but he refused. He said, \"You shall have twenty,\" but he refused. He said, \"You shall have thirty,\" but he refused. He said, \"You shall have forty,\" but he refused. Hudhayfa said, \"Leave my camel,\" and he swore that it was his camel, that he did not sell it or give it as a gift."],[4609,"He ransomed his oath for ten thousand dirhams, then said, \"By the Lord of this mosque and the Lord of this grave, if I had sworn, I would have sworn truthfully. This is something with which I ransomed my oath.\""],[4610,"He ruled concerning a hunting dog: forty dirhams; concerning a sheepdog: a sheep; concerning a crop dog: a measure of food; and concerning a house dog: a measure of dust. It is incumbent upon the one who killed it to give, and incumbent upon the owner of the dog to take, along with whatever is deducted from the reward."],[4612,"The Prophet ﷺ rejected the testimony of the treacherous man and the treacherous woman, and of one bearing malice against his brother, and he rejected the testimony of one dependent on a household, while allowing it against others."],[4617,"Shurayh used to accept the testimony of every religious community against its own community, but he would not accept the testimony of a Jew against a Christian or a Christian against a Jew—except for Muslims, for he used to accept their testimony against all communities."],[4620,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is protected of the arak trees? He said: That which the camels' hooves cannot reach."],[4627,"He informed him that Umar came out to them and said: I found the smell of drink on so-and-so, so I asked him what he had drunk, and he claimed that he had drunk tila. I am going to ask about that drink; if it intoxicates, I will flog him. Then Umar flogged him with the full prescribed punishment."],[4629,"Upon him ﷺ, similar to it, and he did not doubt."],[4630,"Upon him ﷺ, without any doubt, and Luwayn said from Hammad that he traced it back and did not doubt."],[4631,"Upon him ﷺ, without any doubt. And Dhalaj b. Ahmad narrated to us; Musa b. Harun narrated to us; Muhammad b. Malik al-Basri, the neighbor of Ibn Hasanat, narrated to us from him."],[4645,"From Ibrahim, his statement: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and it is the drink that intoxicates you. This is more correct than the one before it; no one traced it back except al-Hajjaj, and there are discrepancies reported from him. Ammar b. Matar is weak and Hajjaj is weak; it is only from the statement of al-Nakha'i."],[4646,"Every intoxicant is forbidden—it is the drink that intoxicates you."],[4647,"Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak said: This is a false hadith."],[4648,"He said concerning this hadith that came: Every intoxicant is forbidden—it is the cup from which one becomes intoxicated."],[4661,"Uthman b. Ahmad narrated to us; Hanbal b. Ishaq narrated to us; Abu Ghassan narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us from Ibrahim b. al-Muhajir with this. And Qasim al-Ju'i narrated it from al-Firyabi from Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Sha'bi from al-Nu'man b. Bashir, and he erred in it."],[4669,"A gulp of it is forbidden."],[4674,"She said: Whatever intoxicates in a large amount, a single sip of it is forbidden. [This is] mawquf."],[4678,"Upon him be peace: Every intoxicant is forbidden. And Tawus, Ata', and Mujahid narrated from him: Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is forbidden. And Qays b. Habtar narrated it from him, and likewise was the fatwa of Ibn Abbas concerning the intoxicant."],[4679,"A small amount of that which intoxicates in large amount is forbidden."],[4680,"A small amount of that which intoxicates in large amount is forbidden."],[4681,"That he asked A'ishah about nabidh, and she said: O my son, Allah did not forbid khamr because of its name; He forbade it because of its outcome. Every drink whose outcome is like the outcome of khamr is forbidden like the prohibition of khamr."],[4692,"I used to prepare nabidh for Umar in the morning and he would drink it in the evening, and I would prepare it for him in the evening and he would drink it in the morning, and he would not put any dregs in it."],[4694,"Nabidh was prepared for Umar upon his arrival, and it was delayed a day, so a nabidh that had become strong was brought. He said: He called for large bowls and poured it out, then poured water over it."],[4696,"I performed Hajj with Umar twice, and I heard him say: We drink nabidh to cut what is in our bellies from camel meat, lest it harm us."],[4697,"A bedouin drank nabidh from Umar's water skin and became intoxicated, so Umar applied the legal punishment to him."],[4698,"Umar passed by a water skin belonging to a man from Thaqif and said: Bring me this nabidh. It was brought to him, and he took it and found it strong. He said: Whoever is troubled by anything from this nabidh, let him break its intensity with water."],[4699,"I carried baskets of khabis to Umar b. al-Khattab. When I placed them before him, he opened some of them and said: O Utbah, do all the Muslims find the like of this? I said: O Commander of the Faithful, this is something reserved for the commanders. He said: Take it away; I have no need of it. He said: While I was with him, he called for his food, and thick meat and coarse bread were brought. I reached for a piece, thinking it was a camel hump, but it was the ligament of the neck. I chewed it, and when he was distracted from me, I placed it between me and the table. Then he called for his nabidh, which had almost turned into vinegar, and mixed it until it was drinkable, then he drank and gave me to drink. Then he said: O Utbah, we slaughter a camel every day. Its haunches and choice parts are for those of the people of the regions and the Muslims who are present with us. As for its neck, it is for us: we eat this thick meat that you saw and drink with it this nabidh to cut it in our bellies."],[4700,"Abu Saeed Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Ibrahim b. Mishkan al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yahya al-Sarakhsi the judge narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ali narrated to us: Abdan narrated to us, from Sufyan b. Abd al-Malik, from Abdullah b. al-Mubarak, who said: Abdullah b. Umar al-Umari asked Abu Hanifah about the drink. He said: They narrated to us from your father, may Allah have mercy on him: If it troubles you, break it with water. Abdullah said to him: What if you are certain and not in doubt?"],[4702,"A man drank nabidh from Ali's water skin at Siffin and became intoxicated, so Ali ﷺ applied the legal punishment to him."],[4703,"A Bedouin drank nabidh from Umar's water skin and became intoxicated, so Umar applied the legal punishment to him."],[4708,"He ﷺ became thirsty while circumambulating the House, and he was brought nabidh from the water station. He frowned, so a man said to him, \"Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No. Bring me a bucket of Zamzam water.\" He poured it over it and then drank while circumambulating the House."],[4711,"He ﷺ was brought a man who had become intoxicated from date nabidh, and he flogged him."],[4713,"There is nothing in a drink of nabidh that makes it appropriate for a believer to risk his religion with it."],[4716,"He ﷺ was asked about wine: can it be made into vinegar? He said, \"No.\""],[4725,"It has reached me that Allah slaughtered what is in the sea for the children of Adam."],[4729,"Whatever the sea casts out or recedes from of fish, eat it; and whatever you find floating, do not eat it."],[4730,"Whatever the sea throws out, or ebbs away from, or is caught in it, eat; and whatever dies in it and then floats, do not eat."],[4731,"From Jabir, similar to it, in mawquf form."],[4732,"There is nothing in the sea except that Allah, Exalted is He, has slaughtered it for you."],[4734,"The floating fish is lawful for whoever wishes to eat it."],[4735,"A fish floating on the water is lawful."],[4736,"Indeed Allah, the Exalted, has slaughtered for you what is in the sea, so eat all of it, for it has been properly slaughtered."],[4737,"I bear witness regarding Abu Bakr al-Siddiq that he ate a fish floating on the water."],[4738,"All fish are properly slaughtered."],[4739,"All fish are properly slaughtered, and all locusts are properly slaughtered."],[4740,"He said: Allah, the Exalted, said: 'Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food, as provision for you and for the travelers' [al-Ma'idah 96], and its food is what it casts up."],[4741,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'Lawful to you is the game of the sea and its food' [al-Ma'idah 96]: Indeed, its game is what is caught, and its food is what the sea casts up."],[4742,"That he rode in the sea with a group of his companions, and they found a fish floating on the water. They asked him about it, and he said: 'Is it good, has it not changed?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then eat it, and set aside my share of it.' And he was fasting."],[4743,"That the companions of Abu Talha obtained a floating fish, and they asked Abu Talha about it, and he said: 'Give it to me as a gift.'"],[4746,"Upon him be peace, he was asked about a fetus that comes out dead. He said: 'If you wish, eat it.'"],[4751,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[4756,"That he said: 'Whoever finds ample means and does not offer a sacrifice, let him not come near our mosques.'"],[4768,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, should I take a loan and offer a sacrifice?' He said, 'Yes, for it is a debt that will be repaid.'"],[4770,"Ja'far b. Nusayr narrated to us, Ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Zuhayr b. 'Abbad narrated to us, Suwayd b. 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us something similar."],[4779,"I said to Abu Hanifah, 'From where did you take this—that a man who works with another man's wealth without his permission should give the profit in charity?' He said, 'I took it from the hadith of 'Asim b. Kulayb.'"],[4784,"Khalid b. al-Walid embraced Islam after the conquest of Khaybar."],[4788,"We used to eat the meat of horses. I said, 'What about mules?' He said, 'No.'"],[4804,"He said about a mouse falling into ghee or oil: 'Make use of it, but do not eat it.'"],[4813,"It was forbidden to eat the animal slaughtered by a Magian, or the game caught by his dog or his bird."],[4814,"He said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we mix with the polytheists, and we have no pots or vessels other than theirs.' He said: 'Avoid them as much as you can. If you cannot find any, then wash them with water, for water is their purification, then cook in them.'"],[4817,"About a Muslim who slaughters and forgets to say the name of Allah, he said: 'There is no harm in it.'"],[4818,"He did not see any harm in it."],[4819,"If a Muslim slaughters and does not mention the name of Allah, then let him eat, for the Muslim has within him a name from the names of Allah."],[4825,"From 'Amir, something similar to that."],[4838,"ﷺ , similar to the hadith of Yazid."]]);
